{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded","id":1210732,"title":"A Closer Look: Solars vs Dragonblooded","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-23T18:36:22-07:00","id":1210732,"title":"A Closer Look: Solars vs Dragonblooded","content":"So I've seen this kind of thing crop up in a few threads, there's even another thread about it but that's kind of drifted. I've got a lot to say anyway. Plus it's exam time and all my exams are over, so time to turn that hard analysis to Exalted! That means it's time for a closer look.<br /> <br /> I'd like to point out here that I love the DB charmset as previewed and I have very very few criticisms of it. I'm head over heels for most of it and this is not meant to bring it down.<br /> <br /> Most of what I've seen has concerned the idea of Dragonblooded being able to fight Solars, let's take a look at that shall we?<br /> <br /> Here in the spoiler is a close mechanical look at what lead me to my conclusion below<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <b>Attack/defense</b><br /> <br /> Okay so the first thing that we might want to know is, how easily can a Solar hit a DB? The dice caps favour the Solar, 10 to 6, the good news is that the DB one is slightly easier to hit because attributes tend to be more valuable than specialties. The bad news is that's the only good news. Apart from their excellency DBs don't actually have many charms that make them harder to hit. Even then the few charms they get are often along the lines of &quot;(Essence) 1s on the attack roll can reroll successes starting with 7s.&quot; which seems okay until you realize that the first melee charm for Solars rerolls 1s. The Solar also has a bunch of options like free full excellencies, big flurry attack charms and Rising Sun Slash to add bonus non-charm dice.<br /> <br /> Alright so let's check the other way around! Not so good here either, Same dice cap scenario, and DBs barely have any way to boost accuracy, often as little as rerolling (essense) non-1 failures. Whereas the Solar has cheap and easy penalty negators.<br /> <br /> <b>Damage/Mitigation</b><br /> <br /> Damage? Well here the disparity is much larger. Solars have a plethora of ways to boost damage into the sky with things like Thunderbolt Attack Prana and Hungry Tiger Technique. What kinds of resistance charms might DBs have to counter this? Not much, they've got a 4 mote charm to add (Stamina) soak to a single attack, and a couple of other things further down the tree which aren't that impressive. Most of them are instant and/or very costly.<br /> <br /> Flip side for the DBs? Not good, the Solars have big scenelong charms that add a lot of soak, and other charms to do things like half withering damage. So they're going to struggle to get any initiative away from a really combat focused Solar, and even when they get it the damage they deal with decisives can be mitigated. On top of all that DBs have really few ways to actually boost their damage, almost none at all for withering OR decisive. They don't have a lot of multi-attack charms either that could help with this, and the ones they do have make 2-3 attacks tops.<br /> <br /> <b>Higher Essence</b><br /> <br /> Things at least improve for the DBs with essence though, right? I'm afraid not. They do a little bit, but mostly the higher essence DB effects make things happen which are bigger, wider ranging, or with more targets, but not more damage or accuracy.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Okay so if you actually read that, first of all thank you, second of all things are looking pretty bleak. TLDR; Solars have DBs beat in accuracy, damage, defense and soak/mitigation.<br /> <br /> Well it gets bleaker sadly, with one of the main schticks of DBs being that they tend to do better when they're already doing well. They have a big list of charms that can only be activated if you're already ahead in initiative, or have aimed for 2 turns, or have blocked multiple attacks in a row, or punish your opponent for racking up a big onslaught penalty. Against a Solar you probably won't have higher initiative, you won't have the luxury of sitting back and aiming, you won't defend against their superior attacks very often, and they often quite easily drop their penalties.<br /> <br /> <br /> What does this mean? It means that a combat focused Solar is a damn hard fight for a single DB! Or even a small group of them. &quot;But Doctor Love Monkey&quot; I hear you cry &quot;I thought Solars weren't supposed to be impervious to DBs this time around.&quot;. Don't worry, they aren't. Let me give you a few Solar archetypes and show how they'd go. Spoilered again for space.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>The Beast*</b>: We all know this guy, the guy who takes nothing but melee, dodge and resistance charms, always wears his heavy armor, never has less than 5 dex. This guy is a tough fight. At essence 1 he still stands a chance of beating an essence 5 DB, but it's not as bad as you think. His only hope is to burn them down with a quick series of combos before his mote pool runs dry, after that he's basically screwed. At higher essences he can start to put together combos that in a white room can wipe a whole party of Dragonblooded. If you're fighting him as a PC party of DBs do not let him whiteroom you. Be willing to take losses and wear him down. You're going to have to hit him with some tough stuff in order to make him spend motes though, so expect heavy losses. You're relying on lucky dicerolls of less than 50% chance to hit most of the time, and the reverse to being hit.<br /> <br /> <b>The Well Rounded Fighter</b>: He's a dawn, sure, but he's got hobbies. He's picked up some sail, some war, some lore and some medicine. He's got charms in all of them. He's got good stats but not perfect. He's got a basic setup of melee charms to get him through combats easily enough. This guy is actually scared of a high essence DB. Remember when I said a lot of DB charms rely on you getting ahead first? Well getting ahead on this guy isn't impossible, and once you do you can do some decent damage. Even at medium essence this style of character doesn't want to face a full Wyld Hunt. He won't have the combos needed to take them out quickly, and while his defenses are decent he can't afford to keep using Dipping Swallow + Excellency to defend against every attack. If this is the Dawn in your PC party, a powerful Wyld Hunt will still be a threat for sure, especially if he's not maxed his dex.<br /> <br /> <b>The Ledger Jockey</b>: This guy is not a Dawn. He's an Eclipse**. Which means he's got a target on his head. Literally. He's a bureaucracy supernal with maybe the essence 1-2 charms of a martial art that he picked up. This guy goes down hard to a high essence DB. This is really where DBs get dangerous, because you're likely going to crash him on the first turn, then your anima is going to burn him while you decisive him into oblivion. Even at higher essence he's going to need to use tricks to avoid Wyld Hunts because he doesn't have the huge melee/dodge/resistance suites to defend against the DB dogpile. Just make sure he doesn't have any friends like The Beast up there.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Almost done I swear! This is all looking awful isn't it? It feels like the Solar charmset was almost designed to counter the DB one, with cheap, easy and hard counters to almost anything the terrestrials can muster. I mean if that's the case what's even the point? Can DBs do anything? You BET they can! They can strike weapons with the power of Earth to make them 1000 times heavier, they can use charms to fly across the battlefield in an instant and strike a foe, they can use presence to breathe fire and dodge to grab an opponents attack and hurl it at another enemy instead. It's SO COOL, it's just that the raw, pure power is low. You have to dodge the attack to redirect it, and that Earth weight one is a special gambit that you need to hit with, ect. It's not impossible, and it is helpful when it happens, but it's hard to pull off.<br /> <br /> So again, what's the point? The point is you're not always fighting Solar exalted, silly! This is where, in my opinion, DBs really shine. Fighting a Solar is a hard fought, frustrating slog, like a final boss fight. On the other hand fighting a pair of Hellboars is fantastic. For a Solar circle I wouldn't even ask them to roll, it'd be boring and pointless. For a DB sworn kinship on the other hand that's a fight! The boars can't ignore onslaught penalties, they don't have insane defense ratings or soak boosters or decisive damage negators. Plus if they stunt/willpower/environmental penalties they can actually hit a DB, whereas basically any Solar who's not intentionally gimped can raise their defense high enough to be 99% safe.<br /> <br /> Also, here the DB ability to deal more damage to things that they're already doing well against is an actual boon. Big monsters in exalted tend to not have the skill or dice caps of a Solar, but make up for it by big health pools and special abilities. Doing well against them in initiative doesn't mean you're going to win, but those punishing charms help to ensure you will.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> TLDR; So that's the light at the end of this tunnel. DBs don't have the raw power to match Solars for attack, defense, damage, soak, decisive mitigation, penalty negators or special tricks. They aren't so far behind though that Solars can't be beaten, it just takes luck, numbers and thinking outside the whiteroom. In exchange we get a splat that can meaningfully engage with most of the antagonists in the corebook with a veritable metric ton of charms that are really really cool and make for a dynamic and literally spectacular combat. Because who doesn't want to ride a self-made explosion to safety, or grapple a foe at long range with tendrils of water?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *There is absolutely nothing wrong with this character type. It's perfectly fine to have a character who's whole motivation is being the greatest fighter ever. No criticisms here for doing that. At least until you do it every time for 5 campaigns.<br /> <br /> **Or Twilight or you know whatever...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":20}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T18:53:58-07:00","id":1210737,"title":"","content":"This is the biggest difference I am seeing between the EX3 Core and DB:WFHW, you have this great system of mechanics in the EX3 Core that should make for one of the most exciting and complex rpg experiences out there...and the first thing the Solar charms do is make that entire system meaningless by boosting values to ridiculous degrees or just outright negating entire elements and challenges within the system. DB:WFHW doesn't do that, the DB charms presented in the book don't break the system, they let you find advantages and more optimal paths within the mechanics, but they almost never let you outright ignore mechanical challenges and that is how it should be. Up until this point the time I most enjoyed playing with the EX3 Core mechanics was actually as a mortal in a short game we ran, but looking at DB:WFHW I can see myself having that same experience while playing a DB.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T19:00:36-07:00","id":1210739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1210737#post1210737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the biggest difference I am seeing between the EX3 Core and DB:WFHW, you have this great system of mechanics in the EX3 Core that should make for one of the most exciting and complex rpg experiences out there...and the first thing the Solar charms do is make that entire system meaningless by boosting values to ridiculous degrees or just outright negating entire elements and challenges within the system. DB:WFHW doesn't do that, the DB charms presented in the book don't break the system, they let you find advantages and more optimal paths within the mechanics, but they almost never let you outright ignore mechanical challenges and that is how it should be. Up until this point the time I most enjoyed playing with the EX3 Core mechanics was actually as a mortal in a short game we ran, but looking at DB:WFHW I can see myself having that same experience while playing a DB.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's sadly one of the reasons why the Solar Exalted have to be the Corebook splat instead of the second one.<br /> <br /> Because if the Solars were anyone but the first Exalted out of the gate, they would seem INCREDIBLY cheap. Player resentment for that, and player sentimentality for the Dragon-Blooded as the first and most defining Exalted of the game, would basically doom any effort to persuade people to see Solars as anything but Anathema.<br /> <br /> To cast Solars as returning kings and queens trying to reclaim their unjustly stolen thrones and avenge their treacherous murders, they kind of have to come first. Also, they best fit the basic heroic protagonist mold, and are the biggest thing responsible for the sudden change in Creation's status quo.<br /> <br /> They're also the easy mode to the Dragon-Blooded expert mode; especially now.<br /> <br /> But if it weren't for those factors, the Dragon-Blooded absolutely should have been the first Exalted of the game, in every Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T19:05:40-07:00","id":1210741,"title":"","content":"I haven't looked at the DB Charms much yet myself, but one thing I have to ask - Solar Charms generally don't ELIMINIATE the Onslaught penalty. They allow the Solar to ignore the effects, but the penalty is still, strictly speaking, there. You say that one circumstance in which the Dragon-Blooded thrive is their opponent having a high Onslaught penalty, and then say &quot;but Solars can drop their penalties!&quot; Aren't they usually just <i>ignoring</i> their penalties? Does that make a difference in this scenario?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T19:16:44-07:00","id":1210749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1210741#post1210741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't looked at the DB Charms much yet myself, but one thing I have to ask - Solar Charms generally don't ELIMINIATE the Onslaught penalty. They allow the Solar to ignore the effects, but the penalty is still, strictly speaking, there. You say that one circumstance in which the Dragon-Blooded thrive is their opponent having a high Onslaught penalty, and then say &quot;but Solars can drop their penalties!&quot; Aren't they usually just <i>ignoring</i> their penalties? Does that make a difference in this scenario?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually a good question. I'm not sure if ignoring the onslaught penalty for your defense also ignores it for your opponent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T19:21:10-07:00","id":1210752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1210739#post1210739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that's sadly one of the reasons why the Solar Exalted have to be the Corebook splat instead of the second one.<br /> <br /> Because if the Solars were anyone but the first Exalted out of the gate, they would seem INCREDIBLY cheap. Player resentment for that, and player sentimentality for the Dragon-Blooded as the first and most defining Exalted of the game, would basically doom any effort to persuade people to see Solars as anything but Anathema.<br /> <br /> To cast Solars as returning kings and queens trying to reclaim their unjustly stolen thrones and avenge their treacherous murders, they kind of have to come first. Also, they best fit the basic heroic protagonist mold, and are the biggest thing responsible for the sudden change in Creation's status quo.<br /> <br /> They're also the easy mode to the Dragon-Blooded expert mode; especially now.<br /> <br /> But if it weren't for those factors, the Dragon-Blooded absolutely should have been the first Exalted of the game, in every Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally agree with this, its like you read my mind. In fact I just asked in the Ask the Devs thread how they will be balancing splats going forward. The question came up if Lunars and Sidereals would be able to meaningfully interact in a circle with Solars and the response was &quot;yes&quot;, but personally I feel that it would be a much better idea going forward to balance splats for how they should be able to interact with DB not Solars. To me Lunars will be much more fun to play if they are balanced to be a monster/antagonist scary enough to challenge a wyld hunt or a hero strong enough to fight the injustice of the Realm. Trying to crank them up to rival Solars in any way is a fool's errand if you don't want them to just end up being &quot;easy mode&quot; as you put it. In fact right now I think its more accurate to say Solar's are &quot;god mode&quot; where you just win, while DB's are &quot;regular mode&quot; where it isn't difficult to succeed but you still actually have to play the game to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T19:26:57-07:00","id":1210753,"title":"","content":"A good thread, and one of the reasons why Solars (though I love them) are difficult to Storytell for. There are so many interesting antagonists in the core book (and the monthly additions) but that are pretty much meaningless opposition against Solars unless you buff them a lot first. I've found that if I want to make a simple Exalted QC antagonist for my Solars to go up against, I need to at least add extra dice to their rolls to make the fight even close to fun.<br /> <br /> I don't have that fear for my coming DB game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T19:28:52-07:00","id":1210759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1210752#post1210752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I totally agree with this, its like you read my mind. In fact I just asked in the Ask the Devs thread how they will be balancing splats going forward. The question came up if Lunars and Sidereals would be able to meaningfully interact in a circle with Solars and the response was &quot;yes&quot;, but personally I feel that it would be a much better idea going forward to balance splats for how they should be able to interact with DB not Solars. To me Lunars will be much more fun to play if they are balanced to be a monster/antagonist scary enough to challenge a wyld hunt or a hero strong enough to fight the injustice of the Realm. Trying to crank them up to rival Solars in any way is a fool's errand if you don't want them to just end up being &quot;easy mode&quot; as you put it. In fact right now I think its more accurate to say Solar's are &quot;god mode&quot; where you just win, while DB's are &quot;regular mode&quot; where it isn't difficult to succeed but you still actually have to play the game to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, well honestly I think the DBs in WFHW can hang with Solars as long as they do it right. If the past is any indication though Lunars and Sids will be between the two, and have their own unique things to go along with it. It might be borderline a bit easy, but hopefully not go too far with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T20:43:42-07:00","id":1210780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1210752#post1210752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I totally agree with this, its like you read my mind. In fact I just asked in the Ask the Devs thread how they will be balancing splats going forward. The question came up if Lunars and Sidereals would be able to meaningfully interact in a circle with Solars and the response was &quot;yes&quot;, but personally I feel that it would be a much better idea going forward to balance splats for how they should be able to interact with DB not Solars. To me Lunars will be much more fun to play if they are balanced to be a monster/antagonist scary enough to challenge a wyld hunt or a hero strong enough to fight the injustice of the Realm. Trying to crank them up to rival Solars in any way is a fool's errand if you don't want them to just end up being &quot;easy mode&quot; as you put it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Robert and the others will manage to achieve all of those objectives. Solar Exalted are already &quot;monster/antagonist scary enough to challenge a Wyld Hunt&quot;, and they can't all shapeshift into werewolves and bears and elephants and birds and rats.<br /> <br /> One other thing occurs to me: Having the Solar Exalted come before the Dragon-Blooded also makes it possible to cast the Lunar Exalted as something other than Anathema. Which would be HARDER to do for them than Solars despite them not being QUITE as cheap, because the Lunar Exalted seem much more monstrous by nature and because they've practically EMBRACED the label of Anathema to terrorize the Realm.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In fact right now I think its more accurate to say Solar's are &quot;god mode&quot; where you just win, while DB's are &quot;regular mode&quot; where it isn't difficult to succeed but you still actually have to play the game to do it. </div> </div> </div>I don't think they're quite as easy as that, but we nevertheless agree that they're the easiest mode in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T20:58:45-07:00","id":1210792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1210753#post1210753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A good thread, and one of the reasons why Solars (though I love them) are difficult to Storytell for. There are so many interesting antagonists in the core book (and the monthly additions) but that are pretty much meaningless opposition against Solars unless you buff them a lot first. I've found that if I want to make a simple Exalted QC antagonist for my Solars to go up against, I need to at least add extra dice to their rolls to make the fight even close to fun.<br /> <br /> I don't have that fear for my coming DB game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think there was an unstated expectation that the original Devs had in which the EX3 Core relies on players reigning themselves in and making suboptimal choices in order to make the game more balanced and fun. The problem is that they never stated that expectation and designed charm trees that quickly steer you into game breaking combo's. I love the Solar narrative themes, they mesh with the characters I like to play more than any other splat I think, but it is honestly exhausting trying to play a Solar that is so artificially suboptimal just to try and make them actually fun. And as you say if the people you are playing with don't do the same you are quickly left behind in every encounter while the GM struggles to take the useless antagonists presented in the EX3 core and make them a challenge for even the most minimally specialized Solar.<br /> <br /> Honestly if it was up to me I would say that Solar's need a ground up rewrite, EX3 succeeded fantastically in creating a much better base mechanical system than 2e and I love it as it is, but honestly the rest of the EX3 Core still completely failed in making Solars any less a splat that just activates charms to unfailingly succeed. And to me that makes playing EX3 Solars so unappealing no matter much how they are supposed to be about legendary prowess in their themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T21:10:49-07:00","id":1210793,"title":"","content":"I don't need a rewrite, to be honest. I've used the system so much in the last few years that I've learned to live with the hiccups. The only thing that bothers me are dice tricks such as &quot;reroll X many 1s unless Y rolls a 6 because then the Z transforms into a Pony.&quot; For a game that was supposed to be relying on less dice rolls (which is why attack flurries were removed), it sure failed to comprehend why dice tricks are bad game design. My only gripe with DB charms is that this stuff is continuing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T21:17:53-07:00","id":1210798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1210749#post1210749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's actually a good question. I'm not sure if ignoring the onslaught penalty for your defense also ignores it for your opponent.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the case according to the devs in teh Q&amp;A thread, but I would need to dig to find it. But for effects depending on a Solar having onslaughts, Charms that let you ingore them don't like,s top you having that penalty by default I Think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T21:23:49-07:00","id":1210801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1210793#post1210793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't need a rewrite, to be honest. I've used the system so much in the last few years that I've learned to live with the hiccups. The only thing that bothers me are dice tricks such as &quot;reroll X many 1s unless Y rolls a 6 because then the Z transforms into a Pony.&quot; For a game that was supposed to be relying on less dice rolls (which is why attack flurries were removed), it sure failed to comprehend why dice tricks are bad game design. My only gripe with DB charms is that this stuff is continuing.</div> </div> </div> </div>They have a free dice roller app that seems well set up to handle it when that kind of possibly annoying book keeping is needed. Lets you select double successes on numbers and auto reroll on other numbers (and you can select more then one number at a time). Doesn't cover 'and if your opponent rolls such and such' but it does save the rolls so you can reference them instead of having to write them all down to simplify it a little.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T21:29:01-07:00","id":1210805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1210780#post1210780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Robert and the others will manage to achieve all of those objectives. Solar Exalted are already &quot;monster/antagonist scary enough to challenge a Wyld Hunt&quot;, and they can't all shapeshift into werewolves and bears and elephants and birds and rats.<br /> <br /> One other thing occurs to me: Having the Solar Exalted come before the Dragon-Blooded also makes it possible to cast the Lunar Exalted as something other than Anathema. Which would be HARDER to do for them than Solars despite them not being QUITE as cheap, because the Lunar Exalted seem much more monstrous by nature and because they've practically EMBRACED the label of Anathema to terrorize the Realm.<br /> <br /> I don't think they're quite as easy as that, but we nevertheless agree that they're the easiest mode in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solar's definitely fit that role as the monster/antagonist, though as the original poster states they maybe stretch the bounds a little too far in the difficulty of DB overcoming them as an antagonist. My point with Lunars and Sidereals was more that when you are balancing them it seems to me that it is more productive to build them proportionally to being a challenge to DB rather than designing with the intent to make them a rival to Solars.<br /> <br /> In my mind if there was a scale of 1 to 10 in potency within the mechanics of exalted you would have a mortal at 1, a DB at 3 or 4, and a Solar at 10 in the current state of the game. The problem is that the base mechanics work really well even at 1, and the further you go up the scale the more you compromise those mechanics and the ability of EX3 to be a game where you can be meaningfully challenged without making your GM jump through burning hoops. If you are now designing Lunars and Sidereals that leaves you with a choice, do you balance them at a power level of 5 or 6 with the goal of making them a step up above DB, or do you place them even higher at 7, 8, or even 9 in an attempt to put them in a playing space that overlaps with Solars? In my mind the later option really runs the risk of Lunars and Sidereals falling into the same pitfalls of mechanical power that Solars suffer from. I think it would be healthier for EX3 as a whole if Solars are left up on their pedestal for better or worse as these unapproachable gods, while future splats ignore them and look to each other to set their relative power within a range that compliments the mechanics rather than overwhelming them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T21:37:54-07:00","id":1210811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1210793#post1210793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't need a rewrite, to be honest. I've used the system so much in the last few years that I've learned to live with the hiccups. The only thing that bothers me are dice tricks such as &quot;reroll X many 1s unless Y rolls a 6 because then the Z transforms into a Pony.&quot; For a game that was supposed to be relying on less dice rolls (which is why attack flurries were removed), it sure failed to comprehend why dice tricks are bad game design. My only gripe with DB charms is that this stuff is continuing.</div> </div> </div> </div>The DB do have some of those dice tricks but they seem a bit less arbitrary to me, they feel more like a clear bonus and less like matching three cherries on a slot machine.<br /> <br /> Our group kinda did the same thing feeling out Solars, through a series of medium length campaigns we learned the in and outs of playing EX3 Solars and pretty much found every trick and option to make them more playable and challenge them...but then we moved on to other systems for a bit and realized looking back that we have literally ZERO interest in playing EX3 with Solars ever again, and its not like we just got burnt out on them for the time being, with the benefit of hindsight we are really certain that they just aren't something that we consider worth wasting the time and effort on to massage a satisfactory experience out of playing them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T21:42:32-07:00","id":1210815,"title":"","content":"I adore the narrative of Solars. And my storytelling is usually more story oriented and mechanics-lite. Probably why I'm more tolerant to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T21:57:45-07:00","id":1210818,"title":"","content":"So that's combat, what about social? I haven't made time to read the book yet but from what I hear the gap might be far narrower there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T22:48:40-07:00","id":1210828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1210818#post1210818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So that's combat, what about social? I haven't made time to read the book yet but from what I hear the gap might be far narrower there.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Cracks knuckles*<br /> <br /> <br /> Eh...tomorrow...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T23:30:32-07:00","id":1210838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1210811#post1210811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The DB do have some of those dice tricks but they seem a bit less arbitrary to me, they feel more like a clear bonus and less like matching three cherries on a slot machine.<br /> <br /> Our group kinda did the same thing feeling out Solars, through a series of medium length campaigns we learned the in and outs of playing EX3 Solars and pretty much found every trick and option to make them more playable and challenge them...but then we moved on to other systems for a bit and realized looking back that we have literally ZERO interest in playing EX3 with Solars ever again, and its not like we just got burnt out on them for the time being, with the benefit of hindsight we are really certain that they just aren't something that we consider worth wasting the time and effort on to massage a satisfactory experience out of playing them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I have to say STing for Solars and even playing one was an odd experience. I felt almost as if they were out of scope with the world they were in. To which some people would reply, &quot;Of course they are, that's the point!&quot;. That's not really what I mean though, it's just that the challenges that the game seemed to be leading me toward my players were just so far beneath them, and I couldn't plausibly come up with harder ones. I ended up having to make a river spirit dragon as powerful as a directional censor to get the kind of plot I wanted out of it, and that just felt wrong.<br /> <br /> Maybe the scope that I wanted to play at just wasn't Solar scope? I preferred smaller games centered around a single kingdom, but all the threats of the wilderness or the gods just ended up crumpling to my players without having to pass over a second thought. I might come back to ST them if I want to play a truly epic game where the world is being torn apart and I can justify some of the stuff better. Otherwise it can feel at bit like playing Superman in the Nolan Batman films.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T23:33:15-07:00","id":1210839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1210818#post1210818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So that's combat, what about social? I haven't made time to read the book yet but from what I hear the gap might be far narrower there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would say that looking at the DB charms they are still numerically way less powerful in terms of the social systems, but the saving grace there is that EX3 does a pretty good job of making the social system something that can't be &quot;won&quot; or &quot;lost&quot; unlike like the combat system. So even if Solars are way more likely to wildly succeed in social actions, the result of those actions are usually way more nuanced and flavourful, in contrast to that same sort of threshold success attached to a sword strike utterly obliterating someone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T23:52:15-07:00","id":1210846,"title":"","content":"I think tellings stories for Solars is like the good comics for Superman, that is, the best and most compelling Superman stories are not about him being challenged by comprable power, but rather How he deals with the consequences and problems of having so much power. These arnt the easiest stories to tell, and tell good, but this may be part of it. I am not trying to say anyone is playing the game wrong, but rather that the types of stories that Solars excel in may be narrower than other splats. Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T00:24:11-07:00","id":1210852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1210846#post1210846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think tellings stories for Solars is like the good comics for Superman, that is, the best and most compelling Superman stories are not about him being challenged by comprable power, but rather How he deals with the consequences and problems of having so much power. These arnt the easiest stories to tell, and tell good, but this may be part of it. I am not trying to say anyone is playing the game wrong, but rather that the types of stories that Solars excel in may be narrower than other splats. Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Those are also my favourite superman comics. Although I admit sometimes watching big blue struggle can be good too. Even something as simple as needs the help of Lex Luthor's secretary to remove his kryptonite necklace.<br /> <br /> Either way I have definitely head this before. The problem there is threefold in my opinion. One is that it requires a lot of buy in from all the players. You need to have a party that's basically willing to sit there and have interesting philosophical debates about how much of their power is too much, at what point do they ceaS being leaders and start being slaves to the million injustices of the world, how can they give their people free will and security, etc.<br /> <br /> Another is just that those stories are hard to craft. I consider myself a pretty veteran ST, and I struggle to do that kind of plot on a weekly basis.<br /> <br /> The third is that you actually don't need to be as powerful as all that to tell those kind of stories. Well, okay to be One Punch Mans Saitama you do. DBs are perfectly capable of telling those stories though. A Solar might tear down a Satrap effortlessly and then the story would be about what are the consequences of living in a place that's been a satrapy so long that their culture has started to entwine itself with each other, can you even separate them anymore? Do you deport the troops who surrendered? What of the ones who fought for the realm loyally but were natives?<br /> <br /> You can actually tell those stories with Dragonblooded protagonists too, but the focus is more split I guess. Whereas in some satrapies I might jus tell let the circle walk into the throne room and hand wave the ensuing combat to get to the good stuff, I mean what's he got? A couple young DBs and a few mortal guards? Whereas there'd be at least a few sessions of terrestrials setting up this coup. <br /> <br /> <br /> So maybe that's it, the Solar focus is just different, the combats are kind of supposed to be compelling for their one sidedness. Like maybe I should play out that throne room brawl just to remind everyone how easy it is, and then contrast that to how hard the other parts are. Either way I think i like the lower power version better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T02:11:28-07:00","id":1210868,"title":"","content":"I wonder if Infernals and Abyssals will fall into the same &quot;easy mode&quot; problem as solars do. It might be unavoidable, all things considered.<br /> <br /> Still, I suppose they'll at least have the solars to fight. And finally provide a challenge to the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T05:01:26-07:00","id":1210902,"title":"","content":"Has anyone looked into what anti-HTH options DBs have?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T05:48:40-07:00","id":1210913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1210902#post1210902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone looked into what anti-HTH options DBs have?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is an essence 3 resistance charm that can reduce knockback called immovable mountain technique. It\u2019s up to the ST for the effect but it suggests HTH might half the successes for the purposes of determining knockback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T05:55:19-07:00","id":1210918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded#post1210732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Great analysis&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> I would be excited to see you do this for DB vs Lunars (when we get them) as they are enemies and have been for a long time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T06:39:00-07:00","id":1210931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>light-hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1210918#post1210918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I would be excited to see you do this for DB vs Lunars (when we get them) as they are enemies and have been for a long time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! Stay tuned in this thread for my non-combat analysis! I might split it into non combat and social.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T07:12:49-07:00","id":1210944,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a> I think you raise VERY valid points and I absolutely agree these are not easy to run stories. I think it might have been an added benefit of mine that I was running by weekly not weekly. I think you accurately put it that a Solar games focus is different than the others, by nature of who it is. When I ran my Solar Shard, I typically came at the party indirectly, or at an angle from what they were used to. Typically the main villains were trying to use their own strength against them, and in that way it creates drama and tension. Though like supes, the only ones who could challenge them on an equal footing were things massively outside the league of anything else in setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T08:05:57-07:00","id":1210958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1210838#post1210838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe the scope that I wanted to play at just wasn't Solar scope? I preferred smaller games centered around a single kingdom, but all the threats of the wilderness or the gods just ended up crumpling to my players without having to pass over a second thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>And, to be fair to you, a lot of the flavor for Solar Exalted in first and third edition seems to agree with what you want to play. Like, the book suggests against a global perspective, but that can be hard to do when you have to go up to Second Circle Demons, other Celestial Exalted, or Directional Gods of War to challenge players meaningfully for combat. I've yet to find a full fix for it, but here's a couple of things I've tried.<ul><li>First is just kinda buffing most things in the book. The EX modes in <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1qA52CN4tbGbGS74qwL4LQiXE5f5lHCkk2C7dccIHF98/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Sandact6's amazing bestiary</a> are a good approach to this.</li> <li>Actually, just use Sandact6's bestiary. If you get past the trolling in its writing, the thing is full of mechanical blocks that you can reskin into basically any game to make combat more challenging for PCs.</li> <li>Another trick I have taken to is making battle groups more powerful. For starters, I've made Might much, much more common. It's still rare to see things running around with might all the time, but any god worth its salt can hand out Might to their people for important battles. Secondly, attacks from battle groups inflict onslaught penalties equal to the group's Size; fighting an opponent in the middle of their Size 5 battle group is now mostly suicidal.</li> <li>With the new Dragon-Blooded content, I haven't had a chance to try this stuff, but you'd better believe that boss-tier Dragon-Blooded do not play by the same rules for Aura mechanics. Wanna fight a narratively important Dragon-Blooded? Their Aura is going to be what <i>they</i> want it to be, elemental keywords be damned.</li> <li>The other trick is, as people in this thread mentioned, players choosing intentionally suboptimal builds. I highly recommend this one. One of my friends is running a game where the game-contract agreement was &quot;No Combat (Archery, Brawl, Martial Arts, Melee, Thrown) Supernals&quot; and it runs much closer to what the text suggests Solars should feel like. Our circle is running a kingdom, shaking the world, and being the talk of the region, but we're also dreading and preparing the day that the Realm, Lookshy, Prasad or (gulp) all three notice us</li> </ul>When it comes to Dragon-Blooded PCs in Solar parties, I actually think that they're in a good spot. They're going to underperform the other PCs, but they can do weird elemental shit that Solars don't get (without evocations) and being in a party with Solars actually covers one of their main weaknesses for combat - needing to be doing well consistently. Lastly, I think that the nature of the current Dragon-Blooded set is such that the only real buffs they need in a Solar party are some tweaks on experience numbers. This is a really slapdash fix, but bringing Evocations down to 10xp (or lower, if necessary) can put a serious bandaid on that power scale. Same with giving a player some free Terrestrial XP each session for being a Terrestrial in a Celestial group.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T10:24:36-07:00","id":1211025,"title":"","content":"What do you think of the DB's chances with the Immaculate Styles? I'm only a few charms in but they seem stronk<b>\u2122</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T10:49:54-07:00","id":1211042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211025#post1211025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think of the DB's chances with the Immaculate Styles? I'm only a few charms in but they seem stronk<b>\u2122</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Versus the combat monster Dawn that was described earlier nothing really changes because most of the powerful DB charms you will never get to use and when you do they will probably not even hit. One on one even when super combat focused against the laid-back Dawn you will still get destroyed. Two-three DB combat monsters versus one laid-back Dawn is doable for sure at lower essence values. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T10:55:52-07:00","id":1211046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211025#post1211025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think of the DB's chances with the Immaculate Styles? I'm only a few charms in but they seem stronk<b>\u2122</b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'll note that Earth Dragon Style has some good stuff, especially regarding fall damage and HTH.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T11:05:26-07:00","id":1211057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211025#post1211025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think of the DB's chances with the Immaculate Styles? I'm only a few charms in but they seem stronk<b>\u2122</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ll do an immaculate update tonight before I do my non-combat analysis. A little preview though is the styles are good, damn good, and have good in-style synergy. It even helps shore up some of the damage and mitigation holes a bit. Can it overcome the previous hurdles though? We\u2019ll see.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackheartz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211042#post1211042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Versus the combat monster Dawn that was described earlier nothing really changes because most of the powerful DB charms you will never get to use and when you do they will probably not even hit. One on one even when super combat focused against the laid-back Dawn you will still get destroyed. Two-three DB combat monsters versus one laid-back Dawn is doable for sure at lower essence values. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I will also say that this is probably a bit cynical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T12:41:31-07:00","id":1211106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211057#post1211057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019ll do an immaculate update tonight before I do my non-combat analysis. A little preview though is the styles are good, damn good, and have good in-style synergy. It even helps shore up some of the damage and mitigation holes a bit. Can it overcome the previous hurdles though? We\u2019ll see.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I will also say that this is probably a bit cynical.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, that was not my intent and just to clarify I love the DB charmset and am completely fine with where they stand powerwise. The basic premise of my post still holds true in white room fights, so the correct thing to do is what you suggested and do not let combat focused Dawns white-room you. I mean I could run an actual simulation, if I was not too lazy to set it up, (usually 10000 repeats) like I did for combat focused werewolf vs combat focused vampire in the Werewolf subforum a few years back but I think its pretty clear in this case what the result will be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3669,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","user":"blackheartz","date":". 04-24-2018, 03:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T12:59:57-07:00","id":1211111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1210739#post1210739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that's sadly one of the reasons why the Solar Exalted have to be the Corebook splat instead of the second one.<br /> <br /> Because if the Solars were anyone but the first Exalted out of the gate, they would seem INCREDIBLY cheap. Player resentment for that, and player sentimentality for the Dragon-Blooded as the first and most defining Exalted of the game, would basically doom any effort to persuade people to see Solars as anything but Anathema.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sunder, this is maybe the smartest thing you've ever written and you should be proud of putting your finger directly on something important in a very concise way.<br /> <br /> One quibble:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But if it weren't for those factors, the Dragon-Blooded absolutely should have been the first Exalted of the game, in every Edition. </div> </div> </div>I would say there's another factor; Solars have a lot less baggage for your aspiring hero type or from a player coming in from a system that's a lot less focused on society and history than any other Exalt type.<br /> <br /> The Dragon-Blooded have basically ruled the world for like 1500 years, have a polity that has a colorable argument for &quot;greatest empire the world has ever known&quot; at their back, and there are enormous societal expectations and the baggage that come with them undergirding them. Sure, you can play an Outcaste who doesn't live in the Realm... which means chunking 9/10ths of your available system resources.<br /> <br /> Lunars and Sidereals and Abyssals have their own societies and baggage. Sidereals HELLA have that; they focus heavily on finding you and inculcating you hardcore into your role in their ranks. Being a ronin is and always has been... difficult. Lunars are more capable of going it alone but the Silver Pact is still there and other Lunars will have certain expectations regarding how you treat them and how you interact with the Forever War going on between them and the Realm. Abyssals... well. I mean, you literally can't create an Abyssal without a faustian bargain.<br /> <br /> Solars absolutely don't have that. There's a very clean, hard break between the time when they had a society around them and the time the game is set in. The genocide and their imprisonment was near-complete, and they return in a world as blank slates, without Elders to tell them what is expected of them and to inculcate them into a shared society with shared beliefs. They come from everywhere and can do anything, and the only real baggage they have is &quot;the Evil Empire wants you to die.&quot;<br /> <br /> (It's a little like playing a Jedi.)<br /> <br /> This is a good way to give players a huge array of options. You can play the classic lone hero, or group of mismatched heroes, who begin the game drinking in a tavern somewhere without having to worry about this giant pack of peers who might judge you and try and fit you into boxes and circumscribe your life. (They might try and murder you, of course.)<br /> <br /> I feel like this is very important in a starting splat.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T13:19:15-07:00","id":1211119,"title":"","content":"I'll start by noting that I'm yet all that familiar with the system. So please read my question as a question, not as some sort of statement about how things are.<br /> <br /> An issue that I didn't see discussed in this thread is that mote regeneration for DB's is the same as for Solars. If the solars are outnumbered, how many times can they use their full excellences before they're down to 5 motes each round? When the essence supplies are low won't 2 dragonblooded make short work of one solar of equal experience? With numbers, won't limited essence respiration typically push a fight in favor of several dragonblooded winning over few solars, despite their better charms and higher die pools?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","user":"Apromor","date":". 08-20-2018, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T13:56:00-07:00","id":1211145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Apromor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211119#post1211119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll start by noting that I'm yet all that familiar with the system. So please read my question as a question, not as some sort of statement about how things are.<br /> <br /> An issue that I didn't see discussed in this thread is that mote regeneration for DB's is the same as for Solars. If the solars are outnumbered how many times can they use their full excellences before they're down to 5 motes each round? When the essence supplies are low won't 2 dragonblooded make short work of one solar of equal experience? With numbers, won't limited essence respiration typically push a fight in favor of several dragonblooded winning over few solars, despite their better charms and higher die pools?</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s a good point, I think you might grasp this system better than your think, and one I will address in my next analysis post. Also there\u2019s a mathematical difference between withering and decisive attacks that, unfortunately, interacts poorly for the DB charmset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T14:14:32-07:00","id":1211153,"title":"","content":"This actually brings up a question I think is critical to address. When you are up against an E5 The Beast, how many Dragon-Blooded does it take to kill him? Because, frankly, if the answer is less than a million, then the ruleset is in better shape than Second Edition was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T14:54:42-07:00","id":1211167,"title":"","content":"What do DB synergies with other Exalted feel like they could look like? Particularly I'm thinking of the two Celestials, who are the main sort of &quot;Able to mix it up with Solars without being a) Solars or b) sort of apocalyptic and bad for people in general and you maybe wouldn't want to help them&quot; splats, and of those, particularly the erstwhile DB allies, the Sidereals.<br /> <br /> The mention of DBs having more strengths when they have room to breathe or get ahead makes me wonder if there's a bigger return to having them in the battle against a Solar when they've got an ally who can take care of taking the pressure off. Basically, do they do &quot;support&quot; as a relative strength? (Which I'd guess they maybe ought to, given what their role in the grand scheme of things is meant to be.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T15:13:51-07:00","id":1211176,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m just going to put this here as my $0.02 on the Solar power level. I actually LOVED the fact that nothing could really challenge my Dawn. It was a lot of fun walking around knowing that you could turn any and everyone into juice, but that\u2019s just not who you are. And it was so fun getting to show it every now and then. My character never took a single health box of damage ever, but I never felt like the adventures we went on were easy. I would have felt somehow cheated if my Dawn had met his veritable match in combat, though. The challenge to our group was making a positive difference in the world without being monsters, and I think that\u2019s kind of the point of Solars. Yes, I can pop the governor\u2019s head like a zit, but then the people only see a murderous beast, and we\u2019re trying to \u201csave them\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T15:19:51-07:00","id":1211179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211111#post1211111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sunder, this is maybe the smartest thing you've ever written and you should be proud of putting your finger directly on something important in a very concise way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, though I feel like I said the same thing earlier this month. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1210737#post1210737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the biggest difference I am seeing between the EX3 Core and DB:WFHW, you have this great system of mechanics in the EX3 Core that should make for one of the most exciting and complex rpg experiences out there...and the first thing the Solar charms do is make that entire system meaningless by boosting values to ridiculous degrees or just outright negating entire elements and challenges within the system.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211111#post1211111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars have a lot less baggage for your aspiring hero type or from a player coming in from a system that's a lot less focused on society and history than any other Exalt type.<br /> <br /> The Dragon-Blooded have basically ruled the world for like 1500 years, have a polity that has a colorable argument for &quot;greatest empire the world has ever known&quot; at their back, and there are enormous societal expectations and the baggage that come with them undergirding them. Sure, you can play an Outcaste who doesn't live in the Realm... which means chunking 9/10ths of your available system resources.<br /> <br /> Lunars and Sidereals and Abyssals have their own societies and baggage. Sidereals HELLA have that; they focus heavily on finding you and inculcating you hardcore into your role in their ranks. Being a ronin is and always has been... difficult. Lunars are more capable of going it alone but the Silver Pact is still there and other Lunars will have certain expectations regarding how you treat them and how you interact with the Forever War going on between them and the Realm. Abyssals... well. I mean, you literally can't create an Abyssal without a faustian bargain.<br /> <br /> Solars absolutely don't have that. There's a very clean, hard break between the time when they had a society around them and the time the game is set in. The genocide and their imprisonment was near-complete, and they return in a world as blank slates, without Elders to tell them what is expected of them and to inculcate them into a shared society with shared beliefs. They come from everywhere and can do anything, and the only real baggage they have is &quot;the Evil Empire wants you to die.&quot;<br /> <br /> (It's a little like playing a Jedi.)<br /> <br /> This is a good way to give players a huge array of options. You can play the classic lone hero, or group of mismatched heroes, who begin the game drinking in a tavern somewhere without having to worry about this giant pack of peers who might judge you and try and fit you into boxes and circumscribe your life. (They might try and murder you, of course.)<br /> <br /> I feel like this is very important in a starting splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, quite.<br /> <br /> Starting the game with the Solar Exalted allows players to engage with the game engine and the setting only as much as they want to.<br /> <br /> For the first splat of a game without any advanced material ready, and for completely new players, that\u2019s absolutely vital. <br /> <br /> If the players want to immerse themselves in the challenges of the engine, they can play suboptimal or mortal characters.<br /> <br /> If they want to immerse themselves in the setting, they can Exalt as a mortal Dynast, or ally with the Silver Pact, or swear allegiance to a Deathlord... or they can just kick around in forgotten dungeons and explore new frontiers and slay dragons like DnD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-24-2018, 06:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T15:37:15-07:00","id":1211187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steamfunk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211153#post1211153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This actually brings up a question I think is critical to address. When you are up against an E5 The Beast, how many Dragon-Blooded does it take to kill him? Because, frankly, if the answer is less than a million, then the ruleset is in better shape than Second Edition was.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking at the Immaculate styles.... I'm thinking a proper Wyld Hunt could mess one up, if we're talking a full set of 5 Sworn Kin Immaculate Shikari with the Elemental Dragon styles, mortal auxilaries (to ramp up that onslaught, especially if any of the DBs is using War to coordinate them) and some of the nastier combination options (Dragon Vortex Attack with all 5 elements involved is <i>mean</i>, and it hugely synergizes with stuff like Earth and Water Dragon styles penalizing a target for having movement or wound penalties)<br /> <br /> Which really looks into a specific mechanical thing I noted, which is how Solar penalty negators actually work. Do they count as literally a &quot;cleanse&quot;, removing the penalty for the duration? Or are they simply a counterbalance, essentially giving the Solar an equal-and-opposite buff to neutralize the penalty? The former is MUCH more painful to Immaculate Dragon Stylists than the latter, because of how Earth and Water still bypass penalty negation by the way their charms interact with how many movement or wound penalties they have. And then you have the potential for your Fire Aspect to start using Fire Dragon to literally burn away a Solar's initiative and essence to drain him faster.<br /> <br /> It's possible that the Beast could still win that kind of optimized, massed opposition? But I think it'd be far from effortless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1817-opmegs","name":"OpMegs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1817_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T15:56:57-07:00","id":1211193,"title":"","content":"Didn\u2019t all five Styles used to allow the heaviest of armor? Now Air and Wood only allow light, and neither Fire or Water can go heavy.<br /> <br /> But then, \u201cmagitech Elemental Dragon Armor and Warstriders\u201d aren\u2019t meant to be the inevitable end-goal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T17:48:56-07:00","id":1211240,"title":"","content":"Okay I'm back at the computer time for another write up. I'm planning to do another three sections. One which includes the Immaculate styles and a deeper dive into exalted's power dynamics and combat structure. It's gonna get a little mathy but I promise to keep it at a minimum. Then I'm going to do social charms, comparing DBs to Solars, and then other non-combat stuff like craft/athletics and do the same.<br /> <br /> Ready? Okay here we go.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211025#post1211025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think of the DB's chances with the Immaculate Styles? I'm only a few charms in but they seem stronk<b>\u2122</b></div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, what are the Immaculate Styles doing to help? Well a lot actually. For one we have a good damage adder, Perfect Blazing Blow, doubling 8s up to (Essence) times basically adds (Essence) auto successes to the damage roll. Sweet. We've also got a few charms for soak and some resistant evasion, nice! These styles are powerful. Unfortunately, they sacrifice some stuff for that power. Most importantly, armor. Air dragon can only wear light, Fire Dragon, medium, ect. That's kind of a mark against them, and unfortunately it's more bad news with none of the styles doing much more than the attack/defense charms from the main set to stop attacks.<br /> <br /> <b>Why are Solars So Dangerous?</b><br /> <br /> Okay so why is this such a big deal? Well to understand that we first need to understand why Solar exalted are SO deadly. Once we have a good sense of why that is, we can see why so much hinges on attacks, particularly decisive ones.<br /> <br /> The first reason that they're so deadly is the intentional structure of the Solar charmset. They have a LOT of charms which are supplemental and/or reflexive, that means they can combo together complementary effects for a massive boost that's greater than the sum of it's parts. Lets take a look at a few, shall we? What follows is a big somewhat intricate Solar combo.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Take, for example Thunderbolt Attack Prana. An athletics charm actually! Which costs 4m 1wp, supplemental, can be comboed with any other ability, allows the user to jump a range band in any direction and DOUBLES damage after it is rolled. This alone means that a Solar can be deadly at as little as 8 initiative.<br /> <br /> Now lets see what we can combo this with. I like the look of Invincible Fury of the Dawn there. For 5m 1wp that lets me make up to 5 attacks, distributed how I please, move a range band between each attack, and instantly gain initiative equal to the number of attacks I want to make. Also, apart from the excellency, and charm I use on one attack can be used for free on the others. It can also be activated reflexively after using Peony Blossom Technique.<br /> <br /> So since all the stuff is free past the first I might as well load up, Excellent Strike (3m) rerolls 1s until they fail to appear, neutralizing a common DB trick to boost their defense in the process, and Hungry Tiger (3m 2i), which lets our overflow attack successes add to the damage.<br /> <br /> Plus, of course, Rising Sun Slash, which activates on a straight 7,8,9,10 being rolled and gives me one bonus non-charm sux and (essence) non-charm dice on the attack roll.<br /> <br /> OKAY so we're ready to make our attack. With as little as 10 initiative, lets see what we can do. We'll make 5 attacks, instantly giving us 5 initiative. That's 5 attacks with 3 base damage, then we attack. First we use Perfect Strike Discipline to give our first attack a full free excellency, between that and a level 2 stunt we're basically rocking 25 dice to attack, plus rerolling 1s, plus a big non-charm bonus with Rising Sun Slash, which is surprisingly common at those dice levels. Against a typical DB Defense of, say, 10, they've got no hope. Simplified calculations give us around 16 successes. That overflows by 6 so we get to deal 9 damage, which is then doubled thanks to TAP, giving us around 7.2 health levels, which is lethal against somebody without ox-bodies. If we drop our first target, great, if not, hit them again. When they drop we then reset Perfect Strike Discipline, for another free full excellency, and can jump a range band if we have to in order to strike our next target, and so on.<br /> <br /> If we have just one target the onslaught penalty keeps racking up so that's good too.<br /> <br /> And if we have a charm called Foe-Cleaving Focus we actually regenerate a mote for every 10 on an attack that triggers Rising Sun Slash. Which is good because that took like, at least 20-25 motes and 3-4 willpower.<br /> <br /> <br /> People are going to point out that wearing artifact full plate would use hardness to defend decently against that, but this was just an example to show how Solar charms work, I don't want to proc a mechanics arms race to infinite xp.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Phew! That was a lot of stuff! You might have noticed that we used up a lot of motes and a ton of willpower, you may also have noticed that we killed everyone in the process. All of that up there? That can be activated after striking with One Weapon Two Blows, and then Peony Blossom Attack, which SHOULD result in more than 10 initiative. That's just one of many many combos out there.<br /> <br /> This is sort of the nature of The Beast, who's just in it to go full throttle on power. If he can reliably hit you, then he just runs roughshod all over you, just like that. So how reliably can he hit you? If you're a DB wielding an artifact medium weapon your max defense is around 10, his max withering with a light artifact weapon is 26 dice, 21 for decisive, and he's got dice tricks like Excellent Strike and Rising Sun Slash to boost that even further and negate your defenses that use his 1s against him. So yeah he's hitting you.<br /> <br /> Conversely as a DB your highest is 22 withering, 17 decisive, and his parry is 12, his dodge can be even higher. That's why accuracy and defense are so important, because the Solar has an insane ability to generate damage. They likewise have an insane ability to absorb it but I'll be here all day if I go into that.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is actually a design feature! Not a bug. Part of the fun of Solars is coming up with those insane combos, or building them as your character grows, and unleashing them. Now let's look at DBs. Well, in contrast so stark we should call it Iron Man a ton of their charms are Simple! They don't combo together at all, they're all just discreet individual tricks and powers that do really cool one-off things. It makes for some fun charm trees, but also kills their ability to mix a ton of stuff together and explode their power like a Solar can. Incidentally, this might answer your question @Apromor.<br /> <br /> <b>Outnumbering Solars</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Apromor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211119#post1211119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An issue that I didn't see discussed in this thread is that mote regeneration for DB's is the same as for Solars. If the solars are outnumbered how many times can they use their full excellences before they're down to 5 motes each round? When the essence supplies are low won't 2 dragonblooded make short work of one solar of equal experience? With numbers, won't limited essence respiration typically push a fight in favor of several dragonblooded winning over few solars, despite their better charms and higher die pools?</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars simply have the power to end fights early enough that respiration doesn't always matter, at least if there's high essence or a Dawn involved. What if there isn't a Dawn though? And the small circle is like essence 1-2? Then you're absolutely right! A larger group of Dragonblooded will wear down those 1 or 2 Solars. If those terrestrials are unleashing their full power on every attack and you're defending the same, you're going to run dry fast. Particularly because your full excellency is 170% as expensive as the DB one, and doesn't even have any special benefits added.<br /> <br /> That's kind of why the DB charmset doesn't quite work to counter a true combat monster Solar. THAT BEING SAID, it's not hopeless, it's just hard. You need to rely on luck, you might only have a 40% chance of hitting him and he's got a 65% chance of hitting you, but he could easily roll poorly on his join battle, and then you and your Hearth roll well, work together, get a few more lucky rolls to hit him and crash him right off the bat. It can happen, and if it does then you stand a good chance of winning! Which is a huge difference between this edition and the last. If you get lucky, or somehow bend the environment to help you, then you can beat even those odds. It's just that you don't have a similarly devastating combo.<br /> <br /> There's another upside too, and it also stems from Solars being so combo-happy. If they don't have bits of the combo, their power drops off drastically. That's why the Well Rounded Dawn is so much easier than The Beast. He's not taken TAP and all the Rising Sun Slash upgrades, which tanks that whole combo a lot up there.<br /> <br /> <b>Immaculate Martial Arts</b><br /> <br /> Anyway where was I? Oh yeah Immaculate Martial arts. You know, there's one kind of opponent who's not exalted, but is still really powerful. Spirits. Higher essence gods, elementals and demons can challenge even Solar exalted in my experience, so how are Dragonblooded supposed to beat them? Flippin Immaculate Martial Arts that's how! They're powerful in exactly the kind of ways that Solars are good at defending against, and spirits are not. A circle of Dragonblooded immaculates using these charms on basically any god or demon would be painful to watch. Increasing wound penalties, onslaught penalties, and then crushing them with iconic finishing moves. This is a &quot;vs Solars&quot; thread, but I thought I should just mention that they're still great<br /> <br /> Against a less than optimal Solar, they can actually work. As soon as you start ranking up those penalties you basically add a dipping swallow tax to every attack that you make, that's good. The other effects if you can land them are even better, like Hungry Earth. In the event that you get that off the Solar can't retreat or use any shenanigans to hit and run, which is great. So I guess the conclusion is that if you want to fight Solars, bring Immaculates anyway, but the odds are still not on your side without numbers and environments.<br /> <br /> Aside: Did you know that an Air Dragon master can sit in an open field, using Avenging Wind Strike, chakrams and Lightning Strike Style to fling opponents away and strike them at distance before they even get close enough to swing at her? That's so cool.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'll end this post here but start a new one comparing Social charms. Sorry if it was a bit rambly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T19:57:21-07:00","id":1211272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211240#post1211240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first reason that they're so deadly is the intentional structure of the Solar charmset. They have a LOT of charms which are supplemental and/or reflexive, that means they can combo together complementary effects for a massive boost that's greater than the sum of it's parts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you can discount the way that Solars have &quot;get out of jail free&quot; cards in a way that Dragon-Blooded don't.<br /> <br /> A lot of the Dragon-Blooded charm trees have finishing moves/alpha strikes that have a difficult reset condition attached to them. Solars have those too... but the Beast has access to at least one kind of &quot;nope! Fuck <i>you</i>&quot; perfect. Dragon-Blooded struggle with that.<br /> <br /> This puts Dragon-Blooded in a bit of a bind, because it means committing in heavily might merely result in HGD or Seven Shadow Evasion getting popped. But trying to stand in against a Solar over the long haul... ooof.<br /> <br /> On a narrative, rather than purely mechanical, level, there just aren't likely to be that many Dragon-Blooded who have fought anything other than mortals or other Dragon-Blooded. They do exist, of course, there are veteran shikari who have stood in against Lunars and Fair Folk and terrible demons and other monstrosities, but most Dragon-Blooded won't have that experience. Going up against guys who just fucking break the rules in the way Solars do is going to be a new, terrifying, and potentially short-lived experience for many of them.<br /> <br /> (I can't speak for other GMs but I always try and bring a pinch of &quot;what sort of CHARACTER decisions would this guy make in a fight?&quot; to my fights. A hard-bitten professional Dragon-Blooded officer in the Legions who has had the best training available and understands how his essence relates to his vocation inside and out and has seen some crazy shit is, in my opinion, far more likely to make 'mechanically optimal' choices than a Dragon-Blooded who has spent the last hundred years being the hardest, baddest, most awesome motherfucker in his postage-stamp sized personal kingdom in the back of beyond, even if they both technically have made the same Charm picks. The former would treat a Solar much differently and perhaps more cautiously than the latter, who might be used to solving problems by simply committing in hard and trusting that when he comes out the other side, he'll still be standing and his opponent will not. Because fuck, that's always worked on everyone else in Creation, right?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T20:11:03-07:00","id":1211276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211272#post1211272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think you can discount the way that Solars have &quot;get out of jail free&quot; cards in a way that Dragon-Blooded don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are all excellent points. I also try to make my antagonists feel realistic, and not tailored to my players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T21:26:01-07:00","id":1211289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211276#post1211276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> These are all excellent points. I also try to make my antagonists feel realistic, and not tailored to my players.</div> </div> </div> </div>DrLoveMonkey, I can totally get where you are coming from by trying to make the antagonists part of a lived in world. However, I would submit that the system works better in a fashion where antagonists act as fools to character action, atleast when discussing antagonists for Solars.<br /> <br /> This to me I think makes DBs better for a more simulationist approach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T21:28:23-07:00","id":1211290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211193#post1211193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn\u2019t all five Styles used to allow the heaviest of armor? Now Air and Wood only allow light, and neither Fire or Water can go heavy.<br /> <br /> But then, \u201cmagitech Elemental Dragon Armor and Warstriders\u201d aren\u2019t meant to be the inevitable end-goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Time to make a earth style user that rides around in a warstrider wrecking things with a huge kanabo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T21:48:57-07:00","id":1211293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211193#post1211193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn\u2019t all five Styles used to allow the heaviest of armor? Now Air and Wood only allow light, and neither Fire or Water can go heavy.<br /> <br /> But then, \u201cmagitech Elemental Dragon Armor and Warstriders\u201d aren\u2019t meant to be the inevitable end-goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1e Fire Dragon Form was not compatable with armor and the others were silent, although Earth's pinnacle (Perfection of Earth Body) was not compatable with armor either. In 2e this got opened up to any armor as there were no actaul armor categories. 3e introduces more granular ones, with only Earth compatable with all kinds of armor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T22:39:07-07:00","id":1211300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OpMegs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211187#post1211187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Looking at the Immaculate styles.... I'm thinking a proper Wyld Hunt could mess one up, if we're talking a full set of 5 Sworn Kin Immaculate Shikari with the Elemental Dragon styles, mortal auxilaries (to ramp up that onslaught, especially if any of the DBs is using War to coordinate them) and some of the nastier combination options (Dragon Vortex Attack with all 5 elements involved is <i>mean</i>, and it hugely synergizes with stuff like Earth and Water Dragon styles penalizing a target for having movement or wound penalties)<br /> <br /> Which really looks into a specific mechanical thing I noted, which is how Solar penalty negators actually work. Do they count as literally a &quot;cleanse&quot;, removing the penalty for the duration? Or are they simply a counterbalance, essentially giving the Solar an equal-and-opposite buff to neutralize the penalty? The former is MUCH more painful to Immaculate Dragon Stylists than the latter, because of how Earth and Water still bypass penalty negation by the way their charms interact with how many movement or wound penalties they have. And then you have the potential for your Fire Aspect to start using Fire Dragon to literally burn away a Solar's initiative and essence to drain him faster.<br /> <br /> It's possible that the Beast could still win that kind of optimized, massed opposition? But I think it'd be far from effortless.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> In the Ask the Devs thread, Vance specifies that charms like Dipping Swallow Defense only<i> ignore</i> penalties, they don't <i>remove</i> them, so charms like Ferocious Jab still get the benefits.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1069692#post1069692\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...92#post1069692</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T00:14:25-07:00","id":1211313,"title":"","content":"<b>Social Abilities</b><br /> <br /> Right anyway before sleep tonight on to the actual proper social versus analysis that I promised to do. This should be much better thought out and easier to read than my last post.<br /> <br /> I actually typed out a huge analysis of every ability, comparing and contrasting each, but it was repetitive. The real problem is that there IS no comparing the two, they competencies in each area barely overlap, amazingly. Where they do overlap however, there is a theme. Basically the Solar version of each ability is focused on doing what the mortal version does really really well. It's broad and it's powerful. They use dice tricks, charms that discount costs, and some other tricks to influence or read multiple people at once, or forcing situations where they can apply it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Terrestrials do things very differently. In the areas where their charms overlap with the Solar competencies the Dragonblooded version tend to be both less powerful and more focused. The focus is usually on passions, inciting them, stifling them, seeking them out. It also focuses on loyalties, forming them quickly, and breaking them in others. In these places they can't be said to surpass Solars, not really, but they can do things Solars can't. Like instantly form a tie of loyalty to another DB and gain bonus diced based on that for the scene.<br /> <br /> But here's the thing, what Dragonblooded CAN do with these abilities is just awesome. Like a presence charm which lets you breathe fire in quite a powerful attack honestly is pretty powerful. DB combat charms let you fight less efficiently than a Solar but in interesting and unique ways. DB social charms do that sometimes, like being able to instantly form or strengthen an intimacy for another terrestrial when they're in danger, but at other times they apply the idea of the ability outside the context of the system. Like the performance charm that lets you hide an ambush in a performance, and the integrity charm which lets you seek vengeance without rest, food, or drink, so long as you do nothing but seek retribution.<br /> <br /> What this does that's so great is that, true, you're often relying on your excellency and maybe a few other tricks based on passionate intimacies to get by in the social system, your social DB has a much broader array of capabilities than a similarly focused Solar. For example if a super social focused Solar gets jumped in a diplomatic meeting, they're kind of relying on their bodyguards and few scant combat charms to get by. A DB who's similarly presence focused inhales deep and turns the would-be assassins to ash with a presence charm.<br /> <br /> <br /> So yeah, basically that's it for a power comparison. The DB versions, after some careful consideration, are decidedly weaker, except in a few key areas, like it's very difficult to get a properpy focused terrestrial to betray their sworn kinship, for example. In those areas they might almost be a match for Solars, but they lag far far behind in other areas, often having only their excellency to work with. If you're going up against a Solar in the social game, you're going to need to leverage passions and loyalties to even have a shot, and even then prepare to have this escalate into a fight as they try and wrestle away your granite hard intimacies and you get frustrated trying to pierce their defenses. Lucky for you, your presence charm includes adding health levels and soak and his doesn't.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I might do a comparison on the rest of the non-combat stuff like Athletics and Craft if anyone wants to see it. Those systems are a lot more crunchy and leave less up to the ST so you can expect a bit more clear cut contrasts. I've got some stuff to say about Craft and Athletics for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 04-25-2018, 03:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T01:10:59-07:00","id":1211318,"title":"","content":"A couple of thoughts.<ul><li>The whiteroom Solar is the boogieman for everyone. Some builds of &quot;The Beast&quot; are capable of inflicting multiple casualties on a circle of Solars or at the very least make everyone who wasn't playing a Dawn feel like they were being actively punished.</li> <li>Since I'm once again seeing people who appear to be having issues with this. The easiest way to challenge Solars (Exalts in general really) is to distribute action across multiple scenes. Look at how movies handle fight scenes, they don't just ram everyone in together and hope for the best.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T06:41:18-07:00","id":1211391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211318#post1211318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A couple of thoughts.<ul><li>The whiteroom Solar is the boogieman for everyone. Some builds of &amp;quot;The Beast&amp;quot; are capable of inflicting multiple casualties on a circle of Solars or at the very least make everyone who wasn't playing a Dawn feel like they were being actively punished.</li> <li>Since I'm once again seeing people who appear to be having issues with this. The easiest way to challenge Solars (Exalts in general really) is to distribute action across multiple scenes. Look at how movies handle fight scenes, they don't just ram everyone in together and hope for the best.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>As to your first point I\u2019m with you 100%. We actually developed a saying among my ex3 group \u201ceven Solars can\u2019t beat Solars.\u201d We once had a PC Dawn use an antagonist\u2019s own Superbad resistance against her to build up 65 initiative in a single action, and then unleashed it in an AoE that annihilated every one of our enemies. It was kind of awesome the first time but she was a recurring villain and we had to implement a house rule to stop him from doing that every time she showed up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The second point for me is difficult. If you\u2019ve got a party of 5 Solars the fights that lead up to the climactic battle need to be at least challenging enough to make them spend more than they respire. They need to keep getting harder too or else subsequent action scenes will just be opportunities to regen motes.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve both used and been in parties where the ST used this to great effect, but only in Armageddon scenarios. Like once my ST had us fight a horse of billions of chitin monsters, wave after wave. Another time I used it when my PCs were storming a Satrap\u2019s palace during a demon invasion, where they fought a couple of battle groups lead by demon commanders with huge brass siege golems as support in two different scenes before the final encounter. That was awesome.<br /> <br /> But I wrestle with them storming a non-demonic satraps palace. How many DBs could there possible be in it? Not even ten right? Even eight or nine is a lot. I dunno. This is probably just a power scope thing I\u2019m getting wrong somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T07:14:00-07:00","id":1211397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211391#post1211391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like once my ST had us fight a horse of billions of chitin monsters, wave after wave.</div> </div> </div> </div>Best idea for a Primordial I've seen in ages. Multitudinous chitin monster horse is my new jam.<br /> <br /> I bet the Solars would find a way to tame and ride it, tho.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T07:17:55-07:00","id":1211399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211397#post1211397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Best idea for a Primordial I've seen in ages. Multitudinous chitin monster horse is my new jam.<br /> <br /> I bet the Solars would find a way to tame and ride it, tho.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed we did. It was basically the immune system of an ncient and lobotomized primordial being. So we basically ended up grabbing some and riding along their gateway to the things prison dimension and setting off one of those soul destroying bombs.<br /> <br /> <br /> I hope nobody gets the impression that I hate Solars because of how hard it is to work with them. I think they\u2019re awesome, just frustrating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T08:59:13-07:00","id":1211440,"title":"","content":"I think Murcushio was playing on what was probably a misstype of &quot;horde&quot; and &quot;horse&quot;. But I just might be the one who got it wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T09:21:23-07:00","id":1211445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211440#post1211440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Murcushio was playing on what was probably a misstype of &quot;horde&quot; and &quot;horse&quot;. But I just might be the one who got it wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>...I got like 3 hours of sleep last night so, uh...basically... !!!SMOKE-BOMB!!!<br /> <br /> On second thought I stand by it, that would be an awesome enemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 04-25-2018, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T10:57:32-07:00","id":1211468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211240#post1211240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take, for example Thunderbolt Attack Prana. An athletics charm actually! Which costs 4m 1wp, supplemental, can be comboed with any other ability, allows the user to jump a range band in any direction and DOUBLES damage after it is rolled. This alone means that a Solar can be deadly at as little as 8 initiative.<br /> <br /> Now lets see what we can combo this with. I like the look of Invincible Fury of the Dawn there. For 5m 1wp that lets me make up to 5 attacks, distributed how I please, move a range band between each attack, and instantly gain initiative equal to the number of attacks I want to make. Also, apart from the excellency, and charm I use on one attack can be used for free on the others. It can also be activated reflexively after using Peony Blossom Technique.<br /> <br /> So since all the stuff is free past the first I might as well load up, Excellent Strike (3m) rerolls 1s until they fail to appear, neutralizing a common DB trick to boost their defense in the process, and Hungry Tiger (3m 2i), which lets our overflow attack successes add to the damage.<br /> <br /> Plus, of course, Rising Sun Slash, which activates on a straight 7,8,9,10 being rolled and gives me one bonus non-charm sux and (essence) non-charm dice on the attack roll.<br /> <br /> OKAY so we're ready to make our attack. With as little as 10 initiative, lets see what we can do. We'll make 5 attacks, instantly giving us 5 initiative. That's 5 attacks with 3 base damage, then we attack. First we use Perfect Strike Discipline to give our first attack a full free excellency, between that and a level 2 stunt we're basically rocking 25 dice to attack, plus rerolling 1s, plus a big non-charm bonus with Rising Sun Slash, which is surprisingly common at those dice levels. Against a typical DB Defense of, say, 10, they've got no hope. Simplified calculations give us around 16 successes. That overflows by 6 so we get to deal 9 damage, which is then doubled thanks to TAP, giving us around 7.2 health levels, which is lethal against somebody without ox-bodies. If we drop our first target, great, if not, hit them again. When they drop we then reset Perfect Strike Discipline, for another free full excellency, and can jump a range band if we have to in order to strike our next target, and so on.<br /> <br /> If we have just one target the onslaught penalty keeps racking up so that's good too.<br /> <br /> And if we have a charm called Foe-Cleaving Focus we actually regenerate a mote for every 10 on an attack that triggers Rising Sun Slash. Which is good because that took like, at least 20-25 motes and 3-4 willpower.<br /> <br /> <br /> People are going to point out that wearing artifact full plate would use hardness to defend decently against that, but this was just an example to show how Solar charms work, I don't want to proc a mechanics arms race to infinite xp.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A few things worth noting:<br /> <br /> TAP doubles damage after it is rolled. This means it is <i>very </i>vulnerable to below-average roll results. &quot;A Solar can be deadly at 8 initiative&quot; is, therefore, a bit of a misleading statement - there is a more than 10% chance that the attack will deal 0 or 2 damage, and a more than 20% chance that it will only deal 4 damage (inflicting a mere -1 wound penalty on a character with even a single Ox-Body purchase). Over five attacks, your chance of getting no abnormally low result is roughly 0.7^5 - slightly less than 17%. And you're paying a point of Willpower for the privilege every time. Which you also need to fuel your Perfect Strike Discipline.<br /> <br /> Moreover, Hungry Tiger Technique can only be used on crashed targets, which most characters you're alpha striking are definitely not going to be. (Granted, if you're wielding Stormcaller, this requirement can be waived... if you manage to get your storm's Intensity up to 6. Good luck doing that over the course of a single round.) This means you're going to have to use Fire and Stones Strike instead, for a much more reasonable (Essence or 3, which, let's not kid ourselves, is going to work out to 3 in the overwhelming majority of cases) extra damage per attack.<br /> <br /> Out of curiosity, let's calculate the probability of missing a maxed attack against a fully specialized Dragon-Blooded defense! You've got 11 dice as a base, +2 stunt, +8 excellency to round it out, so you're rolling 21 dice plus an auto-success against a defense of 6 +3 excellency +1 stunt +1 willpower (after all, if he's going to die anyway, he may as well spend that point, not like he's gonna use it after). Anydice tells me that after taking Excellent Strike into account, this pool has a 74.91% chance to hit a defense of 11, which is far from guaranteed - but also ignores Rising Sun Slash. Sadly, while I can easily calculate the probability of successfully proccing RSS on a 21 dice roll, going through the hassle of determining the likelihood of successfully proccing it on a roll that would've missed otherwise, but managed to hit because of it is not really worth my time.<br /> <br /> <br /> All things considered, no matter how awesomely kitted out a Dawn might be, I'd always put my money on a team of five E3 shikari in decent artifact gear and a reasonable number of Ox-Body purchases, just by virtue of the massive collective mote pool and action economy advantage. Even if the Dawn manages to doomcombo one or two right out of the gate, he'll tire himself out in the process, and the other side has +10 motes per turn to spend and three times the chance of landing a hit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":".  herp derp, I forgot to actually take the Excellent Strike autosuccess into account 04-25-2018, 02:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T11:16:46-07:00","id":1211474,"title":"","content":"Awesome math <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3443_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3443\" data-vbnamecard=\"3443\">aluminiumtrioxid</a> !<br /> <br /> Yeah in the case of a 5v1 the Solar has to be really really built and definitely high essence if they want a hope of winning. If you can take out three right off the hop your defences and things like counter attack can help you win against the remaining two, but you need a big mote pool to do it for sure. Also unlike previous editions a bad roll, especially on the join battle, can all but ensure a loss on your side.<br /> <br /> Ox- bodies also really help, the more you give each character the more it skews to the DBs favour! Which is a great point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T11:27:20-07:00","id":1211477,"title":"","content":"Also, doesn't TAP require you be able to move, so wouldn't it only work on the first attack?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T11:31:37-07:00","id":1211479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211313#post1211313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might do a comparison on the rest of the non-combat stuff like Athletics and Craft if anyone wants to see it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like to see it, if you ever feel like writing it up. This topic has been interesting so far, and I haven't been in many games, so I feel like your posts have helped me understand how the game works in play and what players might be capable of.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We once had a PC Dawn use an antagonist\u2019s own Superbad resistance against her to build up 65 initiative in a single action, and then unleashed it in an AoE that annihilated every one of our enemies. It was kind of awesome the first time but she was a recurring villain and we had to implement a house rule to stop him from doing that every time she showed up. </div> </div> </div>That's impressively ridiculous. How did he manage that? I've seen Solar combos for outputting tons of decisive damage, but I didn't know it was possible to get that much initiative in a single tick against any opponent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/157-phoenix_kensai","name":"Phoenix_Kensai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar157_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T11:47:24-07:00","id":1211489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211477#post1211477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, doesn't TAP require you be able to move, so wouldn't it only work on the first attack?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Funnily enough, going by a strict reading, the answer to that question is &quot;yes, <i>except </i>if your opponents are in the air at less than short range&quot;. I originally wanted to make that point, but the &quot;if the Exalt uses this Charm to move to another range band, it counts as her movement action for the round&quot; clause tripped me up - I thought &quot;so if the character uses Invincible Fury of the Dawn's movement clause to propel herself towards her foes, she doesn't move with TAP, therefore her move action isn't used up&quot;. However, I forgot that it specifically says &quot;aerial targets up to short range, or ground targets at another range band&quot;, which means you can't use TAP after moving into close range with movement granted by IFoD.<br /> <br /> So, going by strict RAW, you can only use TAP once per round unless you have access to powers that grant you extra movement actions (such as One Extra Step in Solar Athletics) <i>or </i>you're attacking aerial targets who are less than a range band away from you (in which case, you can still activate the Charm due to the &quot;up to&quot; clause, and you're not using up your movement action because you're not moving to another range band).<br /> <br /> This is weird and slightly funny emergent behavior, but I think it's legit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T12:05:51-07:00","id":1211494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211477#post1211477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, doesn't TAP require you be able to move, so wouldn't it only work on the first attack?</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoa really? I\u2019ve never seen anyone mention that before, and we\u2019ve used it a ton for various characters. I thought I\u2019ve read it over very carefully before but I must have somehow parsed it wrong every time. <br /> <br /> I hope I haven\u2019t abused it in an unintended way before. Once I combined it with the pinnacle crane style charm for quadrupole damage, but if I recall I had already closed to close range. Damn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T12:17:55-07:00","id":1211499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211494#post1211494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whoa really? I\u2019ve never seen anyone mention that before, and we\u2019ve used it a ton for various characters. I thought I\u2019ve read it over very carefully before but I must have somehow parsed it wrong every time.<br /> <br /> I hope I haven\u2019t abused it in an unintended way before. Once I combined it with the pinnacle crane style charm for quadrupole damage, but if I recall I had already closed to close range. Damn.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'v heard anecdotally it wasn't originally in the playtest, but the wording was changed specifically due to it being abused.<br /> <br /> Depending on how you read some of the &quot;can&quot; and &quot;If&quot; statements it can go either way, especially since there are two use cases, vertical and horizontal.<br /> <br /> The gist of it was the &quot;leap&quot;part isn't just fluff, and you aren't shoryukenning into someone's face.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1072717#post1072717\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...17#post1072717</a><br /> <br /> edit: I'm not sure how I feel about using it to juggle in the air. It seems okay with RAW, but I find the RAI dubious, and see it going either way between Rule of Cool and Chicanery-No.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":1542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","user":"MoroseMorgan","date":". 04-25-2018, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T12:41:49-07:00","id":1211509,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the more I look at it, the more I think the balance between Dragon-Blooded and Solars is spot on as long as there is just kinda an understanding in the setting that The Beast is an extreme exception and that balanced Dawns are the rule. If that is the case, the setting works because The Beasts exist as the kind of character to be beaten with huge military actions, plot device evocations, and extreme tactical chicanery. The kind of thing that goes on to be legend and tragedy for the Wyld Hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T12:49:02-07:00","id":1211513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steamfunk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211509#post1211509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, the more I look at it, the more I think the balance between Dragon-Blooded and Solars is spot on as long as there is just kinda an understanding in the setting that The Beast is an extreme exception and that balanced Dawns are the rule. If that is the case, the setting works because The Beasts exist as the kind of character to be beaten with huge military actions, plot device evocations, and extreme tactical chicanery. The kind of thing that goes on to be legend and tragedy for the Wyld Hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I think you\u2019re correct. As long as your ST isn\u2019t building ever Solar to be the greatest combat monster they can, and as long as your PCs aren\u2019t either, it looks pretty good.<br /> <br /> When I did that huge whole combat analysis it was with the idea that no single DB SHOULD have a good chance of beating a dawn cast. The exception being very high essence DBs, which have two advantages. The higher mote pools mean that if the Solar can\u2019t take them out quickly they\u2019ll run out of gas, and the decisive attack tricks they\u2019ve got are devastating enough that with a lucky strike they can end the fight almost as easily as the dawn can. Which is SCARY considering how few things in the whole game can do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T13:01:58-07:00","id":1211516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211513#post1211513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah I think you\u2019re correct. As long as your ST isn\u2019t building ever Solar to be the greatest combat monster they can, and as long as your PCs aren\u2019t either, it looks pretty good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to put in my $0.02, in my experience most Dawn Castes I run into in Ex3 are something in between the Beast and the Well-Rounded Fighter. A little less monomaniacal than the former, but not spread as broadly as the latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Won't you believe in him? Even if there is no God, or Buddha...there is still Kamen Rider.&quot; \u2014Taki Kazuya, <i>Kamen Rider SPIRITS</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Now...count up </span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">all your sins.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","name":"CycloneJoker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T13:19:27-07:00","id":1211529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CycloneJoker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211516#post1211516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just to put in my $0.02, in my experience most Dawn Castes I run into in Ex3 are something in between the Beast and the Well-Rounded Fighter. A little less monomaniacal than the former, but not spread as broadly as the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even something as simple as wearing light mundane armor instead of heavy artifact armor makes a massive difference, especially against enemies like dragonblooded who don\u2019t have a ton of withering damage boosters. In mundane light even with The Beast charm setup your chances fall drastically. The lack of hardness would also mean that the dragonblooded animas alone are a dire threat, particularly in the dogpile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T13:20:42-07:00","id":1211530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steamfunk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211509#post1211509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, the more I look at it, the more I think the balance between Dragon-Blooded and Solars is spot on as long as there is just kinda an understanding in the setting that The Beast is an extreme exception and that balanced Dawns are the rule. If that is the case, the setting works because The Beasts exist as the kind of character to be beaten with huge military actions, plot device evocations, and extreme tactical chicanery. The kind of thing that goes on to be legend and tragedy for the Wyld Hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Tbh I think The Beast is the <i>least </i>dangerous thing a Solar can be. You can divert them, outmaneuver them, find out what they want and exploit that knowledge to make them be disruptive somewhere else. Someone utterly dedicated to and solely motivated by martial excellence is very easy to deal with, as long as you have something to point them at. Get someone to seduce them so they settle down and live in marital bliss for a few centuries. Play on their desire to prove themselves as the greatest warrior who ever lived and let them know about invincible behemoths that lurk in the forgotten corners of the world. You don't have to best them at <i>literally the only one thing </i>they're good at.<br /> <br /> (Of course, characters with well-developed secondary competencies can just be jumped after they've spent themselves working on a challenge related to one of those competencies. Really, as long as you know who they are and how to find them, it's not terribly difficult to deal with Anathema, assuming you can keep your mouth shut and resist the urge to let the whole world know that you're the Wyld Hunt.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T19:48:57-07:00","id":1211657,"title":"","content":"Sort of a minor nitpick, and really have enjoyed reading this thread, but with root and hand merging Terrestrial Parry caps out at 13-15 (6 base+3 from charms +1 from Weapon + 1 from stunts + 1 from root and hand+ 1 from Willpower+2 full defense) If there are two of them and they have Sheilds they can defend other and counterattack once they have a solid initiative lead and counterattack/distract to leverage the benefit of a defend other/full defense flurry without sacrificing the ability to attack the solar. Two on one, or three on one even, at roughly even levels of experience, terrestrials can be pretty nightmarish it seems to me\u2014 as long as the solar\u2019s initial join battle roll isn\u2019t enough for him to kill them in the first two-three rounds. And that\u2019s just white room, Melee to Melee. <br /> <br /> That said I generally agree with the breakdown presented here and think you have made some really insightful points DrLoveMonkey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T20:11:49-07:00","id":1211669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211530#post1211530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, as long as you know who they are and how to find them, it's not terribly difficult to deal with Anathema, assuming you can keep your mouth shut and resist the urge to let the whole world know that you're the Wyld Hunt.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There goes my idea of playing a character that is such a Realm fanatic that they get a tattoo of the Empress's face on top of their own face.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T21:46:47-07:00","id":1211688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phoenix_Kensai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211479#post1211479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's impressively ridiculous. How did he manage that? I've seen Solar combos for outputting tons of decisive damage, but I didn't know it was possible to get that much initiative in a single tick against any opponent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically a Solar resistance combo that seriously reduces post soak damage with Aegis of Invincible Might, and an archery charm that lets you shoot attacks until you miss or crash your target. Without an onslaught negator her defense was 0 pretty quick and he just kept racking up initiative from successful attacks rather than damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phoenix_Kensai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211479#post1211479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to see it, if you ever feel like writing it up. This topic has been interesting so far, and I haven't been in many games, so I feel like your posts have helped me understand how the game works in play and what players might be capable of.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, lemme flip the script. How about I just go through each ability, give a little description on the themes, the coolest things you can do with each, and contrast a bit with the Solar version, and why you might want to play them.. Let's do this and get to sleep at a reasonable time.<br /> <br /> <b>Archery</b><br /> <br /> A theme that pervades this charmset is a reminder that the wood in your bow and arrows was once alive and can be again. Your bow can become a tree for you to have cover behind, turning any plant into arrows, and having arrows explode into grasping vines. Speaking of Life Swelling Sap Strike, that's something else that comes up a fair bit in this tree, special shots. Where a Solar has like 1 or 2 of these that supplement attacks the Dragonblooded ones instead form the base for an entirely new action. Oftentimes totally modifying the purpose of a shot into a social counterattack that deals physical damage, or an arrow that ignites and explodes into a fireball on impact.<br /> <br /> Another theme present is the military sniper style guardian angel. They can snipe incoming archery attacks out of the air, both protecting her allies and even punishing the attacker. Awesome teamwork.<br /> <br /> From a mechanical point of view they differ from Solars in another way, and that's aiming. The Solar charmset has a lot of ways to enhance aim speed, or attack without aiming at all. Dragonblooded on the other hand are the exact opposite, a lot of the special moves require aiming, with the only way to shorten it being a signature charm that locks you out of all the other signatures.<br /> <br /> Overall, very exciting and fun!<br /> <br /> <b>Athletics</b><br /> <br /> What does athletics do? It lets you run fast, lift things, swim, jump, all that stuff. The Solar charmset is really focused hard on just increasing the scope of those abilities. You run faster and faster, can leap multiple range bands, and eventually just ignore the strength requirements for lifting literally anything, deal damage.<br /> <br /> Dragonblooded get to do much the same, just not quite half as good and often with elemental restrictions, like needing to stand on the ground. On the other hand they can straight up fly. The closest Solar analogue requires a combat target and doesn't let you do anything except fly to it and stick to it, you can't even change targets until you touch the ground again. So yeah, here we've actually got a charm for the Terrestrials which is (kind of) in theme with an ability that's a more powerful effect than the Solar version.<br /> <br /> There's one other theme present here, burning the crap out of people. There are no less than four charms that set your opponent on fire when you run toward/past them. The teamwork charm here is the climbing one, it lets you carve handholds for your self with the option to leave them for your allies.<br /> <br /> Very unique, even more mobile than Solars and totally destructive to enemies and environments.<br /> <br /> <b>Awareness</b><br /> <br /> Solars again, super straight forward. They can see the beating of a fly's wings on the horizon and feel the vibration of a spider crawling on the roof.<br /> <br /> Dragonblooded this time around are very different. Instead of boosting their senses in general they're good at picking out specific things only, namely threats. People who mean to do her harm, disguised people, poisons, specific chosen sounds. There's also an interesting mechanic of moving your point of perspective, either letting your senses ride along with somebody else, or allowing you to send them anywhere along a body of water that you're touching.<br /> <br /> Of course, it also lets you kick ass. Both by disabling enemy's senses, and eventually destroying their motes of essence.<br /> <br /> Very evocative of an intrigue laden game, where the most important thing you need to see is an assassin.<br /> <br /> <b>Brawl</b><br /> <br /> Back to combat with Brawl, Solar brawl is full of powerful and kinetic attacks, onslaught penalties, and crushing grapples. Stuff like Heaven Thunder Hammer flinging enemies around, to going super Saiyan and firing a Kamehameha wave.<br /> <br /> The Dragonblooded ones have the crushing grapples and onslaught too, just way less powerful. What they lack in power though they make up by allowing you to use elements to make grapples and attacks at range, before Solars get the Kamehameha and easier to activate even. It's also got a thing for dragging your enemies all over the place.<br /> <br /> Teamwork plays a big role in this tree, enhancing distract gambits and doing such devastating things as setting your target's hardness to zero. With a full circle of allies around that means that your foe is taking a lot of damage from the animas and can just keep getting hit with lethal damage until the thousand cuts disintegrate him.<br /> <br /> Very much like the Solar version in mechanical theme, but loving the cooperation opportunities.<br /> <br /> <b>Bureaucracy</b><br /> <br /> Solar bureaucracy is a really varied and broad tree. It gives bonuses all over to social transactions, protecting your organization, and, of course, boosting project actions.<br /> <br /> Terrestrial bureaucracy is cool because rather than assume you're the head of a big organization, it has a lot of stuff that seems to imply that you work within a larger organization. Stuff like finding factions and gauging votes. It's also got something else too, resources. With a few different charms you can seem more wealthy, get access to allies, contacts, retainers ect. You can also leverage your wealth directly with charms.<br /> <br /> The teamwork here is actually in partnering with an allied general, your projects give them sweet strategic bonuses. It's also got a really sweet charm that lets you flash a blank piece of paper and force people to see it as official documentation and/or a badge of your authority.<br /> <br /> Pretty straightforward and definitely applicable to high civilization games that DBs will be involved in most.<br /> <br /> <br /> And I think I'll leave that for now, I need to get sleep tonight. I'm really enjoying this though! Most of the charm trees so far have personality, very distinct from Solars. It's actually making Solars more cool as well, before they just kind of did stuff super well with no comparison. Now that we have one the ability to do things like lift a house is actually novel, since it's something that's beyond the other exalted (so far). At the same time though I can definitely see a Solar player getting just a bit jealous of the DB in his party who gets to use his brawl charms to fight enemies in a courtyard while he coolly struts along the ramparts.<br /> <br /> <br /> More tomorrow!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 04-26-2018, 12:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T21:54:29-07:00","id":1211689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211657#post1211657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sort of a minor nitpick, and really have enjoyed reading this thread, but with root and hand merging Terrestrial Parry caps out at 13-15 (6 base+3 from charms +1 from Weapon + 1 from stunts + 1 from root and hand+ 1 from Willpower+2 full defense) If there are two of them and they have Sheilds they can defend other and counterattack once they have a solid initiative lead and counterattack/distract to leverage the benefit of a defend other/full defense flurry without sacrificing the ability to attack the solar. Two on one, or three on one even, at roughly even levels of experience, terrestrials can be pretty nightmarish it seems to me\u2014 as long as the solar\u2019s initial join battle roll isn\u2019t enough for him to kill them in the first two-three rounds. And that\u2019s just white room, Melee to Melee.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I didn't think of that, you're right that's nasty. I definitely feel like, even for a reasonably powerful Dawn, if he doesn't have his circle backing him up he's going to feel that &quot;Awww...fuck.&quot; sensation at fighting multiple dragonblooded, especially as I read through their charms and see the teamwork there. Imagine your setup with trading around initiatives and distracts if the water aspect can get a hold of him and disable his hardness. I can only imagine more inter-player combos will arise as I go through it, almost like how Solars can combo with themselves. It's not a death sentence like fighting two or three other Dawns would be, but he will not enjoy the experience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211657#post1211657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said I generally agree with the breakdown presented here and think you have made some really insightful points DrLoveMonkey.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am honoured by your praise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T01:08:54-07:00","id":1211715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211688#post1211688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Basically a Solar resistance combo that seriously reduces post soak damage with Aegis of Invincible Might, and an archery charm that lets you shoot attacks until you miss or crash your target. Without an onslaught negator her defense was 0 pretty quick and he just kept racking up initiative from successful attacks rather than damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Oh, right, I forgot about Revolving Bow Discipline. That Charm definitely needs some sort of cap on it.<br /> <br /> And thanks for continuing your anaylsis. It's interesting to see your overviews of the Charm sets and their differences.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/157-phoenix_kensai","name":"Phoenix_Kensai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar157_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T02:13:40-07:00","id":1211719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211530#post1211530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tbh I think The Beast is the <i>least </i>dangerous thing a Solar can be.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dawn I was playing in the second part of the playtest would have a good shot at mopping the floor with the Beast because her build punished over-focus on combat. Essentially she has Respect-Commanding Attitude and Battle-Dancer Method coupled with a healthy investment in dodge charms because she's a former slave turned freedom fighter. It wasn't great in group fights because it meant she wasn't fulfilling the tank role people could go &quot;You know what, fine! I'll hit your friends instead!&quot; and she fought bare knuckle so this would be a long ass fight.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, I adore the mental image of her engaging a bigger and better equipped enemy like a matador does a bull and making them look like a fool.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T04:56:14-07:00","id":1211742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211689#post1211689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I am honoured by your praise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure if that was sarcasm resulting from my comment coming across as patronizing but I didn\u2019t intend it as anything but sincere. Hope that\u2019s how it was received.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T05:14:01-07:00","id":1211747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211391#post1211391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The second point for me is difficult. If you\u2019ve got a party of 5 Solars the fights that lead up to the climactic battle need to be at least challenging enough to make them spend more than they respire. They need to keep getting harder too or else subsequent action scenes will just be opportunities to regen motes.</div> </div> </div> </div>My biggest success so far is presenting fights where &quot;mashing the enemy into pulp&quot; is not the only goal (or sometimes not even a primary goal). Spreading the focus gives the the nondawns more space to align themselves as part of the fight and gives the players more considerations to make, which can dramatically increase the tension of the scene.<br /> <br /> Even the most straight up dungeon crawl fight scenario i've seen in play, wyld shaping encounter rolls, there is an element that adds a LOT of tension to the fight: Waves. Those encounter rolls go bad real fast, and you will likely pit yourself against several if you're doing more than just dispelling the chaos. How do you fight a raksha hunting party and stay efficient in case you fight some hannya? And then are you risking low essence or a couple hits, knowing a behemoth can spring from anywhere?<br /> <br /> Battle Groups are really, really good to play up the wearing effect of wave encounters too. You don't gain initiative from them past the ping and crash rewards, Their soak tends to be high and decisives put you at risk despite being extra powerful against them. Add a commander and a couple heroes and you have to burn <i>hard</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 04-26-2018, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T05:16:44-07:00","id":1211748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211742#post1211742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if that was sarcasm resulting from my comment coming across as patronizing but I didn\u2019t intend it as anything but sincere. Hope that\u2019s how it was received.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah totally, I was just being all...Lookshy about how I was receiving it. If this was a Sidereal thread I probably would have said something about, I dunno, i have filed the necessary paperwork to properly receive compliment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T06:09:12-07:00","id":1211761,"title":"","content":"I think it should definitely be remembered that the default assumption for fighting DBs is 'there's more than one of them'. Dragonblooded are never at their best alone, and they know it. Coming together to make something greater than the sum of their individual actions is kind of a theme for them in a way it really isn't for Solars.<br /> <br /> e: and being a more rounded, non-combat-focused build takes away their combat ability less, as most of their abilities involve some method of dipping into combat, so you can't as easily discount the nerds and socialites as major problems in a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T01:00:14-07:00","id":1212559,"title":"","content":"Had to take a break yesterday to actually sleep, time to make up for it today though.<br /> <br /> <b>Craft</b><br /> <br /> The 3rd edition craft system has a lot of knobs and Solars have a fist wrapped around each one. I think the Solar charm tree is nearly 50 charms or something. Slots, craft points, terminus, they've got a few charms for each. They shuffle around points, negate the need for tools and do things way faster. They've also got some ones that just take the system beyond and do things like let you retroactively and instantly finish a hidden project.<br /> <br /> The Dragonblooded don't have half as many charms, although a few common themes are still there. They can negate the need for tools when crafting within an element, they can speed it up as well. The other charms that interact with the actual system are straightforward, but powerful. Stuff like giving a discount on how many points you need to finish a project, and a gambling system to try and get more points.<br /> <br /> The thing that they seem to focus on here is repairing and breaking. They can actually add up to, I think 4 dots of strength for Feats of Strength that involve demolition, or 1 for repairs, and any excess strength that they have gets added as a non charm bonus. They can also speed Feats of Strength demolitions, using their craft speed enhancer. So they break things good and can be really strong when their craft is on the line. It gives me the image of a terrestrial planting her feet on the ground and with great heaving effort raising a roof on a building by herself, just hand over hand on the pully system.<br /> <br /> This one I was very worried about but it turned out better than I expected. A lot fewer things to keep track of than the Solar version, which is good for an already complex system like craft. It's also got a whole lot of cool effects like the strength boosters that guide your character to epic actions, rather than just epic dicerolls. Nice.<br /> <br /> <b>Dodge</b><br /> <br /> Solar dodge is one of the best defenses in the game, and it's full of tricks. Things that manipulate initiative, things that give you motes, burst your dice cap. It's strong in a lot of different ways with a lot of answers to any threat, including a true perfect defense.<br /> <br /> Dragonblooded dodge seems way more aggressive by comparison. There's 3-4 counter attacks of some fashion or another in the set. It definitely feels like DB dodge is all about punishing your foe for attacking you.<br /> <br /> My favourite combo also made it over from the past edition. There's a teamwork charm that lets you leap in front of an attack, reflexively using evasion as a defend other. There's another charm that lets you dodge an attack and then redirect it to another one of your enemies. Put that together and when an Abyssal anathema swings his Grand Daiklave at your hearthmate you streak over to them, catch the blade, push it around your sister and then send it spinning into the zombie horde like a blender. That abyssal just blew all his initiative and motes on a decisive attack that wiped his own army.<br /> <br /> So yeah, that's all you need to know, you can do that with Terrestrial dodge. Tree done.<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity</b><br /> <br /> Solar integrity is kind of an odd duck. It accomplishes the theme of &quot;Being amazing with integrity&quot; in the sense of social system power pretty quickly and then branches out into things that just broaden the the idea of protecting your character from change.<br /> <br /> After the DB one is done protecting your intimacies it gets busy, uh, protecting your intimacies. Okay let me explain better. When somebody tries to convince you to betray your hearth, DB integrity is there to make sure your intimacies on your sheet stay safe. When an anathema comes for your hearthmates, DB integrity is there to help you protect the things you care about physically. That's what's happening with charms like Immolating Phoenix Soul, which allows you to respond to a persuade attempt to make you betray your allies by going berzerk. And when you fail to protect your family? Unflagging Vengeance will make sure you don't have to stop for anything on your road to revenge.<br /> <br /> Terms of enrampagement indeed. I touched on it a bit what it can do before so I'll leave that there.<br /> <br /> <b>Investigation</b><br /> <br /> The Solar one here doesn't differ all that much from the DB one. It allows you to more easily case scenes and profile people, they just do it in slightly different ways. The DB one maybe focuses on emotional attachment to the act, possibly.<br /> <br /> Some cool things that DB investigation can do though are give yourself basically an eclipse protection if you're invited into a building by somebody who has the authority to do that. There's a cool power where you can tell who's a stranger in a town and if they're not where they live. A lot of little tricks like that which don't technically boost case-scene rolls but are generally really useful. They also get this really cool ability to lock onto an arch-nemesis and gain a suite of permanent powers that help them in their cat and mouse game, and stopping them from being deterred.<br /> <br /> Overall some cool distinct effects and otherwise somewhat similar to the solar one, which isn't really bad.<br /> <br /> <b>Larceny</b><br /> <br /> On to larceny! It too is similar in the themes, probably because these last two abilities are more about becoming a character archetype than adding a specific skill. They can both retroactively see a crime scene, pickpocket, pick locks, ect. Of course every time I say that the DB version is similar, it usually comes with some restrictions, which can be fun. Like the anti-pickpocket charm for DBs which pierces the palm of the would-be thief with an essence thorn.<br /> <br /> It gets a few cool and unique things though. Like the ability to submerge an item into stone, a social attack to encourage more people to break the law, it's also got a few ways to disarm opponents. It also seems to have a lot more of a focus on specifically fouling up crime scenes and messing with investigators, whereas the Solar one...well it's got that too but there's just so many other charms that do other things.<br /> <br /> <b>Linguistics</b><br /> <br /> Okay now HERE'S one that I can't say resembles the solar one very much. Solars have the market cornered here with language learning charms, and written and spoken social attacks.<br /> <br /> The DB one's got half that, with a focus again on passions, and half Seal Team Kicks. It has charms for discreet information gathering, communicating instantly over long distances, communicating silently with your allies, and disguising missives. The capstone makes you and your allies fight as though they had one mind and will, seeing through eachother's eyes and defending eachother. That charm also gives double 7s..DOUBLE 7S...on a distract gambit's attack roll. My god this has the potential to make a group of terrestrials so scary.<br /> <br /> Overall this is good. It has absolutely enough support for characters who just want to be great calligraphy artists and writers, and apart from that they're so useful to have as support on a mission they're borderline required.<br /> <br /> <b>Lore</b><br /> <br /> Yeah, lore. Solar lore has a ton of charms for training, introducing facts, discovering facts, manipulating essence and forging the wyld into a design by force of your very will.<br /> <br /> The Dragonblooded version is a really cool foil for it. It technically has a lot of what's above, but it does it in such a different way. Where Solars do things in a kind of secular way, it almost seems like lore for DBs is a religious experience. There's a certain reverence of knowledge, and linking it to the elements. Not only can DBs manipulate and transfer essence, but aura as well, and there's this big running theme that the lore master of the group is guiding and bolstering his allies. You don't have to take it this way, but a monk with a lot of lore is PERFECT.<br /> <br /> Mechanically there's a lot of playing around with specialties and, of course, elemental manipulation for attacks. Bolt, Burst, Dragon Vortex, it's every Avatar's dream. Dragon Vortex alone deserves it's own paragraph. It's essence 5, but it lets you combine your powers with your ally's and become the ultimate embodiment of elemental fury. It's the kind of thing that can end an army or a city if used right.<br /> <br /> I'm quite impressed here with Lore, I never would have themed it like this myself and I'm so glad they did.<br /> <br /> <b>Medicine</b><br /> <br /> Thumbs up on Solar medicine, I've used it on many characters myself and have rarely been disappointed. Reattach limbs, treat disease, poison, damaged health levels.<br /> <br /> The first thing you might notice about DB medicine is that it's not just about healing, it's about hurting. Using medical knowledge and essence to poison, numb, and infect your enemies. It's also got a great charm to treat mental illness, which, as Isator pointed out in his thread, his magical and useful, without making mental illness seem like a simple disease to be killed. You've also got an awesome charm for fixing crippling injuries, if your patient wants to their injury can be repaired by plant matter. This ranges anywhere from a bark patterned scar to basically a prosthetic grass arm.<br /> <br /> I'm now picturing a formerly blind character with brilliant eyes that change colour with the seasons to match blossoming lilac flowers in the spring, brilliant leafy green in the summer, fiery reds and golds in autumn and deep brown bark in the winter.<br /> <br /> That actually runs into a theme with medicine as a whole. Unlike with Solars, who tend to boost their own ability and use that to heal their patients, Dragonblooded just heal them by magic. This actually has a mechanical benefit even, the first couple wound restoring charms in both trees actually favour the DB for speed! Imagine that. You don't help them get better, you MAKE them get better, and now damnit.<br /> <br /> It's got all the base competencies, and a lot of flavour besides, and how can anyone complain about having a charm which is in some ways more powerful than the Solar version?<br /> <br /> <b>Melee</b><br /> <br /> We've talked enough about Solar melee.<br /> <br /> Dragonblooded melee however, that needs more words. Starting with it's banishing to elsewhere charms, they let you pull a weapon out of the same element you stored it in, as though all fire in the world is spiritually the same to the Terrestrial, and even form a weapon out of pure stone or water or what have you. The teamwork is also pretty strong in this ability, using the finesse of melee to interpose for allies and even counter with a distract gambit. It might kind of relate to the subtle idea that the swordsman is also traditionally the leader character in mashup gangs like this. Just look at any sentai series.<br /> <br /> It's also got that thing, which is a theme for fire in general, where it really likes having higher initiative than its opponents.<br /> <br /> Mechanically it's pretty solid, with a few effects having some cool overt elemental manipulation like a large cloud of steam that gives allies initiative or grasping roots that make your weapon awesome. It's also got a really nice wide spread of aspects within it, letting anyone be a swordsman if they want to.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think I might leave that there. Performance is going to be a doozy to read through and I probably won't even have all that much to say on it. I like how the DBs have enough options that relate to their element as to grant a boon while fighting in it, but not so many that you feel dumb not doing it all the time. It's also just an aggressive charmset overall, with trees like dodge dealing a lot of damage, integrity making you a lion to defend your intimacies, and medicine aggressively healing and hurting. I'll get to the rest of it this weekend though, this has been fun!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T00:14:53-07:00","id":1213688,"title":"","content":"Going to do a quick on here just so I keep up with it<br /> <br /> <b>Occult</b><br /> <br /> Now I played a Supernal occult Solar and as I recall it's really focused on a few things. It has an entire tree branch dedicated to this mandala of sealing/warding charm, a few charms to manipulate and fight spirits, and a couple others that boost sorcery, particularly mote collections.<br /> <br /> The DB one dues have that, but they go about it in a different way. Whereas the Solar charms feel like you're just exerting your willpower over spirits, with charms that just bind spirits or allow you to see them, the Terrestrials feel more like they're using some kind of universal sorcery laws. Like instead of just warding a place against spirits they need to ring it with salt or germinated grain, or how they need a mirror to see spirits and a prayer strip to bind them.<br /> <br /> It's also got this kind of interesting theme of connecting you more deeply with the world. It lets you sense expressions of the elements nearby, summon spirit dragons in the water, all sorts of stuff. Even if you're not a sorcerer this tree definitely makes you feel like one.<br /> <br /> Their sorcery is also really cool, it's only two charms but they're much appreciated. Especially the one that allows them to gather sorcerers motes faster, in the case of Aura much faster, for an elemental spell. With this and one of those sorcerous rituals to draw more motes you're easily snapping off an attack spell every turn.<br /> <br /> Overall I'm impressed, for all the mechanical overlap it does a great job of making it feel unique.<br /> <br /> <b>Performance</b><br /> <br /> You ever play DnD? You like it? Like the Bard? Me too. Solars get some cool stuff that improves their ability to convince people with song, to make phantasmal backup dancers, and to improve their companions in combat.<br /> <br /> Dragonblooded take the cake here though, they can cure disease, hide in plain sight, sing realistic illusions into existence. Solars might be really good at performing but terrestrials are straight up magic. The there ARE charms in here that boost performance rolls, usually related to either passion, authority, or shared intimacies. This would be another great ability for an immaculate monk character. I'm seeing a kind of a trickster monk who uses his song and speech to enchant a forest and the people who live there.<br /> <br /> The thing is the actual performance rolls are kind of overshadowed by the cool other stuff. I don't even mind, it's awesome. You can rock out on a violin and shred physical attacks out of the bow, you can float through a forest. I mean it's just great. You can grab a bit of foliage and magically shape it into any instrument you want. I can't even list how many sweet sassy things you can do with this ability.<br /> <br /> Final verdict? A+, but to be fair this was basically tailored for my sensibilities. I'm pretty sure Solars wish they had this tree though. Teamwork in this tree too numerous to mention.<br /> <br /> <b>Presence</b><br /> <br /> Solar presence is interesting, it not only boosts your ability to personally affect people with the social system, it kind of lets you just empower them to do anything better. More courageous, more skilled, more loyal, more fearful.<br /> <br /> The Dragonblooded themes of passion come to a head in this tree. It's got some pretty cool abilities to just skip a lot of the normal processes with this one, like turning lust into rage into giddy laughter. Which doesn't actually just let you skip the social scene, it just gives a fun shortcut if you can pull it off. There's also a lot of combat charms in here. There's ones for enhancing join battle, for giving yourself more soak and health levels, and even just straight deal damage in an area, among others. I think with presence alone you could almost be a decent combatant, almost.<br /> <br /> There's also a kind of a running theme of loyalty here too. You see it a bit in the Solar tree but it comes out quite a bit harder here. It's actually to the point where some of these effects rival Solar charms. It's good though, you can take this in either a despotic forced Darth Vader enforcer route or a brotherly Captain America and Bucky style bond.<br /> <br /> <b>Resistance</b><br /> <br /> Solar resistance has very little surprises. Apart from a berzerker rage section of the tree really everything is just about resisting damage and poison and stuff.<br /> <br /> Dragonblooded do that too, but also their charms to stave off hunger and sleep and stuff are here, instead of Solar's integrity. I've also been waiting this whole review<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-iQU9XGFSmQ\" target=\"_blank\"> to link this</a>, and here's the most appropriate time. It's got the 5 elements right and everything. It's also got some really cool mechanical effects like gaining hardness equal to your current initiative. It's also got more of that instant healing that we saw in DB medicine that Solars don't really get. Again I feel it's a virtue of rather than being a human ability taken to an extreme it's an utterly inhuman magic.<br /> <br /> Short, simple, straightforward, but with some cool effects to set it apart.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think that's all for today, but I'm continuing to like these comparisons. If all you knew about the terrestrial charmset was that they were weaker than Solars you might not even bother. Which is really too bad, considering DB performance lets you pick a dandelion, shape it into a giant yellow drum with leaf hammers, and beat out a tune of shock waves to defeat an army. Something else I'll notice is that the Solars tend to have a lot more dice trick charms, where as the DBs tend to just have charms that add more unique effects.<br /> <br /> Also there's just a lot of incidental flavour to them. One of the resistance charms that heals you also bursts forth and heals all the wilting plantlife around you, the occult charms require sacred scripts to function, stuff like this really helps bring the charmset alive.<br /> <br /> I might try to finish it off in the next one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T04:33:26-07:00","id":1213738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1211530#post1211530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tbh I think The Beast is the <i>least </i>dangerous thing a Solar can be. You can divert them, outmaneuver them, find out what they want and exploit that knowledge to make them be disruptive somewhere else. Someone utterly dedicated to and solely motivated by martial excellence is very easy to deal with, as long as you have something to point them at. Get someone to seduce them so they settle down and live in marital bliss for a few centuries. Play on their desire to prove themselves as the greatest warrior who ever lived and let them know about invincible behemoths that lurk in the forgotten corners of the world. You don't have to best them at <i>literally the only one thing </i>they're good at.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of people consider The Beast a problem because we've only encountered him when he's following the other PCs around in a state of inertia and would sooner let a circlemate die than perform a Defend Other action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12844-bladewind","name":"Bladewind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T06:24:01-07:00","id":1213771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bladewind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1213738#post1213738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of people consider The Beast a problem because we've only encountered him when he's following the other PCs around in a state of inertia and would sooner let a circlemate die than perform a Defend Other action.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does he also spam \u201cI need healing\u201d?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T07:58:05-07:00","id":1213794,"title":"","content":"Everything about the Beast makes me think of him as either the worst MOBA teammate or an exaltified version of <a href=\"https://www.sbnation.com/nfl/2013/9/5/4691010/breaking-madden-clarence-beeftank-jaguars\" target=\"_blank\">Clarence BEEFTANK.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T08:42:51-07:00","id":1213804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steamfunk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1213794#post1213794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything about the Beast makes me think of him as either the worst MOBA teammate or an exaltified version of <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.sbnation.com/nfl/2013/9/5/4691010/breaking-madden-clarence-beeftank-jaguars&amp;quot;]Clarence</a> BEEFTANK.[/URL]</div> </div> </div> </div>I had somebody play that kind of character in my first ever exalted campaign. He basically used his invincibility to be a total dick and kill every problem that arose from it, including the problems that arose from killing the previous problems.<br /> <br /> Eventually it got so bad every other PC conspired to a huge session long plan that ended with finally killing his character. Which was awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T09:40:30-07:00","id":1213819,"title":"","content":"Gotta say DrLoveMonkey, that I love your comparisons of the charms between Solars and Dragonblooded. I will probably be using these as examples to show my players when we get back to Exalted.<br /> <br /> Keep up the good work! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T10:36:06-07:00","id":1213828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1213804#post1213804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I had somebody play that kind of character in my first ever exalted campaign. He basically used his invincibility to be a total dick and kill every problem that arose from it, including the problems that arose from killing the previous problems.<br /> <br /> Eventually it got so bad every other PC conspired to a huge session long plan that ended with finally killing his character. Which was awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have seen this in games too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T11:25:08-07:00","id":1213833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1213804#post1213804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I had somebody play that kind of character in my first ever exalted campaign. He basically used his invincibility to be a total dick and kill every problem that arose from it, including the problems that arose from killing the previous problems.<br /> <br /> Eventually it got so bad every other PC conspired to a huge session long plan that ended with finally killing his character. Which was awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My RP friends and I have a term for this problem.<br /> <br /> &quot;Former problem player we removed from our group for dickery.&quot;<br /> <br /> But I admit, that's just because we have a low tolerance after years of dickery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5771-krata-lightblade","name":"Krata Lightblade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5771_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T11:29:36-07:00","id":1213835,"title":"","content":"I had to deal with a Beast in my... probably second Exalted game. His player didn't care that clomping around in orichalcum full plate with a surfboard-claymore was going to get him unpleasantly noticed, and beyond simply ignoring the social system, he outright belittled those who wanted to use it.<br /> He ended up having to be booted the heck out for general assin' about.<br /> <br /> Anyway, this thread is really great! Besides simply mapping out what's what with the DB power scale, it also points out all the interesting character and feel to the DB charmset. Honestly, I think DBs have spoiled me. Their charmset feels really tight and flavorful (and even though there's evidently a hunk more charms to be given in the companion because word limit, I still doubt it'll make the charmset too huge), and now Solar charms, despite having bigger and shinier numbers to flail around, just feels... bloaty and comparatively less interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T12:20:14-07:00","id":1213858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beans</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1213835#post1213835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had to deal with a Beast in my... probably second Exalted game. His player didn't care that clomping around in orichalcum full plate with a surfboard-claymore was going to get him unpleasantly noticed, and beyond simply ignoring the social system, he outright belittled those who wanted to use it.<br /> He ended up having to be booted the heck out for general assin' about.<br /> <br /> Anyway, this thread is really great! Besides simply mapping out what's what with the DB power scale, it also points out all the interesting character and feel to the DB charmset. Honestly, I think DBs have spoiled me. Their charmset feels really tight and flavorful (and even though there's evidently a hunk more charms to be given in the companion because word limit, I still doubt it'll make the charmset too huge), and now Solar charms, despite having bigger and shinier numbers to flail around, just feels... bloaty and comparatively less interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>This a problem I've had with Solar's every edition so far. Not that indevidual charms can't be good, I love Solar Athletics for example. It's just that the charmset as a whole dosn't have the same wow factor as DBs, Lunar Knaks or Infernal and Alchemical transhumanism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15685-up-to-eleven","name":"Up-to-Eleven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T22:37:07-07:00","id":1214044,"title":"","content":"I think a lot of the antipathy toward the solar charmset can be (from anecdata) be really narrowed to 3, maybe 4 charmsets. 1) Craft: this charmset has been probably the most continentious in the game, along with the craft system in general. Robert Vance in the Q&amp;A board noted feedback on it directly influenced his design of DB craft. 2) Presence: A large amount of dice adders in the front end of the tree can make it uninspired/Bloated. 3) Performance: similar reasons though I feel compelled to point out this depends on what you are going into performance for imo (Wizard of Oz made several good points on both in the Perception thread). 4) I would argue could be awareness, specifically because how that tree parses out the sense. <br /> <br /> These ones stand out because the are central to many concepts (crafter, face, and different versions of the \u201cI see all the things\u201d char).<br /> <br /> As an example of where imo the solar Charmset shines is 1) Brawl 2) Occult 3) Linguistics 4) Athletics 5) Archery<br /> <br /> This is not to say concerns about solar charm bloat are invalid, but rather that the factors of being first out the gate and the bloat concentrating in a few critical trees, changes the perception of all of the solar charmset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T02:07:58-07:00","id":1214085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ffanxii4ever</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1213819#post1213819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gotta say DrLoveMonkey, that I love your comparisons of the charms between Solars and Dragonblooded. I will probably be using these as examples to show my players when we get back to Exalted.<br /> <br /> Keep up the good work! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beans</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1213835#post1213835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, this thread is really great! Besides simply mapping out what's what with the DB power scale, it also points out all the interesting character and feel to the DB charmset. Honestly, I think DBs have spoiled me. Their charmset feels really tight and flavorful (and even though there's evidently a hunk more charms to be given in the companion because word limit, I still doubt it'll make the charmset too huge), and now Solar charms, despite having bigger and shinier numbers to flail around, just feels... bloaty and comparatively less interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awww! Thank you very much, I definitely appreciate it!<br /> <br /> I've come to the conclusion basically that if you want to play a game about the world ending and hopping from direction to direction fighting directional war gods and massive demon invasions Solars are the way to go, but for the scale of games I prefer to play in and run DBs are looking a lot better. Smaller charms that don't reach as high, but go broader.<br /> <br /> <br /> Okay lets get back to it<br /> <br /> <b>Ride</b><br /> <br /> Ride is an interesting one from the Solar perspective. This is one of those trees like sail, where it's less about the actual ability to ride things and more about the archetype of a horseman. Or Sailor in the case of sail. It's got some cool stuff to give you a real solid bond with your mount, almost like a familiar, and draw strength from that bond. It's also got quite a few combat movement charms, along with the classic Solar &quot;I do this amazing&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> Something you might immediately notice about the DB charm tree is that a lot of the capabilities to make your mount do things exist here in the form of discreet charms, whereas in the Solar tree it's just taken care of by letting your horse use athletics charms as though it were you. Afterwords though we get a lot of interesting stuff that sets it apart. One thing is that there's more utility in this tree than in the Solar one.<br /> <br /> Basically the Solar one just lets your mount go anywhere really damn fast with maybe a few combat tricks. Here we've got your mount adding a huge bonus to it's strength for FoS and damage, running under water, and leading a huge charge of stampeding animals. There's also some combat stuff in here, including a charm that aids horse archers, but the big one here is the charge. There's more than a couple of charms that give a bonus to an attack performed after a rush, or after a movement, and they can be pretty cool. One even gives it's benefit to all nearby allies in Charge of One Hundred Generals, one of my favourite charm names.<br /> <br /> We also see a really cool effect here where a DB can actually mark their steed with their exalted blood and kind of demi-exalt it. This is the first case I've seen of a DB being able to share the power in their blood, and it's pretty cool. The charm is just solid too, it just improves your mount in almost every way.<br /> <br /> It's an easy to understand tree that gets a lot done with just a few charms, it seems.<br /> <br /> <b>Sail</b><br /> <br /> Solar sail I have to say I don't like much. Mostly because with almost no credible antagonists to a Solar captain the sail system totally falls apart, and a very good chunk of this tree relies on that system. I mean Solars in general can suffer a problem of not having anything to challenge them but there's nothing in the corebook that mentions sail based antagonists at all. The rest of the tree is cool though, a lot of nice salty sea captain charms that make you a good leader, hardy and wary.<br /> <br /> The Dragonblooded one fixes that problem. Almost all the sail charms here that interact with the sail system ALSO do something else. So bam, now Solars have a credible enemy to fight AND the Terrestrial tree is useful to groups who don't like the naval combat system! This tree is also home to some of the most epic effects since Dragon Vortex back in lore. Probably because ships are just big things, but it's got stuff like setting the seas on fire, using your vessel to demolish structures, and creating a huge fog bank or maelstrom that can swallow a ship. Wood also gets an instant healing effect again, but this time the living wood of your ship.<br /> <br /> Otherwise it's got some of the same sort of effects to avoid hazzards and be an old salty dog, just with less power but nicely condensed so you're not spending 15 charms to do it all.<br /> <br /> <b>Socialize</b><br /> <br /> Socialize! Man the Solar tree is big. A huge section of it is dedicated to the Persona charms, which lets you assume a different character basically. It's all about reading intentions and social norms otherwise. Stopping people from reading your intentions, reading a whole room yourself, and a bunch of tricks therein to get motes back and stuff.<br /> <br /> With Dragonblooded it almost seems designed for people who want to go into a nation and turn everyone against eachother. You infiltrate their culture, observe them while being inscrutable, stop them from using intimacies of loyalty to protect one another, use magic alchohol to lower their inhibitions, and finally turning them against eachother or a sub-culture/outsider. BUT something you might not immediately realize is that's also the exact skill set you need to pull apart a corrupt organization too. You infiltrate the local branch of the Imperial government, find out who's corrupt, turn those criminals against each other, and then finally turn all the remaining people against them.<br /> <br /> Overall though it's got some great charms that interact perfectly with high class intrigue and political drama. It's usable elsewhere for sure, there's nothing that says you can't infuse the grog in a dingy seaside pub with Sweeten the Tap, but it's home is lounging coolly on the veranda while you sip wine and decide the fate of nations.<br /> <br /> <b>Stealth</b><br /> <br /> Oh boy Solar Stealth. It's got a lot of stuff that's just straight power, like giving penalties to your opponent while banishing certain senses from detecting you at all. It also makes you a real ninja with a few combat charms for ambushing, and eventually being able to do pretty incredible things like teleporting through shadow.<br /> <br /> The DB one has much of the same, like being able to be perfectly silent, as well as mute charms. The muting thing is kind of required for all exalted stealth though, so it's not surprise. The silence is cool though because it has a teamwork affect of being able to make a whole area silent, which also means you can have an entire battle in a room with all your allies and none of the guards outside will hear a peep. It's also got some cool stuff like performance which is reminiscent of illusion magic, there's stuff here to make you invisible and even have an insubstantial decoy of yourself.<br /> <br /> There's also a few charms that aid sneak attacks, but overall it's standout for the straight impossible things it can do. The capstone, for instance, lets you kill somebody by willing the air from their lungs from stealth. That's just a classy way to do an assassination.<br /> <br /> <b>Survival</b><br /> <br /> Solar survival is about two things. living in the hardship of the elements, and playing Beastmaster. More seriously there's a few charms in there for tracking and stuff too, but like half the tree is dedicated to making a familiar of yours into that-which-devours-gods. A powerful familiar properly enhanced might be more powerful than a Dawn even.<br /> <br /> With dragonblooded the running theme is power over nature itself. There's some tracking charms, some teamwork charms to give your allies a solid boost in harsh climates, but the real eye catchers are how it interacts with the elements. Like diverting a raging forest fire, earth bending a landslide clear, or forcing a spring to erupt from the ground. When a DB survivalist seeks shelter, nature accommodates her.<br /> <br /> One of those elements you can interact with though, is beasts. Yep, familiar charms here too, but they feel a lot more cooperative than the Solar ones. Getting the familiar requires you to do some convincing and training, acts of kindness and mutual respect will lead to a companion that defends you, and eventually to things like a twin attack charm where you both launch a finishign move together that succeeds or fails as one.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't have expected DB survival to be this cool. With it you don't so much feel like a super woodsman like you do with Solars, but more a master of the elements themselves.<br /> <br /> <b>Thrown</b><br /> <br /> Solar thrown is a great combat tree that's full of going first, and disabling your target. It's got a ton of things that do everything but kill the person you thrown knives at, luckily it's got a ton of things that kill them too. And help you get your knife back.<br /> <br /> DB thrown looks to keep that up with a good few charms that stack the penalties on. It's also got this cool charm where you throw a weapon and it takes on a life of it's own after it leaves your hand, it's on initiative track and everything, and I can't let this go without pointing out you can use it with Elemental Bolt Attack to have an autonomous bolt of lightning leaping around the battlefield while you continue to fight.<br /> <br /> There's also this interesting thing that happens near the end of the tree where you create a whirlwind as a shield around you that also has it's own initiative track. It surrounds you and defends you from ranged attacks while you sit back and rain death down on the battlefield. It's got a few upgrade charms even.<br /> <br /> It puts an interesting twist on the Solar style of doing it for sure. I encourage anyone reading through the thrown charms to always keep in mind that Elemental Bolt Attack can be used with any of there, making for invisible strikes of water from underneath a river, or flaming exploding shards of rock.<br /> <br /> <b>War</b><br /> <br /> Solar war benefited a lot from the much better new mass combat system of 3e. Unlike the sail system this one has seen a lot of use all over and the charms integrate better with it. It leans a bit heavy on the strategic maneuvers, which I haven't seen used much, but overall it's effective at conveying a powerful and intelligent general. It gives big dice bonuses to those maneuvers anyway as well as buffing your mass combat unit's stats.<br /> <br /> Dragonblooded focus less on the strategic and more on the tactical. They've got more charms for boosting command rolls and rallying them when they falter. What charms they have that end up interacting with the strategic side of the mass combat are big elemental expressions. Reshaping the battlefield with earth, raining down lightning with air, flooding the field with fog from water. I think it works well, there's enough support there for the big strategic battles, while letting, I think, the more common aspect of a captain with a small force who uses it like a second weapon in combat shine.<br /> <br /> Definitely a fan of war, even the more simple dice charms and stuff do more of what I want from it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And there's the end of abilities! I might go on to talk about the coolness of the new MAs and those tantalizing artifacts in the book as well. Something that's come up in this section is the sort of presumption of authority. You see it in socialize and even a bit in sail and stuff, and I think that's a great way of making DBs stand out, since basically no matter where you go in creation they're at worst powerful heroes and at best divine messengers, so that's cool to take advantage of in the official charms.<br /> <br /> Something else in these trees is that we've got some really really overtly big magic things going on that stand out huge from the Solars. Solars have a million successes on the dice roll, sure, but there's nothing you can even roll to fill a forest with fog before a battle, or divert a wildfire. These effects are really interesting and cool to get because they don't just take something you were going to do anyway and make it better/easier, but they give you some real options to do the impossible in big ways.<br /> <br /> Anyway, that's it for now, be back later with MA and Sorcery!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T08:05:32-07:00","id":1214164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1214085#post1214085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Thrown</b><br /> <br /> [...]<br /> DB thrown looks to keep that up with a good few charms that stack the penalties on. It's also got this cool charm where you throw a weapon and it takes on a life of it's own after it leaves your hand, it's on initiative track and everything, and I can't let this go without pointing out you can use it with Elemental Bolt Attack to have an autonomous bolt of lightning leaping around the battlefield while you continue to fight. [...]<br /> <br /> It puts an interesting twist on the Solar style of doing it for sure. I encourage anyone reading through the thrown charms to always keep in mind that Elemental Bolt Attack can be used with any of there, making for invisible strikes of water from underneath a river, or flaming exploding shards of rock.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly, this isn't actually the case; both Elemental Bolt Attack and most of the really cool Thrown charms are Simple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24165-parabola","name":"Parabola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24165_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T09:29:35-07:00","id":1214195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Parabola</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1214164#post1214164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly, this isn't actually the case; both Elemental Bolt Attack and most of the really cool Thrown charms are Simple.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awwwww piss you\u2019re totally right, I forgot to check that.<br /> <br /> I should stop doing these at 5am.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T10:42:02-07:00","id":1214215,"title":"","content":"I belatedly realized that DBs have to take four Occult charms before they can get Sorcery, which is at least mildly a bummer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T11:07:54-07:00","id":1214223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beans</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1214215#post1214215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I belatedly realized that DBs have to take four Occult charms before they can get Sorcery, which is at least mildly a bummer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well.. mechanics aside it makes sense, from a lore standpoint, that DBs would learn a few Occult charms before sorcery because they exalt pretty young, generally before attaining sorcerous enlightenment,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11671,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11671-dramaflo","user":"DraMaFlo","date":". 05-02-2018, 02:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11671-dramaflo","name":"DraMaFlo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11671_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T11:38:04-07:00","id":1214233,"title":"","content":"Hm. So to summarize: Solars have &quot;do stuff good&quot; charms that are powerful and (not bland, so much as &quot;you need to decide how your SPECIFIC hero looks using these&quot;). DB charms have lots of built-in theminess, generally less powerful except in specific areas, instead of &quot;do stuff like a boss&quot; have &quot;get the elements to do stuff for you like a boss&quot;, have attack &amp; defence options in noncombat trees so <u>every</u> DB can be in the army. And DB have some teamwork-synergy charms, although the details so far are kinda vague - one or two team-useful charms per tree? And DB have more &quot;loyal warrior&quot; and &quot;klingon team&quot; social charms, vs Solar being more &quot;I am so mightily awesome you do what I ask&quot;<br /> <br /> And it satisfies one of my 2E peeves re the Usurpation - I can now see mechanically how the DB could have pulled it off, without making Solars so weak they seem like chumps. Basically, even if half the DB stayed loyal, you could send a 5-person strike team against every regular solar or lunar, and 15 against every Beast Solar (using roughly 10k DB, 300 solar, 300 lunar). From your calcs (4WP per death blossom), sounds like the Beast might wipe out two 5-man-bands, but go down to the third. Nowadays you just don't have enough DB to afford that kind of attrition war, Solars are traveling in packs, and both sides have to use mortals for onslaught-meat.<br /> <br /> As far as shoutouts - I see Voltron and Dr Who charms so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2678-spoonr","name":"SpoonR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2678_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T12:26:40-07:00","id":1214261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beans</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1214215#post1214215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I belatedly realized that DBs have to take four Occult charms before they can get Sorcery, which is at least mildly a bummer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes that's true, although at least one is the excellency that you'd definitely pick up anyway. I recommend Fivefold Resonance, Seed and Salt Warding and Spirit Detecting Mirror for the others if you're going pure sorcerer.<br /> <br /> I think the reasoning for this might be that DBs are less powerful and more restricted, and that's compounded by Terrestrial Circle Sorcery being one of the best charms in the game to just dip into. Almost the only reason not to do it is because you don't like how it fits the character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T12:28:27-07:00","id":1214262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DraMaFlo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1214223#post1214223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well.. mechanics aside it makes sense, from a lore standpoint, that DBs would learn a few Occult charms before sorcery because they exalt pretty young, generally before attaining sorcerous enlightenment,</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more that one of the Solar keystones is sorcerous excellence, so they get immediate and cheap access to it, while the DB have to invest a good chunk of development to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T18:56:49-07:00","id":1214389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1214085#post1214085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>War</b><br /> <br /> Solar war benefited a lot from the much better new mass combat system of 3e. Unlike the sail system this one has seen a lot of use all over and the charms integrate better with it. It leans a bit heavy on the strategic maneuvers, which I haven't seen used much, but overall it's effective at conveying a powerful and intelligent general. It gives big dice bonuses to those maneuvers anyway as well as buffing your mass combat unit's stats.<br /> <br /> Dragonblooded focus less on the strategic and more on the tactical. They've got more charms for boosting command rolls and rallying them when they falter. What charms they have that end up interacting with the strategic side of the mass combat are big elemental expressions. Reshaping the battlefield with earth, raining down lightning with air, flooding the field with fog from water. I think it works well, there's enough support there for the big strategic battles, while letting, I think, the more common aspect of a captain with a small force who uses it like a second weapon in combat shine.<br /> <br /> Definitely a fan of war, even the more simple dice charms and stuff do more of what I want from it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Reading this made me realize that both splats war trees slot in fairly well with the general Idea of how the Primordial war went. Solar focus on Stratagems and big picture stuff vs. DB's larger emphasis on the Tactical battles fits into the idea of &quot;Glorious Golden General directs the campaign while the 5 Dragon Lords oversee the various fronts&quot;. In strategy game terms, the Solars are your faction leaders, while the DBs are hero units, though both have the capacity for either role.<br /> <br /> Which makes me very curious for Lunar Mass Combat Charms and Sidereal War.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Life before Death, Strength before Weakness, Journey before Destination.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">&quot;I will protect those who cannot protect themselves&quot;</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4172-marros56","name":"Marros56","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4172_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T19:33:47-07:00","id":1214398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marros56</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1214389#post1214389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which makes me very curious for Lunar Mass Combat Charms and Sidereal War.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Lunar War is probably going to be 'I am the army!' and the Sids might be something like enhancing the way the army works together(communication, orders, etc) or interfering with the other army in the same way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T19:42:21-07:00","id":1214401,"title":"","content":"I feel Lunars would have limited support for commanding battle-groups above a certain size or beyond a certain range. By all means, a Lunar can assemble and lead (or simply unleash) a massive horde of screaming barbarians, but no one said they should be any good at making sure such a force wins. Indeed, the corebook talks about how the Lunar Exalted use such hordes as canon fodder, sacrificing them to bleed the Realm.<br /> <br /> A Lunar could roar like a lion-god to make his orders heard across the entire field, and inspire courage in his followers and fear in their foes as he personally tears enemy heroes and battle-groups apart, but that's about it. Social Full Moons and physical Changing Moons using Charisma or Appearance to lead from the front.<br /> <br /> On the open battlefield, a No Moon might be contributing mostly through casting spells, especially Celestial Circle ones.<br /> <br /> Intelligence-based Lunar warfare, being primarily strategic, may be less about War than it is about Larceny. Spying out strategically vital targets, planning daring infiltrations, and then leading, small, intimate, well-trained, and specially-prepared strike-teams that no one sees coming and may not even realize is there until after they've left.<br /> <br /> The strategic Lunar experience is about REALLY playing into the situations that normally only grant bonus dice on Strategic Maneuver rolls: <br /> <br /> &quot;General has spies and informants within the enemy\u2019s ranks&quot;, &quot;General has a high-placed traitor within enemy ranks&quot;, &quot;The players have roleplayed one or more scenes in which they obtained some concrete advantage over the enemy or harmed the enemy army (stealing its secrets, devastating its supply lines, killing a famous hero of the opposing forces, etc).&quot;<br /> <br /> Strategic Lunars would be especially good at successfully employing the Demoralized strategy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T20:05:09-07:00","id":1214405,"title":"","content":"Lunar war makes me think of 40k assassins. The shapeshifter that backstabs the enemy general in the chaos of battle. The blender of berserk death that both sides run from. Those two at least feel Lunary, the other two assassins (anti-psychic there so maybe anti-FairFolk here, and the supersniper), not so much.<br /> <br /> Hm. Solar War gets &quot;Tiger Warrior training technique&quot;. Lunars get &quot;warrior into tigerman technique&quot;? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Actually, Lunar war could lean towards guerilla warfare. American Revolution &quot;The Swamp Fox&quot; Franis Marion, who exploited detailed knowledge of the local swamps. Vietcong tactics. Mao's Long March. Mongol's use of &quot;barbarians can travel fast and light so we can attack from behind&quot; and their feigned-retreat-turning-into-an-ambush.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2678,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2678-spoonr","user":"SpoonR","date":".  real ideas 05-02-2018, 11:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2678-spoonr","name":"SpoonR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2678_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T22:33:22-07:00","id":1214424,"title":"","content":"And now I'm imagining an outcaste general using Hidden Thorn Treachery with an allied Lunar as the infiltrator. If that isn't worth at <i>least</i> +5 on the strategy roll then I don't know what is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T23:44:42-07:00","id":1214440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpoonR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1214405#post1214405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, Lunar war could lean towards guerilla warfare. American Revolution &quot;The Swamp Fox&quot; Franis Marion, who exploited detailed knowledge of the local swamps. Vietcong tactics. Mao's Long March. Mongol's use of &quot;barbarians can travel fast and light so we can attack from behind&quot; and their feigned-retreat-turning-into-an-ambush.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you mean gorilla warfare. Eh? Eh? That joke's never been made before...<br /> <br /> Anyway yeah, any exalt is better than mortal at whatever they want to be really good at, even if it's not really their splat's thing. I see Lunar tactics as being more outside the box. Even the DB stratagy charms are kind of staightforward and obvious in their application. The Lunar ones I feel would be less so. Like I fully expect them to have an ambush charm where you don't even realize you're about to fight a battle and then a massive horde bursts forth from woods that seemed just too small to contain them. Like they used their essence and command ability to hide a whole army up trees, just on the other side of sight or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T00:00:57-07:00","id":1214448,"title":"","content":"Hey so I've had a quick epiphany here regarding Solars and DBs. Since DBs start at essence 2, they've actually got way more access to evocations right off the hop than Solars do. So even though their combat charm selection is limited, they can way more easily augment it with their heirloom weapons. It's an interesting balance I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T09:35:38-07:00","id":1214646,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I checked before, and for most artefact weapons you can start with 3 or 4 evocations at character gen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T13:58:21-07:00","id":1214760,"title":"","content":"Thanks for doing all this, DLM. I'm just really giving Ex3 a chance with DB since I wasn't super hot on Solars (after the plural year wait to get uninvested in the game while it languished in developer hell) but DB are one of my top three favorites in this setting and the fact the new book looked so rad was enough to egg me back in. <br /> <br /> The mechanical breakdowns you did especially actually have helped me a lot with internalizing elements of the combat system before my group gets to its first session, and lets me see how DB look in 'action' against actually dangerous threats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T15:46:20-07:00","id":1214801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1214760#post1214760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for doing all this, DLM. I'm just really giving Ex3 a chance with DB since I wasn't super hot on Solars (after the plural year wait to get uninvested in the game while it languished in developer hell) but DB are one of my top three favorites in this setting and the fact the new book looked so rad was enough to egg me back in. <br /> <br /> The mechanical breakdowns you did especially actually have helped me a lot with internalizing elements of the combat system before my group gets to its first session, and lets me see how DB look in 'action' against actually dangerous threats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey thanks! You\u2019ll want to stay tuned then because after MA, a light touch on sorcery, and artifacts, I\u2019ll be posting a summary of how character building is very different for a DB in what you want/can focus on and the widely different options available.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T10:22:07-07:00","id":1215136,"title":"","content":"I'll be interested to see your MA evaluation because I'm personally having a major love-hate relationship with the Immaculate Styles right now. On the one hand, for DBs they're exactly as strong and cool as they're supposed to be. On the other hand, &quot;ex-monk Solar&quot; is (from what I've heard) a fairly popular character concept and for whatever reason the IMAs do a <i>spectacularly</i> worse job than regular MAs of obscuring which of their Charms are definite downgrades from their closest native Solar equivalents.<br /> <br /> Now, before anyone misinterprets that, I want to make explicitly clear that I'm specifically talking about <i>apparent</i> power, and specifically in comparison to other Martial Arts styles. The best way to put it is: while yes, the default assumption should be that any Martial Arts Charm without a Mastery effect is going to technically be weaker than a Solar Charm, all of the regular styles (including the three in WFHW) do a superb job of not <i>feeling</i> that way. The IMAs, on the other hand... don't, which often makes for a rather awkward reading experience and at times severely cuts into their overall &quot;awesome&quot; factor, including for potential DB practitioners.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","user":"Sith_Happens","date":". 05-04-2018, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T10:35:35-07:00","id":1215140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1215136#post1215136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll be interested to see your MA evaluation because I'm personally having a major love-hate relationship with the Immaculate Styles right now. On the one hand, for DBs they're exactly as strong and cool as they're supposed to be. On the other hand, &quot;ex-monk Solar&quot; is (from what I've heard) a fairly popular character concept and for whatever reason the IMAs do a <i>spectacularly</i> worse job than regular MAs of obscuring which of their Charms are definite downgrades from their closest native Solar equivalents.<br /> <br /> Now, before anyone misinterprets that, I want to make explicitly clear that I'm specifically talking about <i>apparent</i> power, and specifically in comparison to other Martial Arts styles. The best way to put it is: while yes, the default assumption should be that any Martial Arts Charm without a Mastery effect is going to technically be weaker than a Solar Charm, all of the regular styles (including the three in WFHW) do a superb job of not <i>feeling</i> that way. The IMAs, on the other hand... don't, which often makes for a rather awkward reading experience and at times severely cuts into their overall &quot;awesome&quot; factor, including for potential DB practitioners.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ill be sure to focus on that aspect then.<br /> <br /> EDIT: can you think of any specific ones that are direct Solar analogues? I can think of a few that kind of are but I might be missing what you\u2019re talking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 05-04-2018, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T16:07:47-07:00","id":1215259,"title":"","content":"I had just made my peace with the idea that Lunar Exalted would no longer be capable of learning Immaculate Martial Arts Charms when I read the rules again and realized that wasn't actually the case.<br /> <br /> You can still have monks who Exalt as Lunars and go on to learn the Immaculate Charms of their Style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T18:54:52-07:00","id":1215309,"title":"","content":"Okay well either way lets take a look at the immaculate martial arts!<br /> <br /> First of all just a few quick things that help, one the styles have elemental charms. Not only do the style use them themselves, but that means they can generate aura for the other charms as well, like say if you needed earth aura for a resistance charm you could use Earth Dragon the previous turn. Next is they lack both the terrestrial and mastery keywords, meaning that not only are they not worse for DBs but they aren't better for Solars either. Speaking of, DBs are the only terrestrials who can learn them. There's also a cool ability for DBs who've learned the form charm to ignore the terrestrial keyword for any MA by expending their aura. It's cool and definitely allows for a relatively easy route to power without making it just ignore the keyword all together.<br /> <br /> BIG thing to remember before I get into it though, and that's the MA excellency. When I did the short ability previews I almost made a section on each for their excellency ability but it ended up too long. The MA one allows you to block/make lethal attacks with any bare handed attack, and also reroll damage 6s until they fail to appear. That means basically every single MA attack that I''m about to talk about also has &quot;reroll 6s on damage until they fail to appear&quot; for free.<br /> <br /> Anyway onto the actual styles<br /> <br /> <b>Air Dragon</b><br /> <br /> Air Dragon style is pretty cool, it's the only style with a ranged weapon (kinda) and it makes good use of it. It's all about positioning. You might look at the style and initially think that Evasion is your main form of defense here, but it's not, it's distance. You can flurry a disengage with an attack, knock back opponents to long range, make your unarmed attacks ranged, and have multiple ranged simple charms.<br /> <br /> It also has a few charms to see in the dark, reestablish stealth in plain sight, and some mobility charms. So yeah it gets around and it's hard to pin down. How's it for the actual power of the attacks though? Pretty good! Lightning Strike Style lets you get overflow successes on decisive attacks and ignore hardness and cover. It even gets the ability with Hurricane Combat Method to roll a reflexive attack that doesn't count as her attack, and can be a clash. So it's offensive potential is decently high.<br /> <br /> The image of an Air Dragon master is one standing in a wind swept field using chakrams and blasts of wind and lightning to turn back all attackers before they can even step within sword range.<br /> <br /> <b>Earth Dragon</b><br /> <br /> Where Air Dragon's defense was range, Earth Dragon is all about soak. It's compatible with heavy armor, and it's got soak built into it's form charm, which upgrades later, and with a bonus soak adder. Something to notice though is that it's only defense against decisive attacks is hardness, which it can have a lot of. That also means though that if somebody gets a lot of initiative from somewhere else basically your only defense is not getting hit. or a reflexive clash which it also gets.<br /> <br /> How is it on the offense? It centers around smashing attacks and disarming, which is just fun. It's also disabling, with attacks to stack on wound penalties, trap your opponent beneath the earth, and then exploit those penalties with multiple smashing attacks, breaking their weapon along the way. This is a solid style to use if you don't plan on going anywhere, and smashing your opponents prone or taking advantage of Air Dragon knocking them prone is good teamwork.<br /> <br /> The image of an Earth Dragon master is one standing unmoved while catching an opponent's Goremaul, twisting the head off, and then burying his opponent in stone.<br /> <br /> <b>Fire Dragon</b><br /> <br /> Fire Dragon is aggressive as hell, to the point where it's defense is basically how offensive it is. She can burn away her opponent's essence and initiative to ensure they never feel confidant making a decisive attack. You also really don't want to get behind her in initiative because she can stack up the onslaught penalties while dodging around them herself, and then even when she is hit she deals damage back automatically.<br /> <br /> It also seems to have the most straight damage potential of all the styles, and has good synergy with charms from other MAs that also rely on initiative differences. Espeically since it just has the ability to kill enemy initiative while racking it up from multiple sources itself. It's also got a kind of neat trick for an alpha strike where you can roll 2 join battles and pick the highest, but you need to pay for all enhancement charms for each, and then you deal bonus damage if you start things off with a decisive. It's soooo damn expensive but it has the power to just end a fight before it begins.<br /> <br /> The image of a Fire Dragon master is one who flickers around his opponent, burning them to ash and never letting them get their footing.<br /> <br /> <b>Water Dragon</b><br /> <br /> Water Dragon is all about momentum and control. It's got charms to increase grapple, defend while attacking, and building off attacks to actually steal, not just burn opponent's essence along with their initiative. You can also control your opponent with grapple escapes and the ability to actually deactivate enemy charms that they have active. This ability alone can be a game changer as you deactivate that Solar's scenelong penalty negator, thereby meaning they basically wasted the turn they spent getting it up and are also now vulnerable.<br /> <br /> It's also got some pretty solid damage adders and AoE attack charms, which actually most of the styles except Wood seem to pick up. I definitely like it and it does a good job ad what it's trying to do.<br /> <br /> The image of a Water Dragon master is one who gently flows past her opponents attacks and then binds them in their own strength and relentless attacks.<br /> <br /> <b>Wood Dragon</b><br /> <br /> The defense offered up by Wood Dragon is pretty unique. It's got more of that wood aspected instant healing, for both yourself and others, and it adds bonus health levels on top of that. It also borrows a bit from performance in that it can enchant opponents, and then send their soul right to the afterlife. It's also got a really super cool power to use a bow as a staff, it's form weapon, while being able to reflexively swap back to using it as a bow, which means that if you use this style and have archery charms you can instantly snap back to having a ranged attack whenever you want!<br /> <br /> Out of all the styles this one seems the most focused on teamwork. It can heal your allies, it can control and tie up multiple enemies at once, letting your circle focus them down at their leisure, it's just a great support to have. It's also got some surprisingly good damage adding with Eyes of the Wood Dragon, adding probably 5 damage and letting you make better piercing attacks. The cake here though is Soul Mastery, which just negates all the ox-bodies and stuff your opponent took and lets you kill them outright with less effort, but more setup. It's just about the perfect one to round off the previous 4.<br /> <br /> The image of a Wood Dragon master is one who gives strength to her sisters and brothers, gracefully saving them from their foes both during and after the battle.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Summary</b><br /> <br /> These are great! They all offer something really unique in how they play, and they complement eachother well. Also for those who know Ragara Myruun from previous editions, he's a high essence DB who's mastered all 5 styles, and in this edition he's even more scary I think. Just picture the soak from Earth Dragon, combined with the mobility of Air, the damage of Fire, the duality of Water and the resilience of Wood all at once. Terrifying.<br /> <br /> These all work really well and play off the aspect bias that we've seen previously in the ability section. The power also seems to be perhaps slightly above the rest of the DB charmset, but with the caveat that flexibility within an ability is reduced compared to, for example, the myriad of things Brawl is capable of. Combine that with the merit tax and I think it's a decent tradeoff, especially with the armor restrictions.<br /> <br /> Now somebody before asked how these compare to other styles with Mastery, and in general it's both good and bad. As far as effects that are directly comparable like damage adders and stuff the Immaculate Styles tend to lose out, and their big flashy effects generally have a high initiative threshold to use. Also if you can't enter a state of Aura many of the charms become much less good. As a Solar I wouldn't take these if you're looking for a mechanically superior character. I think part of the reason, maybe, to be cynical, that there were so many immaculate Solars in the previous edition is because the immaculate styles were some of the best CMA out there, and if you wanted to make a martial artist they were a great grab.<br /> <br /> As it is now though the effects that other styles DON'T directly emulate are still great. The ability to break an opponent's artifact weapon, or to steal their motes, or instantly healing are all great effects that Solars have great difficulty accessing otherwise. There's also stuff like Heaven Thunder Hammer being better than the Air Dragon knockback, but that needs to be taken in context. Air Dragon can kill you well before you close to melee range, where as Solar Brawl just has a hard time with that. Against an Air Dragon getting knocked back to long range is enough of a death sentence believe me.<br /> <br /> Either way, the effects themselves are still good enough that it's far far from useless to take as a Solar. In fact the Earth Dragon soak adder is BETTER than the Solar one, albeit at a much higher essence requirement for the final charm. I'd still take them if they fit the character, and as I said if you combine multiple of them together they complement eachother really well.<br /> <br /> Anyway that's it for now, let me know if you have any other specific questions, that's it for now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T19:08:17-07:00","id":1215314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1215140#post1215140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ill be sure to focus on that aspect then.<br /> <br /> EDIT: can you think of any specific ones that are direct Solar analogues? I can think of a few that kind of are but I might be missing what you\u2019re talking about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually forget I said anything, I just reread all the IMAs and there's only a handful of Charms between all five that do the thing I'm talking about. As blatantly as they may do it (Air Dragon's Sight and Stone Dragon's Skin being by far the worst offenders, especially the former) I'm really not sure how they managed to sour me on the entire styles the first time around.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Looks like you already did your IMA post anyway, that's what I get for leaving the thread open my whole time reading and not refreshing it when I finished.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","user":"Sith_Happens","date":". 05-04-2018, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T19:28:18-07:00","id":1215322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1215314#post1215314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually forget I said anything, I just reread all the IMAs and there's only a handful of Charms between all five that do the thing I'm talking about. As blatantly as they may do it (Air Dragon's Sight and Stone Dragon's Skin being by far the worst offenders, especially the former) I'm really not sure how they managed to sour me on the entire styles the first time around.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Looks like you already did your IMA post anyway, that's what I get for leaving the thread open my whole time reading and not refreshing it when I finished.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well you weren\u2019t wrong that the effects tend to be less mechanically devastating than the masterykeyworded ones, especially the more simple and directly comparable ones. Honestly even the less directly comparable ones simply aren\u2019t as powerful. I\u2019ve seen Solars kill an entire battle group of blood apes and a second circle demon in one turn with the other mastery keywords styles, and no DB is doing that without like 50 initiative. What they do offer though are diverse effects that you can\u2019t get elsewhere, and good cohesive themes that both work well within themselves and with eachother, again both with one practicioner and many.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T19:56:44-07:00","id":1215326,"title":"","content":"Personally, I plan to house-rule Mastery and Terrestrial effects into them, probably with DBs having means of evading the Terrestrial keyword","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T20:33:49-07:00","id":1215332,"title":"","content":"You know what I just noticed is <i>really</i> scary? Flowing Water Defense in Crane Form.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1215326#post1215326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I plan to house-rule Mastery and Terrestrial effects into them, probably with DBs having means of evading the Terrestrial keyword</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally if I were to give them Mastery effects I'd just do it the lazy way and apply a chapter-wide &quot;Mastery: you count as being in [Style's Element] Aura whenever that's relevant.&quot; Adding Terrestrial effects, on the other hand, would completely defeat the IMAs' purpose; they're specifically supposed to be a way for DBs to punch above their weight class.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T22:31:20-07:00","id":1215369,"title":"","content":"Since DBs are currently the only ones who use the Terrestrial keyword, having a style with the Terrestrial keyword and then allowing DBs to ignore it seems superfluous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1215259#post1215259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had just made my peace with the idea that Lunar Exalted would no longer be capable of learning Immaculate Martial Arts Charms when I read the rules again and realized that wasn't actually the case.<br /> <br /> You can still have monks who Exalt as Lunars and go on to learn the Immaculate Charms of their Style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and except for their excellency caps, they're just as good as Solar ex-Immaculates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T23:53:40-07:00","id":1215386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1215326#post1215326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I plan to house-rule Mastery and Terrestrial effects into them, probably with DBs having means of evading the Terrestrial keyword</div> </div> </div> </div>I might avoid the terrestrial keyword there. I mean do what you want of course, it's your table, but these charms are not CMA strength that DBs get inexplicable access to despite being much more powerful. I mean you've got like, Tsunami Force Shout, for example. it's 10m, 10i, 1wp, and deals what will amount to threshold successes times the wound penalty, which the style only has one way of raising by past what it normally is, and even then only by 1 except against spirits.<br /> <br /> By contrast Dragon Vortex Attack, same essence requirement, costs 20m, 2wp, but no initiative, close to the same initiative trigger requirements, but has 4 times the area of effect, has generally a harder attack condition to avoid, being an environmental attack, and has a similar effect with more damage and less setup, as well as being able to be combined with allies.<br /> <br /> If we look at the closest analogue in the corebook, I think Dancing Devil Trigger Finger, we see that it has a similar area to Tsunami Force Shout, except that a celestial using it gets to roll their full damage against everyone in the blast, while DBs have to divide up their damage like with Dragon Vortex. Also it's essence requirement is 3 not 5, and it costs 7 less initiative, which is huge as the payment for a decisive attack. To do much damage to a bunch of targets with Tsunami Force Shout you have to stack up quite the penalty on all of them, and then roll decently over their defense threshold using a stamina based attack pool, whereas with Dancing Devil Trigger all you need is initiative, which the game is full of ways to get.<br /> <br /> Now, Tsunami Force Shout does get a lot better when you have a bunch of allies who stack on the wound penalties, teamwork being the DB way after all, but now that's requiring even more setup of decisive attacks from multiple people on multiple targets.<br /> <br /> <br /> Basically what I'm saying here is that these immaculate charms don't really feel like base celestial ones, maybe just DB times 1.25 or something. They get a tiny little kick in some places, but the overall costs, restrictions and power are generally much closer to Terrestrial. Unless maybe the way to avoid the terrestrial keyword is to just be a DB, in which case they'll probably be bad enough for all the other terrestrial exalted to not bother with.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually wow Tsunami Force Shout when used solo requires even more effort than I thought. You need to build up initiative, attack, get a wound penalty, reset to base initiative, and then build up to 20 again, and that's if you just want to hit one target. This is one you should definitely avoid sticking a terrestrial keyword on at least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1215332#post1215332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know what I just noticed is <i>really</i> scary? Flowing Water Defense in Crane Form.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's hilarious,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 05-05-2018, 03:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T03:08:03-07:00","id":1215425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1215314#post1215314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually forget I said anything, I just reread all the IMAs and there's only a handful of Charms between all five that do the thing I'm talking about. As blatantly as they may do it (Air Dragon's Sight and Stone Dragon's Skin being by far the worst offenders, especially the former)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ...Air Dragon's Sight can get rid of 4 points of penalties to your defense for 1m without any effort being required on your part.<br /> <br /> But wait, there's more!<br /> <br /> Since it completely shuts down surprise attacks, it even negates effects that fuck around with increasing surprise penalties, like Mistweaver's Death in the Mist or Ebon Shadow's Shadow-Stepping Motion (effectively making it +4 Defense for 1m 1i in that circumstance).<br /> <br /> Not only that, you can also pump up Perception, allowing it to negate 3 points of onslaught. How often do you face more than four incoming attacks in a single round?<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, and there's the Aura bonus for Dragon-Blooded practicioners, making sure that they can take a full invincible flurry to the face and still suffer no onslaught. For Dragon-Blooded, ADS is actually the best argument for the existence of the Martial Artist merit, because otherwise it'd be a no-brainer for 2 ability dots and a Charm on <i>any</i> character who depends on Evasion. (And I'd still dip for it on any martial artist who uses Evasion to defend, like a DPC or Black Claw practicioner.) The extent to which it outclasses native Charms is not even funny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T05:30:07-07:00","id":1215452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1215369#post1215369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, and except for their excellency caps, they're just as good as Solar ex-Immaculates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well...<br /> <br /> Solar Dawn Castes can have Supernal Martial Arts, any Solar can favor all of the unlimited number of Martial Arts Abilities and the Charms derived from them, Solars are resonant with jade artifacts which can form Evocations with Immaculate Charms...<br /> <br /> Solars still have advantages with Immaculate Styles that Lunars do not, so it's a bit early to say Lunars are just as good at them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T05:53:04-07:00","id":1215456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1215332#post1215332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adding Terrestrial effects, on the other hand, would completely defeat the IMAs' purpose; they're specifically supposed to be a way for DBs to punch above their weight class.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOh but we couldn't possibly have that; not with the special class of martial arts designed specifically to resonate with the Terrestrial Exalted. Why, if Solars don't get Mastery effects in every single Martial Art (as opposed to every single one of them barring five), why, the integrity of the idea that they have a special capacity for the Martial Arts just collapses entirely. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T15:21:59-07:00","id":1215606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1215332#post1215332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally if I were to give them Mastery effects I'd just do it the lazy way and apply a chapter-wide &quot;Mastery: you count as being in [Style's Element] Aura whenever that's relevant.&quot; Adding Terrestrial effects, on the other hand, would completely defeat the IMAs' purpose; they're specifically supposed to be a way for DBs to punch above their weight class.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, not interested in having Solars, Sidereals, and so on get involved with Aura mechanics. From the beginning, I wanted the dynamic to be that Solars perform better at the techniques, like every other martial art, while DBs benefited extra from them because of especial synergies with their charmset. Having the IMA involve DB-specific elemental mechanics is a good way to do that (though Ideally I'd probably tune it up to be slightly more beneficial for DBs. Maybe add some other things each style can do while in aura or by spending aura).<br /> <br /> As for Terrestrial, I hadn't thought too deep about it, other than I wanted other Exalted that usually use the keyword to have access to the styles, while still making it more useful to DBs. The whole &quot;spend aura to ignore the Terrestrial keyword on ALL Martial Arts&quot; is possibly enough, though.<br /> <br /> Anyway, If there is interest about IMA from my group and I actually start writing the house rules I'll post my progress in another thread, as my house rules don't really have anything to do with the subject at hand for the forum in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T16:22:15-07:00","id":1215620,"title":"","content":"I see no reason why a style built by an exalt type that is even more skilled at martial arts then solars from the ground up specifically to be used by a particular type of exalted should perform better in the hands of a solar then it does that exalt type. Sidereal are better at it then solars and they are the ones that made them after all, not the dragon blooded. Hell, they probably specifically went out of their way to make sure solars wouldn't be better at it for PR reasons (can't have the vile anathema using the holy martial arts better then immaculate monks).<br /> <br /> Going to say they automatically qualify as a descendant of whatever bloodline an heirloom artifact belongs to if they manage to steal one as well?<br /> <br /> Edit: Hmm, that sounded less harsh in my head for some reason. Not sure how to reword though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 05-05-2018, 08:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T06:19:37-07:00","id":1215753,"title":"","content":"Nobody is more skilled at an Ability than a Solar.<br /> <br /> Sidereals have a special connection with MAs, and have Sidereal MAs, but it was mentioned that they don't have unlimited access to Mastery, as Solars do. So they are not better than Solars at MA. If you get a Solar Tiger Stylist and a Sidereal Tiger Stylist with the same Charms who is better at Tiger Style?<br /> <br /> Of course this could change, but it would be a bad change. Just as I find it bad for IMAs not having Mastery.<br /> <br /> Creating a human skill that a Solar can't master is like trying to keep light from passing through an open window.<br /> <br /> They will naturally conquer it, and you will look like a fool for trying. How do you make a skill for humans to use that at the same time exclude human genius, excellence and brilliance from interacting with, and improving, it?<br /> <br /> It is a contrived idea.<br /> <br /> When all the discussion on this was going on, I said that I was all for the IMAs getting boosts because of some interaction with DB nature, something external to the mastery of a skill, and I find the Aura mechanic great in it's implementation of that. I like how it present throughout the DB Charmset. I really like that the IMAs make use of it.<br /> <br /> I just believe they should also have Mastery effects.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T06:25:29-07:00","id":1215756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1215753#post1215753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody is more skilled at an Ability than a Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>And nobody is more elemental than the Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> The Immaculate Martial Arts are Styles as much about conjuring and manipulating elemental Essence as they are about physical, bodily combat. A Dragon-Blood can summon forth their own elemental Essence to meet the demands of those Charms, just as they can learn Elemental Sheath in order to learn Sea's Verdict's &quot;From The Depths&quot; Evocation and all of the powerful Evocations that follow after it.<br /> <br /> Solars have no inner elemental Essence to meet those needs. They can't conjure elemental stunts with a single mote, just like they can't shapeshift.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T06:44:52-07:00","id":1215761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1215756#post1215756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And nobody is more elemental than the Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> The Immaculate Martial Arts are Styles as much about conjuring and manipulating elemental Essence as they are about physical, bodily combat. A Dragon-Blood can summon forth their own elemental Essence to meet the demands of those Charms, just as they can learn Elemental Sheath in order to learn Sea's Verdict's &quot;From The Depths&quot; Evocation and all of the powerful Evocations that follow after it.<br /> <br /> Solars have no inner elemental Essence to meet those needs. They can't conjure elemental stunts with a single mote, just like they can't shapeshift.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that is what Aura represents? Like I said many times before, I have no problem in having a mechanic that is external to Ability mastering give DBs bonus on using it. That is not a problem.<br /> <br /> To me, the whole pretense of creating a human skill that the infinite masters of human ability and potential cannot master and improve on is silly. No one, specially no other Exalt, should be able to curb the heights of skill a Solar may achieve. Those heights are unfathomable to them, and even to the Solars themselves.<br /> <br /> Humans can still learn the IMA Abilities. So they are still expressions of the human potential, and no matter what anything in the setting tried to do, Solar excellence should have shined through.<br /> <br /> It is like saying that the person who created the light bulb could have created it in such a way as to make it impossible for it to shine light on something specific. It is just against the laws of reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T06:45:52-07:00","id":1215762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1215753#post1215753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody is more skilled at an Ability than a Solar.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bUse an Excellency with it, then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Those heights are unfathomable to them, and even to the Solars themselves.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> And then they slayed the Jabberwocky and saved Narnia.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T06:52:44-07:00","id":1215766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1215762#post1215762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bUse an Excellency with it, then.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And then they slayed the Jabberwocky and saved Narnia.[/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR][/LEFT]</div> </div> </div> </div>You care to counter argue or do you just want to be catty?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T07:11:44-07:00","id":1215773,"title":"","content":"All Solars have a better Excellency than Dragon-Blooded, and it's an Excellency they get <i>for free</i> for every single Martial Art Ability if they favor the Ability or learn at least one Charm of the Style.<br /> <br /> Any Dawn Caste can choose Martial Arts as their Supernal Ability, allowing them to achieve the absolute heights of multiple Styles long before they achieve Essence 5.<br /> <br /> Solar Exalted can supplement their Martial Arts with Solar Athletics, Solar Awareness, Solar Brawl, Solar Dodge, Solar Resistance...<br /> <br /> <br /> Solars have so many advantages that it's wrong to say that the Dragon-Blooded are better at the Immaculate Martial Arts than Solars. It's instead more accurate to say that the Dragon-Blooded are better at expressing the elemental power of the Immaculate Martial Arts, by using elemental Auras that Solar Exalted do not have, whereas Solar Exalted are better at using those same Styles to WIN FIGHTS.<br /> <br /> <br /> If Lunar Exalted are going to be able to combine Attribute Charms with Martial Arts Charms, would that make them better at &quot;Celestial&quot; Martial Arts Style than Sidereals? No, it will simply mean that Lunars have a different set of advantages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 05-06-2018, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T07:18:58-07:00","id":1215774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1215773#post1215773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All Solars have a better Excellency than Dragon-Blooded, and it's an Excellency they get <i>for free</i> for every single Martial Art Ability if they favor the Ability or learn at least one Charm of the Style.<br /> <br /> Any Solar can choose Martial Arts as their Supernal Ability, allowing them to achieve the absolute heights of multiple Styles long before they achieve Essence 5.<br /> <br /> Solar Exalted can supplement their Martial Arts with Solar Athletics, Solar Awareness, Solar Brawl, Solar Dodge, Solar Resistance...<br /> <br /> <br /> Solars have so many advantages that it's wrong to say that the Dragon-Blooded are better at the Immaculate Martial Arts than Solars. It's instead more accurate to say that the Dragon-Blooded are better at expressing the elemental power of the Immaculate Martial Arts, by using elemental Auras that Solar Exalted do not have, whereas Solar Exalted are better at using those same Styles to WIN FIGHTS.<br /> <br /> <br /> If Lunar Exalted are going to be able to combine Attribute Charms with Martial Arts Charms, would that make them better at &quot;Celestial&quot; Martial Arts Style than Sidereals? No, it will simply mean that Lunars have a different set of advantages.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with all of this.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Mastery: This keyword denotes Charms that have a<br /> greater effect when used by those Exalted who are masters<br /> of mortal Abilities: the Solar and Abyssal Exalted. The<br /> Sidereal Exalted, peerless masters of the martial arts, have<br /> their own esoteric methods for accessing these effects.<br /> <br /> IMAs are mortal Abilities.<br /> <br /> I'm saying IMAs should be different just by use of Aura mechanics, not by lack of Mastery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T07:19:16-07:00","id":1215775,"title":"","content":"Reminder that, as nice as some of the IMAs' &quot;While in [Element] Aura&quot; effects are (they tend to look suspiciously like &quot;Mastery but for DBs,&quot; in fact), Solars' higher dice caps and bigger mote pools are probably still worth more on the whole. Especially the mote pools because HOT DAMN do these styles get expensive. So it's not that Solars aren't the best at IMAs, it's just that the gap's a lot smaller than usual.<br /> <br /> (That said, I'd personally still at least <i>consider</i> giving Mastery boosts to those few specific IMA Charms I discussed earlier that will otherwise be legitimately painful for Solar players to have to buy, but those are special cases.)<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ebon Shadow'ed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T07:44:03-07:00","id":1215787,"title":"","content":"To my eye, there are two basic foundations for getting really hung up on there being this small, very specific collection of styles that lack Mastery and Terrestrial keywords. One is getting extremely hung up on the minutia of the made-up metaphysics of the setting being... I won't even say consistent, because actual physical laws don't have that level of consistency... completely inflexible. The other is getting extremely hung up on how great the Solars are; like, when it's going beyond them being the mightiest of the Exalted and into the heights of their power being beyond comprehension (which... no, I can pretty easily comprehend the things marked out by the Essence 5 Charms) and an actual law of reality.<br /> <br /> I find both things to be ridiculous as a basis for assessing the game. It's getting <i>faaaar</i> too immersed into something, beyond the point where it serves as something useful for telling interesting stories and playing fun games.<br /> <br /> \u200bI could contrive an explanation for why the Immaculate Styles work as they do within that paradigm, but I hardly see it as being worth the effort, because it's not a premise I accept, and I regard it as a losing proposition anyway.<br /> <br /> \u200bI find the most important thing to be metatextual, and metatextually, the Immaculate Styles have always held a special place in system and setting in association with the Dragon Blooded. A place that is rather unique in how the game approaches martial arts, and the characteristics given to the Dragon Blooded as reigning Exalted of the setting, both in terms of the forces that they need to fight and the idea of them having an institutionally established monastic order.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo when the martial arts are redesigned from the ground up to flatten Terrestrial and Celestial styles into one plane, with variations for practitioners represented by keywords, I find the weight of that pedigree for how these particular Exalted associate with these particular styles to take precedence, such that it would be undermined by saying &quot;Solars get better use out of them as well&quot;. I'm often sceptical of arguments regarding crossover between Solars and other types as constituting a demand for Solars to get everybody else's cool toys, but I would not dispute somebody seeing that there.<br /> <br /> \u200bI don't find it to be a precedent for how anybody else approaches the martial arts, or any other form of power in the setting, because nothing else has ever had the particular unique relationship that Dragon Blooded have to those five styles.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe only argument that I ever saw that felt like it had any credibility was that lacking Mastery would make an Immaculate Dragon Style an inferior combat choice to other martial arts, or their own Charms, and I find the Charms that have actually been written to sufficiently discredit that. Where else are you getting combat Charms that allow you to make a single attack roll against an indefinite number of opponents and apply a flat Initiative division as damage to all of them? Or various other neat and powerful things that the actual Styles can do? They seem like a reasonable selection compared against the awesome fighting monstrosity that is Black Claw Style.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm actually given to wonder if the Immaculate Styles make up for their lack of such keywords by being generally stronger than most styles. That would strike me as the basis for why people that would be constrained by the Terrestrial keyword being unable to learn them <i>at all</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T08:29:14-07:00","id":1215800,"title":"","content":"In-setting, most dragon blooded never make it to essence 5, and so most dragon blooded will never master the capstones of the dragon styles. <br /> <br /> A dawn can do that at essence 1. Hell, a dawn could do that at chargen. There are only 12 charms in a style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T09:13:42-07:00","id":1215820,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> <br /> <br /> \u200bI don't really get the attitude towards discussing this...<br /> <br /> Why people must be somehow hung up on something to feel the need to house rule? Or is it only a hang up because you feel this specific thing is fine as is? Or do you think the game should be found perfect on every aspect for everyone and any house rule is rooted in an unreasonable lack of satisfaction with something?<br /> <br /> Is this not a place to care and nerd out about game rules and made up metaphsysics without being judged by it? <br /> <br /> If it isn't, what the hell is this place?<br /> <br /> And really? Criticizing how immersed into something people are? That is something... Could you tell, then, what areas of the game experience are fine to plunge into, and what depths of immersion aren't too much?<br /> <br /> If you think that someone a mortal who codified surgery practices, eventually fathomed that someone who learned the same things as him could eventually become so good at it that he could slap a severed eye into an eye socket and have it work perfectly?<br /> <br /> If you think you (or anyone) are truly capable of imagining every way any Solar ever would come up with to express their greatness through any Ability, Idon't know if I pity you for thinking so highly of yourself, or envy you for being one of the greatest creative and imaginative minds ever.<br /> <br /> Why are you trying to mock or dismiss people for buying into what the game proposes, in a game that is specifically about buy in?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1215787#post1215787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI'm actually given to wonder if the Immaculate Styles make up for their lack of such keywords by being generally stronger than most styles. That would strike me as the basis for why people that would be constrained by the Terrestrial keyword being unable to learn them <i>at all</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interestingly enough, this was one of the ways I said I wouldn't mind not having Mastery in IMAs, way back when we didn't even know much about IMAs. If mortals were incapable of learning it, then it wouldn't be a mortal human Ability, and therefore outside Solar scope.<br /> <br /> But this isn't the case, which I don't know if you are saying it is in your statement or if you're suggesting it could be. But as it stands anyone can learn Martial Arts (IMA). Those bound by the Terrestrial Keyword can't learn IMA Charms, the Ability itself, though is a-ok to learn.<br /> <br /> The same way if in the Lunar book there was a MA called World Constrictor Style, which required constricting limbs/body to practice, which would make it something a basic mortal human being is incapable of learning, I wouldn't care if there was no Mastery for it.<br /> <br /> But if its a mortal Ability, I feel Solar awesomeness should be applied to it. Hang me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T09:29:29-07:00","id":1215827,"title":"","content":"You are the one hung up, and we are reacting against you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T09:39:26-07:00","id":1215831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1215452#post1215452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well...<br /> <br /> Solar Dawn Castes can have Supernal Martial Arts, any Solar can favor all of the unlimited number of Martial Arts Abilities and the Charms derived from them, Solars are resonant with jade artifacts which can form Evocations with Immaculate Charms...<br /> <br /> Solars still have advantages with Immaculate Styles that Lunars do not, so it's a bit early to say Lunars are just as good at them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tbh, I forgot about Supernal MA and the fact that Lunars can't favour MA. So you're right.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, in terms of IMA being a mortal ability...<br /> Well, a mortal can learn to fight with a style that can use giant tetsubos or fists, and is compatible with armour. But he can't cover himself in rock skin, or paralyse people, or cause earthquakes. A mortal can learn to fight with his fists or chakrams, but not how to blow a tornoda.<br /> <br /> One could argue that a mortal Tiger stylist can't get tiger-skin, but my point is that the IMA are much more overtly magical than stuff like Snake Style or Single Pulse, and so what the mortal can do is more different from what the Exalt can do.<br /> <br /> <br /> On an unrelated matter, I'm not sure where to put this, but it occurred to me today that a lot of DB charms manipulate passions and emotions, but that sometimes requires people to already be emotional. And then I remembered that the Red Jade powerbow lets you shoot emotions into people, which you could then use your DB Presence and Socialise charms to manipulate. That's a cool little combo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-06-2018, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T10:07:39-07:00","id":1215837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1215827#post1215827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are the one hung up, and we are reacting against you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that for me?<br /> <br /> I think the DB book is awesome. I won't go to the effort of homebrewing any aspect of IMAs, I think they are fine. I'm not a Solar Supremacist, I've actually argued for an increase in power and options for a few DB Charms.<br /> <br /> But if we are in game forum discussing game minutiae, and I feel like rambling about made up metaphysics, am I not in an appropriate place to do this?<br /> <br /> I was only defending someone's right to homebrew whatever he wants without being accused of being wrong for caring about the wrong stuff.<br /> <br /> Why do you invest words in labeling peoples thoughts and feelings, instead of arguing their ideas, or if you see you will not change their minds, or do not care about them, just not engage?<br /> <br /> Isn't that a better option than to be insulting? Or must you always win and/or have some kind of last word?<br /> <br /> Why are you trying to paint me like an unreasonable person with a grudge? Because you don't like what I think about the made up metaphysics? Isn't that a bit petty?<br /> <br /> Who is hung up about what here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T10:15:27-07:00","id":1215841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1215831#post1215831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> <br /> Anyhow, in terms of IMA being a mortal ability...<br /> Well, a mortal can learn to fight with a style that can use giant tetsubos or fists, and is compatible with armour. But he can't cover himself in rock skin, or paralyse people, or cause earthquakes. A mortal can learn to fight with his fists or chakrams, but not how to blow a tornoda.<br /> <br /> One could argue that a mortal Tiger stylist can't get tiger-skin, but my point is that the IMA are much more overtly magical than stuff like Snake Style or Single Pulse, and so what the mortal can do is more different from what the Exalt can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can we examine this a bit more?<br /> <br /> How are IMAs more overtly magical than turning into Gazelle Carp, making people's own shadow murder, filling them with golden light that kills Bad Things<sup>TM</sup>, or have them repent for their sins or burn in hell?<br /> <br /> I think, as far as esoteric and magical things go, IMAs are pretty middle ground.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1215831#post1215831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On an unrelated matter, I'm not sure where to put this, but it occurred to me today that a lot of DB charms manipulate passions and emotions, but that sometimes requires people to already be emotional. And then I remembered that the Red Jade powerbow lets you shoot emotions into people, which you could then use your DB Presence and Socialise charms to manipulate. That's a cool little combo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh that is cool, will check it out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T11:09:49-07:00","id":1215859,"title":"","content":"(don't have book yet)<br /> <br /> Let's say Solars can learn IMA, but can't use the aura-related effects. &quot;Okay, now you force your wood anima into your lungs to breath out poison. Wait what?&quot; How would folks feel about your Twilight Crafter building artifacts to emulate the Aura?<br /> Weirding Module for Air, rockin jade armor for earth, web shooters for wood, something flamey for fire, and uh... something wetty for water.<br /> <br /> Reminds me of a bit from the last Taltos book I was reading. &quot;We are going to use sorcery to power the witchcraft which will emulate sorcery to create a psychic effect.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2678-spoonr","name":"SpoonR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2678_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T11:14:54-07:00","id":1215860,"title":"","content":"I was really enjoying this thread before it ended up being about how Solars have to overshadow other people in their own specialties like we're back in 2e or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5771-krata-lightblade","name":"Krata Lightblade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5771_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T12:36:59-07:00","id":1215872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1215753#post1215753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody is more skilled at an Ability than a Solar.<br /> <br /> <b>Sidereals have a special connection with MAs, and have Sidereal MAs, but it was mentioned that they don't have unlimited access to Mastery, as Solars do. So they are not better than Solars at MA. If you get a Solar Tiger Stylist and a Sidereal Tiger Stylist with the same Charms who is better at Tiger Style?</b><br /> <br /> Of course this could change, but it would be a bad change. Just as I find it bad for IMAs not having Mastery.<br /> <br /> Creating a human skill that a Solar can't master is like trying to keep light from passing through an open window.<br /> <br /> They will naturally conquer it, and you will look like a fool for trying. How do you make a skill for humans to use that at the same time exclude human genius, excellence and brilliance from interacting with, and improving, it?<br /> <br /> It is a contrived idea.<br /> <br /> When all the discussion on this was going on, I said that I was all for the IMAs getting boosts because of some interaction with DB nature, something external to the mastery of a skill, and I find the Aura mechanic great in it's implementation of that. I like how it present throughout the DB Charmset. I really like that the IMAs make use of it.<br /> <br /> I just believe they should also have Mastery effects.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No such thing was mentioned, it was said they can access them for a reason that wasn't 'they are the best at using ability based powers in general' while making to sure to reiterate they are <i>peerless</i> in the martial arts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T12:48:44-07:00","id":1215874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1215872#post1215872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No such thing was mentioned, it was said they can access them for a reason that wasn't 'they are the best at using ability based powers in general' while making to sure to reiterate they are <i>peerless</i> in the martial arts.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem very sure of what I read somewhere in a discussion at least 3-4 years ago. <br /> <br /> You have those quotes in hand or something?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T13:07:35-07:00","id":1215876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1215874#post1215874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You seem very sure of what I read somewhere in a discussion at least 3-4 years ago.<br /> <br /> You have those quotes in hand or something?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 Mastery: This keyword denotes Charms that have a<br /> greater effect when used by those Exalted who are masters<br /> of mortal Abilities: the Solar and Abyssal Exalted. The<br /> Sidereal Exalted, peerless masters of the martial arts, have<br /> their own esoteric methods for accessing these effects. </div> </div> </div>He's basically reading the keyword back to you. It's saying the Exalts who are masters of mortal ability (Solars and Abyssals) get Mastery effects. it also mentions that the Sidereals, who are not masters of mortal ability like Solars and Abyssals, also get Mastery effects, because they are peerless masters of Martial Arts specifically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Life before Death, Strength before Weakness, Journey before Destination.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">&quot;I will protect those who cannot protect themselves&quot;</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4172-marros56","name":"Marros56","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4172_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T14:19:23-07:00","id":1215894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1215874#post1215874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You seem very sure of what I read somewhere in a discussion at least 3-4 years ago.<br /> <br /> You have those quotes in hand or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>You already quoted the relevant material when you posted the part of the core that explains mastery. Sidereal exalted are peerless masters of martial arts that also get mastery effects despite not in general being the best at ability based charms because in that one particular thing they are super awesome specialists. Its not like it is the only things solars aren't the best at, they can't access 3rd circle necromancy at all for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T14:21:18-07:00","id":1215895,"title":"","content":"\u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar988_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"988\" data-vbnamecard=\"988\">Mizu</a> , <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4172-marros56\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4172_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4172\" data-vbnamecard=\"4172\">Marros56</a> <br /> <br /> \u200bNo, you are reading more into that than what it says.<br /> <br /> It says they have esoteric methods to access that level of power. No where does it say they have permanent access to Mastery.<br /> <br /> This was discussed some time ago, people even speculated if the Sutras were going to be that esoteric way, or maybe they get Mastery if they are in the style's form, or if they are dressed all in pink. You know, esoteric methods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T14:29:03-07:00","id":1215897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1215894#post1215894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You already quoted the relevant material when you posted the part of the core that explains mastery. Sidereal exalted are peerless masters of martial arts that also get mastery effects despite not in general being the best at ability based charms because in that one particular thing they are super awesome specialists. Its not like it is the only things solars aren't the best at, they can't access 3rd circle necromancy at all for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would I care if Solars are not best at everything? Necromancy is not a mortal human Ability, and is not called out on the book as being a thing Solars are the best at.<br /> <br /> And Sidereals could have Mastery and the Sutra and Elder Sutra, to make them even more awesome at Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> My argument is that as an expression of skill, no one should be better than Solars. If they, because of factors external to expression of skill, have an end result better than Solars, I couldn't care less.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T14:31:23-07:00","id":1215899,"title":"","content":"You are the one reading too much into flavor text to make them sound mysterious. Do you really think the people who have to dumb down SMA for solars to understand it are going to have to jump through hoops for the mastery effects of 'lesser' martial arts that lesser martial artists get automatically?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T14:43:10-07:00","id":1215901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1215899#post1215899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are the one reading too much into flavor text to make them sound mysterious. Do you really think the people who have to dumb down SMA for solars to understand it are going to have to jump through hoops for the mastery effects of 'lesser' martial arts that lesser martial artists get automatically?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you call teaching something dumbing down?<br /> <br /> This was a real discussion, and if memory is not failing me, Holden had said that Sidereals would have to go through some hoops to get Mastery out of the Charm activation.<br /> <br /> Are you really presuming to know how the Devs will implement Martial Arts for Sidereals? The Devs themselves probably don't know... And you say I'm the one assuming things?<br /> <br /> I feel there is an animus towards Solars and people who enjoy them for what they are.<br /> <br /> I feel like I'm in middle school and people are mocking me for liking the main character of the game, instead of the supercool side ones.<br /> <br /> And I'm trying to tell them that, in fact, I like all characters, I just happen to have certain thoughts about this specific thing about the main one, and they're going &quot;HAHA SOLAR FANBOY!!!! GET OUTTA HERE WITH YOUR SUCKING UP TO THOSE MARY SUES!!!!&quot;.<br /> <br /> Tone it down a bit, will ya?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T14:55:54-07:00","id":1215905,"title":"","content":"You are right, sorry. Not sure why I keep getting heated over this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T15:05:59-07:00","id":1215907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpoonR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1215859#post1215859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(don't have book yet)<br /> <br /> Let's say Solars can learn IMA, but can't use the aura-related effects. &quot;Okay, now you force your wood anima into your lungs to breath out poison. Wait what?&quot; How would folks feel about your Twilight Crafter building artifacts to emulate the Aura?<br /> Weirding Module for Air, rockin jade armor for earth, web shooters for wood, something flamey for fire, and uh... something wetty for water.<br /> <br /> Reminds me of a bit from the last Taltos book I was reading. &quot;We are going to use sorcery to power the witchcraft which will emulate sorcery to create a psychic effect.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyone can learn IMA, even mortals. What is restricted is the learning of Charms, from the Kickstarter Manuscript:<br /> <br /> &quot;The Immaculate styles are intensely demanding. While anyone can learn the fundamentals of the styles, their Charms can only be learned by the Dragon-Blooded and by other martial artists that aren\u2019t restricted by the Terrestrial keyword, such as Solars and Sidereals.&quot;<br /> <br /> So basically,only some hypothetical Terrestrial Exalts (some speculate Liminals), or hypothetical Celestial (because I think, and I may be wrong, all current Celestials aren't bound by that keyword.) will be restricted from learning the Charms.<br /> <br /> I think Aura is an exclusive DB thing, and I wouldn't allow that kind of thing in a table I ran. Not that it is an inherently bad idea, it just doesn't jive well for me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T15:10:32-07:00","id":1215909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1215905#post1215905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are right, sorry. Not sure why I keep getting heated over this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apology accepted friend. Thank you for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T18:47:17-07:00","id":1215955,"title":"","content":"Um, wow okay. So just quickly before we get going I'll have my last word on this I think. You can do whatever you want at your table, you can make Solars less powerful than DBs if you like, it's all good. In my opinion though, even if you give the immaculate styles mastery, it shouldn't be just giving them aura, and you shouldn't give them the terrestrial keyword. Apart from a few notable exceptions the powers have a very DB feel with regards to their costs and restrictions, so it isn't really warranted.<br /> <br /> As for Aura, it's like if there was a Dragon King MA that made heavy use of spinning tail attacks and stuff and the Mastery keyword just gave Solars the benefit of having a tail. Or a Lunar MA that called out if you can shapeshift you gain the ability to add bonus evasion as you reflexively shrink your body or something. It's a tool that Solars just don't have access to. If you do it, I'd recommend picking some of the weaker charms and maybe removing some cost or restrictions, or adding a bit of damage or something. That way they can still be technically better at the style, without having this weird thing where they're somehow vanishing into the wind essence of their own anima when they don't...have...that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krata Lightblade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1215860#post1215860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was really enjoying this thread before it ended up being about how Solars have to overshadow other people in their own specialties like we're back in 2e or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Too right you are.<br /> <br /> *Crosses arms with the mudra of Earth's Pillar*<br /> Strength of Stone Technique!<br /> *Breaks the cross into the stance of the Stone Shattering Root*<br /> Grandmother Oak Exertion!<br /> *Drops to a knee sending out tremors and grabbing the thread by its solid iron axle*<br /> Mountain Toppling Method!<br /> *Draws essence from Pasiap's infinite strength, lifting the thread high in the air and then slamming it back onto the rails*<br /> Unshakable mountain spine!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sorcery</b><br /> <br /> Sorcery! How on earth could sorcery be different for DBs and Solars? It's the same initiations, the same spells, the same rituals. Even the ones in the DB book like the Heptagram initiation aren't DB exclusive at all. So what's the diff? Well actually a lot. The difference here is mostly in the charm support for sorcerous spells.<br /> <br /> Let's start with Solars. Their biggest charm is Spirit-Drawing Oculus. It costs 1wp and all your anima, and it lets you roll a full, free, (int+occult) excellency to gather sorcerous motes reflexively. Which if you're optomized is 21 dice, and over 10 motes on average, stunt it for another 1-2. That, combined with another charm that lets you use your full excellency for free with a reset condition, PLUS shaping rituals, means that you can pull like 20-25 motes into a spell pretty easily. With spells that are Celestial circle or Solar circle this is a big deal, a spell that would be guaranteed for other exalted to take 2-3 turns with, Solars can do it in one.<br /> <br /> The thing is though, for spells of the terrestrial circle, particularly ones that you'd want to cast in combat, it's pretty overkill. Most of those are 10-15 motes, which a full excellency with a stunt and a shaping ritual gets really close to anyway. It's good if you absolutely must ensure that you get that spell of this turn, or if you're not actually a super optimized sorcerer and kind of need it to take less than 2 turns to shape something up.<br /> <br /> There's a few other charms but they're more minor.<br /> <br /> Now as to DBs, the first charm they have to help out all the time is Hidden Secrets Whisper, AKA the DB occult excellency! For each 10 on the roll you reroll a non-1 failed die. It's not much, and a lot of the time it won't help you at all, but there's a few times out there where it will explode your already great roll. Then there's two sorcery specific charms, the first is one that protects you while you shape. Solars have a similar effect with their Twilight anima, but instead of just adding hardness like the twilight anima, this one adds defense and hardness, and in air aura it's even non-charm.<br /> <br /> it's solid and it helps, but the big one here is Dragon Sorcerer Puissance. Whenever you shape an elemental spell you get a bonus mote, or 3 if you're in that element's aura. Rather than the Solar one, which is built to get off huge expensive spells fast and infrequently, this one is built to help you consistently smash out elemental spells. Since it's free and permanent, it makes it much easier to be a battle sorcerer, saving you motes and not wasting precious reset condition spells like the Solars do.<br /> <br /> Let's just say, for example, you're a fire aspect. You're dual wielding a sword and a hand that's trying to cast Flight of the Brilliant Raptor. You leap into battle using a fire aspected athletics charm, putting you in fire aura already. It's not super reliable, but with the bonus from your excellency, a stunt and a shaping ritual you can pretty reliably crack of a combat spell that's fire aspected every turn while using your defend other tree in melee to contribute even further to combat.<br /> <br /> I know it sounds like I'm making a huge deal out of nothing but on a full excellency roll you're actually getting more sorcerous motes than a Solar for slightly over half what they're spending on their excellency. I'd call that pretty impressive myself.<br /> <br /> <br /> So how does this affect how you play your sorcerer? Firstly you don't really have to worry about it until essence 3 anyway, so before that just do whatever you want, but maybe plan ahead. After that though you're going to want to pick spells that align with your elemental aura, or pick charms that let you easily slip into the aura you want for the spells you're going to cast. Like maybe you want to snag one of those shiny resistance charms that gives you bonus soak, always handy, so that you can slip into earth arua for Obsidian Butterflies.<br /> <br /> There's also one other key difference in how the two play, and that's because they get different things out of their charmsets. Solars for example don't really get effects like the Wind Carried Words that DBs get, so they're getting a slight benefit out of sorcery for being able to do that at all. Conversely there's stuff like Silent Words of Deams and Nightmares, that lets you instill something into a person without them even realizing what you've done, which is something Solar charms can do, but DBs have trouble with.<br /> <br /> Anyway, that's gone on long enough about sorcery, next time I'll be talking about evocations and how they are, I think, actually much better for DBs than Solars, and also DB chargen and what you want to look for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T22:20:19-07:00","id":1215988,"title":"","content":"You know what? Lets just keep this momentum going!<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations</b><br /> <br /> Evocations are another one where the difference is big and you might think it's zero, or just slightly lower for DBs because smaller dice caps and resonance list. Since, apart from the evocations locked behind Solar charms there doesn't really appear to be anything different. This one comes down to two things. One is heirloom items, which is pretty minor, but worth mentioning. Heirloom items are items from the DB corebook that have bonus unlocks for a particular bloodline. Like for example if attuning to an artifact grants you that artifact's first evocation, being of the right bloodline actually grants you the first two! Which is very helpful.<br /> <br /> The other is that DBs start at essence 2, which is massive. Most artifacts with evocations have like 1, maybe 2 at essence 1, but the ones I've seen really take off at essence 2. Spring Razor has 1-1-2-2-3 for it's essence requirements, Volcano Cutter goes 1-1-2-2-3-4, Faith's Pillar goes 1-1-2-2-2-3, you get the idea. When you start at essence 2 instead of 1, you go from just dipping your toe into the evocation tree, to usually grabbing more than half of it and really getting it's charm tree online. This means that you can basically take one of the more fighting focused evocations and almost replace your combat tree with what it has, or at least seriously augment it with it's special abilities.<br /> <br /> So like if you get Heavenly Typhoon, the chakram, you can take the first four evocations, the first you get for free, second for free if you're a Ledaal. That gives you a marking ability for bonus withering damage, an occult charm booster, a withering counter attack, and a decisive accuracy/damage booster. That's a foundation for, and almost a complete, little combat suite there. If you've got just a little Air Dragon Style, or Thrown, that's more than you need really.<br /> <br /> Yeah, so it's getting late, but just looking through the artifacts I have access to it really benefits a character being able to take these evocations off of chargen. The heirloom items that enhance DB charms specifically, and unlock even greater power with the correct bloodline means they are something that you're almost always going to want, if you can work it into your character, and makes it well well worth the artifact cost.<br /> <br /> Speaking of chargen, that's just the first thing that you're going to want to look at, artifacts can be a big part of your character and style, more on this in the next post about how you might want to pick charms and what you can do there!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T11:36:29-07:00","id":1216237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1215988#post1215988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Speaking of chargen, that's just the first thing that you're going to want to look at, artifacts can be a big part of your character and style, more on this in the next post about how you might want to pick charms and what you can do there!</div> </div> </div> </div>Notepad is ready, sifu","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T11:53:21-07:00","id":1216250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1216237#post1216237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Notepad is ready, sifu</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Seconded.<br /> <br /> I wasn't expecting the posts on Sorcery and Evocations to be as enlightening, if not moreso, than the initial charm posts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T12:43:11-07:00","id":1216264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1215955#post1215955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's just say, for example, you're a fire aspect. You're dual wielding a sword and a hand that's trying to cast Flight of the Brilliant Raptor. You leap into battle using a fire aspected athletics charm, putting you in fire aura already. It's not super reliable, but with the bonus from your excellency, a stunt and a shaping ritual you can pretty reliably crack of a combat spell that's fire aspected every turn while using your defend other tree in melee to contribute even further to combat.<br /> <br /> I know it sounds like I'm making a huge deal out of nothing but on a full excellency roll you're actually getting more sorcerous motes than a Solar for slightly over half what they're spending on their excellency. I'd call that pretty impressive myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I don't have time to go digging through the Ask the Devs thread, I'm pretty sure a while back the devs declared that fire aura was not actual fire. So you wouldn't be able to use it as a source for a shaping ritual on its own. That is if you're talking about the Ifrit Lord's first shaping ritual. Obviously you can use the shaping ritual if there's actual flames around or use another shaping ritual but if what I remember is correct it's not as simple as &quot;Be Fire aspect. Have Ifrit Lord Ritual. Profit&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T12:51:47-07:00","id":1216271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1216264#post1216264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I don't have time to go digging through the Ask the Devs thread, I'm pretty sure a while back the devs declared that fire aura was not actual fire. So you wouldn't be able to use it as a source for a shaping ritual on its own. That is if you're talking about the Ifrit Lord's first shaping ritual. Obviously you can use the shaping ritual if there's actual flames around or use another shaping ritual but if what I remember is correct it's not as simple as &quot;Be Fire aspect. Have Ifrit Lord Ritual. Profit&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Think he means that Dragon Sorcerer Puissance gives you a bonus to sorcerous motes generation if you're in the right Aura for the spell.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T13:08:14-07:00","id":1216276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1216271#post1216271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Think he means that Dragon Sorcerer Puissance gives you a bonus to sorcerous motes generation if you're in the right Aura for the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bingo. At full excellency with a stunt you\u2019ve got 19 dice, with a bonus 5% average from the excellency, so you\u2019re looking at like 10 successes there. If you\u2019re trying to cast Brilliant Raptor and you\u2019re in fire aura, you pick up an extra 3 motes. So then as long as your shaping ritual can give you at least 2, again this is all on average so you might need more or less, you fire that spell off in one turn and you only burned 6 motes and used one active charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T13:16:05-07:00","id":1216280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1216276#post1216276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bingo. At full excellency with a stunt you\u2019ve got 19 dice, with a bonus 5% average from the excellency, so you\u2019re looking at like 10 successes there. If you\u2019re trying to cast Brilliant Raptor and you\u2019re in fire aura, you pick up an extra 3 motes. So then as long as your shaping ritual can give you at least 2, again this is all on average so you might need more or less, you fire that spell off in one turn and you only burned 6 motes and used one active charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>But are you factoring that solars get up to 2 more shaping rituals that also generate SMs in a way that DBs don\u2019t? A solar with 3 shaping rituals can generate 7sm (14sm for control) from one, 3-5 sm from stunt, and more from join battle. I see the charm more inline as a stopgap to help their sm generation that solars gain through more rituals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T13:39:20-07:00","id":1216286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1216280#post1216280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But are you factoring that solars get up to 2 more shaping rituals that also generate SMs in a way that DBs don\u2019t? A solar with 3 shaping rituals can generate 7sm (14sm for control) from one, 3-5 sm from stunt, and more from join battle. I see the charm more inline as a stopgap to help their sm generation that solars gain through more rituals.</div> </div> </div> </div>They gotta hit Essence 5 to get all three shaping rituals. It's usually pretty hard to get motes from more than one simultaneously as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T13:42:29-07:00","id":1216287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1216286#post1216286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They gotta hit Essence 5 to get all three shaping rituals. It's usually pretty hard to get motes from more than one simultaneously as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but the get 2 by essence 3, so my point is mostly that puissance fills the same mechanical space that shaping rituals offer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T14:13:28-07:00","id":1216300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1216287#post1216287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right, but the get 2 by essence 3, so my point is mostly that puissance fills the same mechanical space that shaping rituals offer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, kind of. See, you get shaping rituals for free when you take extra circles of sorcery, but actually you can get them other ways too. For example if a DB crafts the Eye of Agamotto, ahem, Talisman of a Thousand Eyes, he gets a free shaping ritual. In fact you can just gain shaping rituals as an effect of story actions.<br /> <br /> Check the sidebar on page 470, even mortals can do it. So while it\u2019s true that high and very high essence Solars get more for free without additional effort, DBs can in theory work hard and keep up, plus their charm. <br /> <br /> You are 100% right though that it narrows the gap, because when you have like 5 shaping rituals at essence 5 the fact that you don\u2019t have the DB Charm doesn\u2019t matter as much, you can still basically do what they do, and depending on the rituals you can even do it easier for a while. On the other hand that\u2019s like essence 3-5 so it\u2019s a ways off in most games, and I\u2019ll be talking about how drastically different the early game is for DBs in my chargen post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T14:48:51-07:00","id":1216314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1216300#post1216300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, kind of. See, you get shaping rituals for free when you take extra circles of sorcery, but actually you can get them other ways too. For example if a DB crafts the Eye of Agamotto, ahem, Talisman of a Thousand Eyes, he gets a free shaping ritual. In fact you can just gain shaping rituals as an effect of story actions.<br /> <br /> Check the sidebar on page 470, even mortals can do it. So while it\u2019s true that high and very high essence Solars get more for free without additional effort, DBs can in theory work hard and keep up, plus their charm.<br /> <br /> You are 100% right though that it narrows the gap, because when you have like 5 shaping rituals at essence 5 the fact that you don\u2019t have the DB Charm doesn\u2019t matter as much, you can still basically do what they do, and depending on the rituals you can even do it easier for a while. On the other hand that\u2019s like essence 3-5 so it\u2019s a ways off in most games, and I\u2019ll be talking about how drastically different the early game is for DBs in my chargen post.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm almost 100% sure this is not true. Check the sidebar on page 466 for instance. It implies that the <i>only</i> way to gain extra shaping rituals is through unlocking additional circles of sorcery. Recently in the Ask the Devs thread RV specifically called out that you <i>don't </i>get a shaping ritual:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1214888#post1214888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whoops, I specifically meant the case where you're a sorcerer already but forgot to say so. Specifically, the sidebar for crafting a sorcerous artifact like the Talisman says you immediately get one of its shaping rituals as an extra when you finish it, so what about if you find an existing one?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1215116#post1215116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't get a shaping ritual for free, although you can start awakening Evocations from the talisman.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T14:51:46-07:00","id":1216318,"title":"","content":"That question, if you read it again, was about what happens if you find an existing sorcerous artifact; you specifically do get an extra shaping ritual if you make one yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T15:03:28-07:00","id":1216330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1216318#post1216318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That question, if you read it again, was about what happens if you find an existing sorcerous artifact; you specifically do get an extra shaping ritual if you make one yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that the original question about the talisman had the answer that finding it would be a valid initiation into sorcery (thus gaining a free shaping ritual), I maintain my stance, though I have put the question to the devs directly in hopes of a direct yes/no answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T15:13:29-07:00","id":1216335,"title":"","content":"Yeah also just...mortals can do it. The only two things mortals can do that exalted can\u2019t is pay more for the same result, and see why kids love the taste of cinnamon toast crunch.<br /> <br /> Also this is all with the understanding that none of this makes Solars any less than the absolute sorcerer kings of the mystic arts, right? An essence 5 DB can cast Obsidian Butterflies real real good, an essence 5 Solar can destroy a city and blight the land for ten thousand years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T15:18:00-07:00","id":1216336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1216330#post1216330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that the original question about the talisman had the answer that finding it would be a valid initiation into sorcery (thus gaining a free shaping ritual), I maintain my stance, though I have put the question to the devs directly in hopes of a direct yes/no answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both the Crafting Sorcerous Relics side bar and The Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes section make clear that you can have the Talisman and initiate into Sorcery through it, by having claimed it, not necessarily made it.<br /> <br /> What Vance was saying in not getting anything for free is just about finding it. Crafting a level 4 Artifact is not something that can be called free, neither in in-setting resources or in character investment, it costs all the experience to raise the Crafts needed for Crafting Artifacts, the Charms to let you safely make a 4 dot Artifact and a Ambition 1 Celestial Working.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T15:28:55-07:00","id":1216339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1216335#post1216335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and see why kids love the taste of cinnamon toast crunch.</div> </div> </div> </div>The true form of the Great Curse","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T15:33:58-07:00","id":1216341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1216335#post1216335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah also just...mortals can do it. The only two things mortals can do that exalted can\u2019t is pay more for the same result, and see why kids love the taste of cinnamon toast crunch.<br /> <br /> Also this is all with the understanding that none of this makes Solars any less than the absolute sorcerer kings of the mystic arts, right? An essence 5 DB can cast Obsidian Butterflies real real good, an essence 5 Solar can destroy a city and blight the land for ten thousand years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally, I was trying to pushback against the idea that because DBs get a thing Solars don\u2019t it\u2019s not fair (which may be a straw man but still). By pointing out that they don\u2019t need it because they get more free shaping rituals which fill the same mechanical space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T15:42:44-07:00","id":1216345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1150529#post1150529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Currently, there's no way for a Dragon-Blooded sorcerer to access multiple shaping rituals. That's not necessarily an ironclad prohibition, and it may be something that gets expanded on in, say, a book on sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>If anyone can just get sorcerous initiations in play then this statement is patently false. So...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T16:02:57-07:00","id":1216356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1216345#post1216345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If anyone can just get sorcerous initiations in play then this statement is patently false. So...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an ST adjudicated contradiction in rules then. Devs say you can't get more than one right now, corebook mentions 2 ways of getting them. Either way it's still remarkable for the fact that an essence 3 DB can more easily craft certain terrestrial spells than an essence 1 Solar, barring supernal occult and even then once per day, which is something that's true in basically no other case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T16:30:43-07:00","id":1216371,"title":"","content":"Dragon-Sorcerer Puissance also has the benefit of being delightfully flavorful, which is worth a good deal in my book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T17:32:20-07:00","id":1216396,"title":"","content":"Here is Vance on the subject.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1216365#post1216365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can gain additional shaping rituals at the Storyteller's discretion, but there's no centralized universal mechanic for doing so. The rules for gaining a shaping ritual by creating a sorcerous relic provide a good polestar for how difficult/expensive that should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T23:15:36-07:00","id":1216509,"title":"","content":"Soulfarer and Quincunx from AotC also provide Evocations that are pretty much shaping rituals in weapong form. From that precedent I don't see a reason to forbid players to grab relevant rituals for a small xp fee, with the caveat that they need to be *relevant*, representative of a grand illumination in the way the character uses sorcery. (or in other word: Chicanery - No)<br /> <br /> Example: the classic Heptagramm trained Sorcerer that slowly incorporates more and more elements of foreign (and barbaric!) spellcasting. She eventually strikes a bargain with a spiritual being of great power, eventually learning another shaping ritual. That's a great reason: it's an in-game supported decision, it shows the character's evolution, and cherry on top, provides story hooks about the spiritual relationship vs Immaculate doctrine (or at least, fundamentalists views of doctrine, right Deled?), but also the &quot;barbaric&quot; ritual's effect on her strained social standing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3657-sagara","name":"Sagara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3657_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T00:18:35-07:00","id":1216526,"title":"","content":"Lets talk character gen. DBs get more specialties, way more merit dots, and cool aspect abilities. Unfortunately they give up free excellencies and a supernal ability for it. Well, kind of, their excellencies are sort of free considering they're kind of like 2 charms in one.<br /> <br /> <b>Aspect</b><br /> <br /> This is the most defining aspect of your character. It give you your aspect powers, but it more importantly prevents you from entering any other element's aura when your anima is at bonfire. Also at essence 5 it prevents you from buying a second signature charm other than your element, unless you already did that at essence 3. The aura thing is the biggest deal here. We'll get into this later.<br /> <br /> The other thing is that the effects of your anima are supposed to have a subtle influence on your personality. It's not like you get totally hijacked by an elemental stereotype, but it's just a little push in a certain direction that you might want to include in your backstory. This is actually mechanical, believe it or not, as doing so will make it easier for you to get your Dragon XP, which is helpful. If you don't want to make it a part of your character's everyday actions you might even want to have it where the emotions latent in her blood boil up every so often. Like your normally reserved and cautious fire aspect just flares up and does something impulsive every so often, something they strive to control.<br /> <br /> I think most of the aspect powers are pretty good and straight forward, there's really not much to say there. In context to different abilities and play styles they can really come into their own.<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes</b><br /> <br /> So starting things off with attributes. Pretty much nothing changed here from the Solar set.<br /> <br /> lol, just kidding. As a Solar you need to put a lot more stock in your attributes versus when you're thinking about it for DBs. Solars base their dice caps off of their attributes, so if you want to be an amazing Solar brawler, but also want to be big and burly, taking 3 dex instead of 5 robs you of 4 dice when you go all out. God help you if you decide to have dex 2 and lose out on 6 dice overall.<br /> <br /> If you're doing up a DB though the choice has less of a deep impact. If you really feel like you want a fighter who's got 5 strength but need to sacrifice down to 3 dex for it, then don't sweat it. Your excellency combined with a 5 in your ability will keep you afloat. Especially since as a DB you'll be able to lean on the teamwork of your hearth more.<br /> <br /> <b>Abilities/charms</b><br /> <br /> So abilities are something you really have to look at because there's some major interactions with your aspect. This is debatably a charms thing but you can start thinking about it here. Certain abilities just naturally fit to aspects, the ones that are set to them for your aspect abilities, but there's also some that kind of flow well even without being that aspect technically. For instance there's a little bit of a bias towards air in the archery tree, and fire for the firewand section, but no earth offshoot. That means there's really no charm benefit to being an earth aspected archer, it will just lock you out of every one of your aura abilities when you hit bonfire.<br /> <br /> You are going to have to play a bit of a game here. For your primary abilities, combat/social/other, picking something that's in line with your aspect can help a lot, but there are things you can do to mitigate the problem if you choose to make that earth aspected archer.<br /> <br /> That's because there's 3 sort of hidden tiers in the charm trees. Balanced, Aspected and Aura. Balanced charms being charms that don't affect your aura at all, except to help you get into it if you want. Aspect charms being charms that will knock you out of another aura, but otherwise don't require it. Aura charms are charms that require a specific aura up that your bonfire or Aspect charms might knock you out of.<br /> <br /> Your real bread and butter charms, your excellencies, your basic damage adders and stuff, those tend to be balanced. So if you're an earth aspect trying to keep air aura for the flashy air archery charms, you can go wild with full excellencies and stuff and keep up that aura. Your anima will be a swirling sandstorm for the whole combat. Then if you absolutely must go bonfire, don't worry, because that only locks you out of your Aura charms, not your Aspect charms. It sucks, I know, but you've got 2/3 of your charmset to work off of, be more careful next time.<br /> <br /> All that being said, if you actually go for a matched aspect, fire aspect swordsman, wood aspected archer, ect. it can be really freeing. Just go anima banner as fast as you can and really lean into the aura effects with full power.<br /> <br /> On the other hand an earth aspected archer gets bonus soak, hardness, and knocks people back a range band with her anima flux. So yeah that's pretty good too.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also one last thing on specialties, these are more important to DBs, they add to your dicecap. There's not too much other than that for them to interact with though, so don't worry that you'll need an applicable specialty to use a charm. In fact there's a lot of charms that give you a temporary specialty.<br /> <br /> <b>Merits</b><br /> <br /> Merits for DBs are crazy. Getting up to 18 without even spending bonus points, this can be the real power of the Dragonblooded splat, setting power. It's no sweat at all to grab everything you need to be an established merchant lord with contacts, influence, backing, and heirloom artifact and resources. Then if you decide to spend bonus points on even more merits? Who even NEEDS charms, you're a seriously major player in your chosen field. I'm not even kidding a little bit there, you could basically get yourself into such a position of power that you wouldn't need to burn a drop of essence to contribute to almost any story.<br /> <br /> Of course you take that and, well, remember all those charms we talked about in the ability section where there's a presumption of authority and wealth? Now you've got that cash and clout in spades, and charms to help you leverage it further. You also have every justification you need to take any of these merits, your cultural heritage gives you your complete pick of whatever you want in whatever amount you wish to have.<br /> <br /> I can attest personally to this being a really fun character to play, and it stacks up with multiple people too. For example where a Solar circle might opt to calm the folks of a town facing annihilation by Raksha horde by letting their Zenith give a big public speech to calm, comfort and distract them, and then letting the Dawn and Twilight out to go fight it alone so nobody sees their animas flaring. The DB merit masters handle it a different way.<br /> <br /> First you deploy a navy battle group to the region from your home port on the south coast of the Blessed Isle. Two large troop transports carrying over 200 soldiers each, and an escort of a further two warships with 50 marines each on board. You show up and declare that Venala of the Righteous Steel is here to protect them, your famous name giving hope to the people that they may yet live. They look upon your army with a mixture of fear and relief, they know many people have been brought to heel by the soldiers of the Realm, but today they are the shield against greater horrors.<br /> <br /> Then you greet the Satrap like an old friend, because you are, and smoothly negotiate the temporary command of her forces under your leadership for a unified defense. The local mercenaries who were getting skittish about their odds have their nerves calmed with a good talking to and a talent of silver. Then finally, when the time comes for the defense, you charge into battle, surrounded by your elite bodyguards, bearing the Hearthstone of Courage, your great aunt's manse-stone that burns away fear in men's hearts, set into Summer's Pyre, the ancient storied daiklave that was used by Cathak Cainan himself to turn back far greater fairies than the ones you face today. Only now do you take more than a passing glance at your charm sheet.*<br /> <br /> Now I know Solars can do that too, technically, they just need to pump a lot more bonus points into it, almost all of them maybe. What they can't do though, or at least it's basically impossible to do, is have that kind of backing attached to a place like The Realm. You'd have to be a secret Solar, or have all of your own personal military and connections that aren't through the empire, and that will get noticed. When a DB gets noticed like that, it makes his status go way up in the Dynasty, when a Solar gets noticed like that, the Wyld Hunt perks their ears up as a possible indication of anathema. So you see even if they can do it it's harder and makes for a much different story where you want to keep your head down anyway.<br /> <br /> <br /> And that's where I'll leave it today, talking about charms is going to be a really big task since the essence thing changes the whole game and there's even more to say on elemental affinity and aura, and I want these to be in at least semi-readable chunks.<br /> <br /> <br /> *This is actually kind of a microcosm of how DBs and Solars can play differently as well. It's something I'll do a bit on after chargen and probably the last part of this thread. Solars can tend to power through things with their awesome might and heroic nature, whereas DBs tend to be encouraged, often to the point of necessity, to engage with the world on a deeper level to get traction going.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T23:51:02-07:00","id":1216915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1216526#post1216526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*snip all your posts*</div> </div> </div> </div>You're awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T22:01:03-07:00","id":1217268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1216237#post1216237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Notepad is ready, sifu</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1216250#post1216250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seconded.<br /> <br /> I wasn't expecting the posts on Sorcery and Evocations to be as enlightening, if not moreso, than the initial charm posts.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1216915#post1216915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! Thank you all very much. In fact grab your notepad because this is a long and complicated one.<br /> <br /> <br /> On to charms, and how you might pick them.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1205373-madletter-s-dragon-blooded-charm-cascades\">MadLetter's Awesome Dragon Blooded Charm Trees</a> will be very helpful in this section<br /> <br /> <b>Essence</b><br /> <br /> The biggest two things that are going to change if you've been making Solars is that you start at essence 2, and you don't have a supernal. When you're making a Solar, your character has the incredible power to ignore essence requirements for one ability. This is great, for Solars anyway, because it lets you expand your power to ridiculous heights and really grab hold of that Solar Supremacy. An Essence 1 athletics supernal for example could just snag every FoS charm and punch a fortress wall down in a single blow.<br /> <br /> Dragonblooded don't have that, but the thing is a Solar is also restricted to essence 1 charms everywhere else. We already talked about how that makes a huge difference with evocations, but how about martial arts too, eh? Yeah! No non-MA-supernal Solar is going to get more than essence 1 charms in their MA, and for a lot of styles, all the Immaculate ones included, that means no form charm until they hit essence 2. That's not the only thing though, I mean just for Wood Dragon (the first style I checked) out of the first 6 charms 2 are essence 1 and the rest are essence 4.<br /> <br /> Lets look at how that works out for Solars. You can't even start purchasing essence 2 charms until you're essence 2, which means that you need to have already spent 50xp, which is like 7 charm purchaces and 56xp if all you're doing is buying favoured charms, or 6 and 50xp if you buy one out of favour charm. So if you're being xp efficient and spending only favoured charms, and getting 5xp per session, you're going through 13 sessions before you get your very first essence 2 charm. And to get all 4 from wood dragon? You're 18 sessions, or 90xp into the game before you reach where the Wood Aspect was at from session 1.<br /> <br /> So it works better for martial arts, but that also applies to the basic charms as well, and in this case the effect is twofold. Because you don't have a Supernal, there isn't anything sucking away your charm purchases. When you have the option to take an essence 1 resistance charm, or an essence 5 lore charm that lets you destroy a city, it can be pretty tempting just to ignore that resistance charm.<br /> <br /> It frees you up to just go wide, you have complete access in equal part to every tree, but it also frees you up to go somewhat deep into specific areas of a tree. So lets say you're really into melee, but you don't care about the defense/counter attack portion of the tree. At essence 1 you'd be restricted to just two charms...bleh, not fun. At essence 2 you can grab 6, which is more than half of them.<br /> <br /> There's also something else too, since your next essence up is at 150xp, you're not going to have to worry about much past that for quite a while. In fact 32 sessions before essence up, and by then you're going to have an extra 19 charms past your original 15+. So since you're looking to snag 35 non-MA non-spell charms before hitting essence 3 you can seriously broaden your character. Think about picking up a martial art, or sorcery, or even just grab charms from melee, archery, presence, resistance, ride, occult and bureaucracy at the same time. With all the dragon xp that you'll get, upping those stats if they're low shouldn't even be hard.<br /> <br /> You also don't get free excellencies, so picking up 1-2 charms in an ability can get you those dice adders that will be so appreciated. You might even want to go really broad right from the start, pick 5 abilities and get 3 charms in each of them, give or take one or two. That way you'll have lots of room to grow in what you want to specialize in, and get a bunch of dice adders and useful charms. Also lots of ways to enter aura, speaking of...<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Aspect</b><br /> <br /> Okay so we've seen how your essence lets you be both less specialized but more generally competent* than essence 1 with a supernal. Now lets talk more about aspect and how that affects your character for charm purchases, because you're going to want to look a bit ahead here. Don't worry though if you didn't think things through you're usually only one or two charm purchaces away from fixing it.<br /> <br /> I already talked about there are three somewhat kinda hidden tiers of charms, Balanced, Aspect and Aura. Balanced not affecting aura negatively, Aspect knocking you out of other auras, and aura requiring you to be in aura.<br /> <br /> There's also a kind of a bonus side-tier which is charms that have extra affects from shedding or being in aura. For instance Presence's Eternally Argumentative Flame is a balanced fire charm that reduces the penalties for flurrying a social attack, but in fire aura negates them entirely. If you want to use this charm to full effect, you might think twice about taking Grinding Millstone Argument. You also might want to take Sweeten the Tap from socialize, which is a fire/wood charm that you use at the start of the scene, which will put you into fire aura already before you start talking.<br /> <br /> There's lots of little interactions like this all over the charmset, but what it boils down to is this. When you're in a scene, lets say a combat one but they can be social or anything really, do you want to be in a particular aura? For example in Earth aura to use Rolling Boulder Blow. If you're an earth aspected brawler you might want to take only that, Stone Fist Strike, Crushing Avalanche Grasp, and the four balanced Brawl charms. That's a nice 7 charms there for your combat ability.<br /> <br /> However if you're a fire aspect, still do it, but be careful. When your anima flares up you lose out on Rolling Boulder Blow and some bonus effects from Stone Fist Strike. For times like these I might suggest that you even pick up some water aspected charms, just no aura ones. That way when your anima flares up you have a secondary combat suite to fall back on where you don't take advantage of aura, but now you can feel free to use all those water charm combos so it's not really a bad thing it just changes how you fight. This would be much more helpful if you were a water aspect and could then just switch to using water aura charms, but that's why aspect still matters.<br /> <br /> There's something else here too, and I mentioned it above, and that's getting yourself into aura when you need it. Since you only come into aura at the end of your turn, if you can somehow use a properly aspected charm before the combat starts, that can help.Like if you use an awareness charm to sense an ambush, or a fire charm in the social scene that turns into the combat. That earth aspected brawler might want to take some of these to help out.<br /> <br /> So my advice here is that if you're kind of new to this exalted thing, or even just DBs, maybe stick with the element that your primary abilities seem to want to be in, or just take up to the balanced charms in the tree. Or at least try to find your aspect's charms in the tree you're in so you don't accidentally disable your powers.<br /> <br /> And above all let none of this stop you from making a cool character. If you want to play a fire aspect brawler, or an earth aspect archer, or an water aspect occultist, in spite of there being no charms, apart from signatures, in those trees that match your aspect, go for it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think that's all there is really to know about picking charms, except what I mentioned previously in the abilities as to what to expect from each tree. Next time I post might be the last for this series as I finish up chargen and talk a bit about how the DB play experience is different from the Solar one, from both a ST and player perspective.<br /> <br /> <br /> *Note here that I mean specialized/competent versus a DB setup that's more like the Solar one, Solar charms are powerful enough to make this statement debatable when comparing direct DB to Solar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T23:58:57-07:00","id":1217284,"title":"","content":"I recall some developer advice to the effect of treating the actual initiation of combat as a new scene for the purposes of charms and aura to get around pre-fight simple charm chicanery, unless it really strongly makes sense to treat it like the same scene.<br /> <br /> In this case, it\u2019s that they consider it desirable that Dragon-Blooded generally can\u2019t and won\u2019t start the first round of combat already in aura.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s easy to read that in a negative way, but I prefer a positive framing. It means you don\u2019t have to worry about having the right charm that you can actually use pre-combat to begin combat in aura, because it will only matter when the fighting starts!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Violet Green, Freelancer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","name":"VioletDreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T04:31:37-07:00","id":1217331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VioletDreamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1217284#post1217284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recall some developer advice to the effect of treating the actual initiation of combat as a new scene for the purposes of charms and aura to get around pre-fight simple charm chicanery, unless it really strongly makes sense to treat it like the same scene.<br /> <br /> In this case, it\u2019s that they consider it desirable that Dragon-Blooded generally can\u2019t and won\u2019t start the first round of combat already in aura.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s easy to read that in a negative way, but I prefer a positive framing. It means you don\u2019t have to worry about having the right charm that you can actually use pre-combat to begin combat in aura, because it will only matter when the fighting starts!</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense, I think probably using Sweeten the Tap or using an awareness charm to sense an ambush miiiiight still work for that? But it doesn\u2019t quite matter so much as I predict DB combat will last for more rounds than Solar combat in my experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T05:44:47-07:00","id":1217350,"title":"","content":"As I understand it, you need to use a charm on your turn to enter aura, not someone else's turn. Or similar equivalent outside of combat.<br /> <br /> So using a simple charm before combat should be fine, but I think sensing an ambush probably counts as the other guy's turn.<br /> <br /> Not sure though. It's a bit fiddly, tbh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-10-2018, 08:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T06:53:40-07:00","id":1217378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1217268#post1217268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragonblooded don't have that, but the thing is a Solar is also restricted to essence 1 charms everywhere else. We already talked about how that makes a huge difference with evocations, but how about martial arts too, eh? Yeah! No non-MA-supernal Solar is going to get more than essence 1 charms in their MA, and for a lot of styles, all the Immaculate ones included, that means no form charm until they hit essence 2. That's not the only thing though, I mean just for Wood Dragon (the first style I checked) out of the first 6 charms 2 are essence 1 and the rest are essence 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Styles whose Forms are E1, by the way, are Snake, Tiger, White Reaper, Ebon Shadow, Nightingale, Black Claw, Steel Devil, Golden Janissary, Mantis, and White Veil. Not to counter your point, but there are at least a decent number of Styles who let you get the Form at E1.<br /> Sadly, my favorite (Dreaming Pearl Courtesan) is not one of those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T07:19:50-07:00","id":1217385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beans</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1217378#post1217378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Styles whose Forms are E1, by the way, are Snake, Tiger, White Reaper, Ebon Shadow, Nightingale, Black Claw, Steel Devil, Golden Janissary, Mantis, and White Veil. Not to counter your point, but there are at least a decent number of Styles who let you get the Form at E1.<br /> Sadly, my favorite (Dreaming Pearl Courtesan) is not one of those.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell me about it, I had one of my players who was an eclipse take Crane style off the hop, it\u2019s got an essence 2 form as well, and man that style REALLY wants it\u2019s form. Before you get it you don\u2019t feel very much like a crane stylist at all.<br /> <br /> As to the ambush I definitely wouldn\u2019t give it to you if you enhanced your join battle with only one aspect, but I think maybe the ambush stealth roll is supposed to happen before join battle? Maybe? I dunno. Come to think of it using only air aspected charms to enhance your stealth roll might also work for that.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not something you should feel is required anyway, from what I\u2019ve seen most of the aura charms are decisive anyway so you should have time to get that up before you need it, unless you ARE trying to assassinate somebody.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T07:35:38-07:00","id":1217393,"title":"","content":"Even saddled with the Terrestrial keyword, in some ways MA can be more fun with DBs both because of the Essence thing and because Dynasts, at least, can comfortably dump seven or eight Merit dots into Martial Artist and an Artifact weapon or armor (even that sweet, sweet, pricey Silk Armor); a Solar who's not super-devoted to doing MA might worry about that cost, but even a Dynast who's not going whole-hog for Martial Arts can happily pull out Five-Dragon Fliff Maneuver and have enough to get lots of other things.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, on the other hand, having to buy their Excellencies does matter and the DB must consider their investment cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8026,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","user":"Beans","date":". 05-10-2018, 10:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T13:18:48-07:00","id":1217757,"title":"","content":"Hey guys sorry for the late update, school is picking up again. Tomorrow I\u2019m going to run through a few test combats with chargen DBs against various things, so I can add that to the next analysis. Any suggestions on reports you\u2019d like to see? I\u2019ve got four players, one of each aspect except earth, using each of their in aspect combat abilities. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m going to try and run a typical PC mix, so everyone has a bit of combat but not everyone is all 5s in everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T14:56:34-07:00","id":1217785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1217757#post1217757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any suggestions on reports you\u2019d like to see?</div> </div> </div> </div>How well they stack up against the creatures in the beastiary which aren't just spirits and undead.<br /> <br /> I saw someone in some thread (this one?) comment that a lot of the monsters that Solars plain blow by the instant they have a Dawn with a combat suite in their circle are actually pretty decent challenges for Dynasts. I'm starting a game focused on nation building in a conquered region after a Wyld Hunt threw down the local Anathema pretender to the title Prince of the Earth so I figure I might be able to get some mileage out of the wild and untamed regions of the area. Can a regional hellboar problem risking the ruination of the harvest be an actual driving challenge, etc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T16:15:59-07:00","id":1217811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1217785#post1217785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How well they stack up against the creatures in the beastiary which aren't just spirits and undead.<br /> <br /> I saw someone in some thread (this one?) comment that a lot of the monsters that Solars plain blow by the instant they have a Dawn with a combat suite in their circle are actually pretty decent challenges for Dynasts. I'm starting a game focused on nation building in a conquered region after a Wyld Hunt threw down the local Anathema pretender to the title Prince of the Earth so I figure I might be able to get some mileage out of the wild and untamed regions of the area. Can a regional hellboar problem risking the ruination of the harvest be an actual driving challenge, etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was actually thinking the same thinng. I\u2019m not super optimistic about the hellboar but claw striders maybe. I might even see how they face against the tyrant lizard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T06:29:25-07:00","id":1217952,"title":"","content":"If one hellboar isn't enough, perhaps a whole herd! Giving them mass combat stats isn't insane, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T09:11:33-07:00","id":1217983,"title":"","content":"A group of mortals with Bows can take down a charging Hellboar if it starts at long rane. Though I suppose my players might have gotten lucky or we might have not done a few things correctly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T11:11:57-07:00","id":1218020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1217952#post1217952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If one hellboar isn't enough, perhaps a whole herd! Giving them mass combat stats isn't insane, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the problem there is a fluff one. Hell boars I don\u2019t think are supposed to travel in herds, but maybe like as a fluke stampede?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T17:06:15-07:00","id":1218100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1218020#post1218020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the problem there is a fluff one. Hell boars I don\u2019t think are supposed to travel in herds, but maybe like as a fluke stampede?</div> </div> </div> </div>A sorcerer did it. Bonus points if they did by way of a curse that turned the inhabitants of the Satrapy into hellboars, and now the DBs have to subdue the boars while killing as little of them as possible, then deal with the sorcerer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T18:48:23-07:00","id":1218124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1218020#post1218020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the problem there is a fluff one. Hell boars I don\u2019t think are supposed to travel in herds, but maybe like as a fluke stampede?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vile tricks by the Lunar Anathema seeking to dear down what will one day be a prosperous, devout, and well armed satrapy!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T21:40:24-07:00","id":1218402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1218100#post1218100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A sorcerer did it. Bonus points if they did by way of a curse that turned the inhabitants of the Satrapy into hellboars, and now the DBs have to subdue the boars while killing as little of them as possible, then deal with the sorcerer.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1218124#post1218124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vile tricks by the Lunar Anathema seeking to dear down what will one day be a prosperous, devout, and well armed satrapy!</div> </div> </div> </div>Both good ideas! Unfortunately we only had time for one combat. I'll talk about it after giving a quick word to the rest of the chargen stuff.<br /> <br /> <b>Intimacies</b><br /> <br /> This is pretty short. There's only two things here that you might want to consider. The first is that DBs tend to be a part of something bigger than themselves, Prasad, Lookshy the Dynasty, ect. That means you'll very likely have some kind of intimacy or intimacies relating to that. DBs also have that kind of passionate bent to them so I'd consider including some things you are passionate about. Maybe some passionate feeling you have about a big organization you're a part of or related to.<br /> <br /> On the other hand it's your character, so really this can be anything.<br /> <br /> <b>Bonus Points</b><br /> <br /> Bonus points are just sort of a micro version of what's important. Abilities more than attributes usually, since it affects your dicecaps. Specialties are also something you might want to invest in. You get more than Solars but probably not as many as you want at base. You also don't get free excellencies so maybe consider purchasing more basic charms. I think my favourite thing is just to double down on merits though, just start with like 25. This is another thing that you might consider since you're a DB and likely part of a larger whole, it almost requires an explanation as to why you don't have backing/influence/contacts than why you do.<br /> <br /> So yeah, that's it for chargen. Overall a very different experience, and I would know because I just made 3 in a row yesterday so that my group could do a playtest combat before a double session of DnD.<br /> <br /> <b>Finishing Touches</b><br /> <br /> Not much here to say except the essence pool. Considering your DB will probably have access to artifacts, and those artifacts will almost definitely be worth having, your pools are going to be a little tight. Like 13 personal, 19 peripheral, around there. With your 6 mote maximum excellency this won't run out quite as fast as a Solar with the same pool, but you're definitely going to have to watch it fairly closely. Luckily you also won't have quite the same power to combo a million expensive charms together, so that should help you last too. Either way though, because you lack the ability to just end a combat with one player in one fell swing, and everyone is going to want to contribute, you're probably going to want to pick and choose where you go all out and take advantage of that mote regen.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Test Combat</span><br /> <br /> Character Summaries</b><br /> <br /> I made up 3 DBs, water, wood, and fire aspect using each of their combat abilities. My one player took the initiative and actually made up his own thrown air aspect, so kudos to him. I made characters that had about 5-7 combat charms, pretty much 5 in all their combat abilities, but not so combat optimized as to all have 5 dex or anything. Basically the kind of characters you might see in an actual game, but perhaps slanted a bit towards fighting. I also gave everyone artifact weapons and light/medium armor, except brawl guy, he didn't get a weapon.<br /> <br /> The way I figured it, having around 6 combat charms was either representative of a decently balanced fighter at chargen, or an experienced DB who's focused more on something else.<br /> <br /> <b>The Combat</b><br /> <br /> We hadn't played Exalted in a while, and only 1 of my three players had even glanced at the DB book before yesterday. I did my best to make it fast to catch up on, like by printing out sheets with everyone's charms and effects on them, but starting cold like that is always going to be hard.<br /> <br /> So we started things off super simply, 4 DBs versus 5 claw striders, they got jumped, but not ambushed, at short range and in clear weather and all that. Basically a white room. The DBs started off by charging the fire and water aspect into combat while the air and wood stood back to rain down supporting fire. In the close range the two DBs burned motes hard on attack and defense, trading blows with the claw strider pack but generally ending up on top.<br /> <br /> The brawl charms effectively made up for the water aspect's lack of base damage, and the fire aspect actually built up to a totally free excellency by the end of the fight, although he took a few solid hits right at the start. None of my players ever got crashed, but they got lucky too, launching a decisive was a real serious risk, especially with the initiative reversal possibilities. Because of that there was actually a pretty decent struggle, not every decisive was a kill shot, and they actually worked to try and disable enemies if they could, rather than just annihilate them outright. The anima flux helped out too, after crashing it sent a few striders down some wound penalties.<br /> <br /> At the end of the fight the two melee fighters were totally tapped, the ranged guys had a good bit of their motes left, and all the striders were taken care of. I definitely feel like this is more my speed for Exalted. I also didn't feel like my players were holding back at all or anything like that, they were fighting smart, and actually having discussions if it would be worth it to attempt a decisive attack and reset or wait for another round.<br /> <br /> All told the combat lasted about 50 minutes real time and about 4 rounds game time.<br /> <br /> <b>More Powerful PCs/Bigger Threats</b><br /> <br /> From the way things looked, this kind of thing wasn't super likely to change until essence up, at least. Oh for sure the players will get more powerful, they'll get more options on what to do, and a few new things to combo together, but they won't explode past a lot of threats the way Solars do. Certainly not to the point where 4/5 of the party is not required for 90% of combats.<br /> <br /> It seems to me that because of the way DBs operate when they take on really big threats like Octavian they're going to have to do some manipulation of the battlefield a bit. Maybe they're going to bring a battlegroup, or summon a bound elemental for aid, or possibly just really step their game up. I get the feeling that a circle of immaculate monks with all their style charms up to essence 2 or 3 would be able to do it with effort, but the IMAs are good and good at killing spirits in particular.<br /> <br /> <b>Verdict</b><br /> <br /> If those claw striders had a DB riding the alpha, or were just one scene in a larger event, I can definitely see this being a more tense scenario. As it was it makes for a good prelude combat, it's got some back and forth to keep it interesting without any single player just biffing their way through it in one action, but not so hard to make this feel like a climax. It also really required everyone, if there were only 3 players, or if they had gotten ambushed and in tighter range things might have gone differently. This is not my experience with Solars at all.<br /> <br /> So yeah, anyway, the test combat went almost exactly as I predicted, which is pretty well. I'm going to need to run a few more, and probably an actual campaign before I lay down the final verdict, but most of my group agreed. This charmset has a more reasonable strength, with less bloat, and flows faster. Something I'll focus on in the next test combat is DB archery, which has a bent for which is aiming that one of my players is concerned about. My initial thought is that it will be worth alternating aiming and shooting for high defense enemies, or enemies you really want to stay away from, but otherwise maybe not worth. The artifacts also help for sure.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Conclusion</b><br /> <br /> Well that was a long journey. I might add more as I do more test combats or maybe run my first campaign, but I'm not sure I have much more to say now. Well, except good job developers. Third edition was a solid improvement on second edition, and this definitely looks like it will be my favourite way to play it. My players agree as well, we stopped playing Exalted for a while and swapped to a 1-20 DnD megacampaign, but this will definitely bring us back after it's done. DBs have always been up there for my favourite type of exalted and this does not disappoint at all.<br /> <br /> It's definitely a different experience than playing Solars, and there's some stories that Solars just tell better, but I think we'll find that playing DBs can be even more rewarding and engaging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T13:46:11-07:00","id":1218677,"title":"","content":"A bit of a digress perhaps:<br /> <br /> When I started my Solar game after the corebook was released, the first thing I did was to house rule away the need for the Martial Arts Merit. I felt it was too expensive, it wasn't fun to have, and the Martial Arts Charms weren't powerful enough to merit that kind of expense. Every Solar martial artist since has been allowed to ignore the Merit.<br /> <br /> The first thing I did now when starting up a DB game was to reinstate the Merit as intended with the canon rules. Recognizing the need for that Merit became apparent when comparing Martial Art Charms with DB Charms. I'll probably still ignore it for Solars, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T16:18:37-07:00","id":1218718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1218677#post1218677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A bit of a digress perhaps:<br /> <br /> When I started my Solar game after the corebook was released, the first thing I did was to house rule away the need for the Martial Arts Merit. I felt it was too expensive, it wasn't fun to have, and the Martial Arts Charms weren't powerful enough to merit that kind of expense. Every Solar martial artist since has been allowed to ignore the Merit.<br /> <br /> The first thing I did now when starting up a DB game was to reinstate the Merit as intended with the canon rules. Recognizing the need for that Merit became apparent when comparing Martial Art Charms with DB Charms. I'll probably still ignore it for Solars, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that makes sense. Particularly with the immaculate styles. It\u2019s not like they\u2019re Solar tier or anything, but they\u2019re straining against the top end of DB tier and punching even above that in some instances. Particularly how they cover for eachother in capability. I know it\u2019d be an insane drain on chargen resources but making a character with 5s in every immaculate style and as many essence 1-2 charms as you could get out of it would be bonkers. You\u2019d have very little ability to do anything but fight, but man could you fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T20:39:15-07:00","id":1218791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1210732-a-closer-look-solars-vs-dragonblooded?p=1218718#post1218718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah that makes sense. Particularly with the immaculate styles. It\u2019s not like they\u2019re Solar tier or anything, but they\u2019re straining against the top end of DB tier and punching even above that in some instances. Particularly how they cover for eachother in capability. I know it\u2019d be an insane drain on chargen resources but making a character with 5s in every immaculate style and as many essence 1-2 charms as you could get out of it would be bonkers. You\u2019d have very little ability to do anything but fight, but man could you fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's why Ragara Myrrun is not to be trifled with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....